{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe","id":1514259,"title":"The followers of Odin as a Werewolf setting element/foe","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-08T18:50:41-07:00","id":1514259,"title":"The followers of Odin as a Werewolf setting element/foe","content":"I\u2019ve often felt that vampires are often underutilized as Werewolf villains. Not that STs don\u2019t use them as antagonists, but very often they are all rather typical and don\u2019t utilize as much variety that the lore indicates. There are some very strong lore ties that get overlooked. It\u2019s unfulfilled potential. I made two earlier threads about them - one about the Dunsirn and another about the Setites. I had some success with those posts in developing those groups so I wanted to see what happened a third time.<br /> <br /> Another neglected opportunity, IMO, is the vampire Odin, also known as the All High. The Get of Fenris have long standing ties to this vampire. Yet I see little about it - probably because while both Vampire and Werewolf mention him, the character never awoke from torpor as part of the metaplot. So this thread is to explore using him as a Werewolf element. For ease, I am going to use the name \u201cHost of the All High\u201d or simply the Host to describe the faction based around this figure.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: the Apocalypse lore leads itself to strange interpretations of the actual Norse myths. Fenris is one of the good guys, but his \u201cbrother\u201d Jormungandr is the Wyrm. Odin is a vampire and thus also an enemy. But one of the Fenrir camps is named after Wotan. It is just a mess if you are trying to connect game lore with myhology. So my main inspiration for this faction is not to reconcile it to actual Norse mythology, but to figure out the best ways I can use it as inspiration for this group. The end result should be something that cause us to think \u201cYeah, I can see the interaction between the history of this group and Norse mythology\u201d, not that one caused the other. It doesn\u2019t matter whether the vampires (and other supernatural beings) came first and the religion after, vice versa, or a mix of the two. Every ST will have their own individual preference.<br /> <br /> I also know that some of this contradicts official canon, especially how the Revised Get of Fenris book attempts to deal with Norse myth. I\u2019m not a fan of what was actually published in the tribebook, though I do give the writers credit for their effort.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T18:52:06-07:00","id":1514260,"title":"","content":"The Host of the All High are the various followers of the Gangrel vampire methusaleh, the All High (known to the Get of Fenris as Odin among other names). Members also refer to their clandestine alliance as the Raven Banner, and the raven remains a symbol of their troth to each other. The Garou most often call it Odin\u2019s Host.<br /> <br /> The Host is most active in northern Europe, stretching from Ireland in the west and reaching east towards Russia - the historical area where either the Norse visited during the Viking Age or were the lands travelled by the All High in pre-history. He has relatively few followers south of the Alps. Some members of the Raven Banner have spread to North America and even elsewhere as a result of migration, but their few numbers in those locations make them extremely vulnerable and unable to connect to their allies.<br /> <br /> As an ancient Gangrel methusaleh of potent generation, the All High is a major figure of the Jyhad. He has plans on how to thwart or defeat Ragnarok, better known among vampires as Gehenna and to the Garou as the Apocalypse. Like the Garou, the All High wants to avert or defeat the Apocalypse. Unfortunately, he has come to the conclusion that the Garou and their cousins are too stupid to understand the true nature of the Apocalypse and the intrigues of the Jyhad. Instead of working with him, these ignorant animals seek to destroy him. Over many centuries he has learned it is useless to discuss this with them or attempt to gain them as allies. He has long ceased trying, content with the other allies he has been able to bring together to prevent the end of the world. To the Garou, the All High is just another powerful Wyrm creature attempting to make his faction the victors of the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> The Garou have fought the All High and his minions for thousands of years, going back to the Nordic Bronze Age and earlier. The Get of Fenris count themselves as his greatest foes, though other tribes have fought his minions as well. The Garou were shocked to hear that Swedish King Inge the Elder an army and Christian priests that destroyed him at Uppsala almost a thousand years ago, but most Garou refuse to believe it. First, it would offend their pride that humans accomplished what they could not. Second, a common prophecy among Garou is that the All High will survive until the Apocalypse, only to be destroyed by the Fenris Incarna himself. Instead, the Garou keep t heir ears open for any evidence that their enemy has returned once again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T18:52:42-07:00","id":1514261,"title":"","content":"A major idea here is the Host as a supernatural \u201carmy\u201d similar to Baba Yaga\u2019s in Rage Across Russia, but for the purpose of surviving Ragnarok (aka Gehenna, Apocalypse, Doomsday, Endless Winter, etc.) as opposed to Baba Yaga wishing to control her homeland. The Host is not intended to be as gonzo or high powered as Baba Yaga\u2019s armies in Rage Across Russia, but are meant to provide a similar challenge to Garou. I also do not see the All High as ancient or powerful as Baba Yaga. While character stats was given for Baba Yaga, I do not think the All High was ever statted - likely because while Baba Yaga was awake, the All High was not. The Host is meant as a long standing setting element that can be used in many historical eras of play.<br /> <br /> The main stylistic difference is that the All High is not as obviously villainous as Baba Yaga was meant to be. The All High sees Gehenna as one of the opening chapters of the Apocalypse. Defeating the Antedeluvians is not enough to avert Ragnarok. Jormugandr (the Wyrm) is his enemy as well, and so even his villainous alliances reject things like the Black Spiral Dancers or the Zmei, Wyrm creatures directly aligned with the Wyrm. More ignorant Wyrm creatures willing to align themselves with him are acceptable allies. Garou PCs might be surprised to learn that on occasion the Host of the All High and they are fighting the same foes. <br /> <br /> Although the All High does not see himself or his allies as being of the Wyrm, from a Garou perspective practically all of the All High\u2019s forces are Wyrm minions. The two sides do not have the same interpretations of the Apocalypse either, so to the Garou the All High remains a sinister figure of the Apocalypse, one which they must defeat along with their other foes. The All High is not meant to be a secret \u201cgood guy\u201d. Just a more ambiguous figure with his own agenda that does not fulfill the Garou stereotype.<br /> <br /> I am going to detail certain elements within the Host separately, but they cover several different groups. Although primarily a vampire faction, the All High has many allies. I will deal with each in step. But for now I\u2019ll step back in case there are comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T23:43:32-07:00","id":1514280,"title":"","content":"Its probably worth noting that fenris is closer to the beast of war than anything in norse myth. You could easily re intepret the children of loki as the triatic wyrm.<br /> <br /> I had a idea of the get perceiving Gaia, an aspect of her as the all father or an ally of the garou nation and their totem being geri and freki.<br /> <br /> Ive historically ran pagan gods as deliberately ambiguous so the idea of wodan/odin/allfather as some evil wizard never really sat right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T11:55:53-07:00","id":1514325,"title":"","content":"On the other hand, if the Greek heroes are frequently tainted monsters that the Furies took down, why not approach the other &quot;linked cultures&quot; in a similar fashion? Werewolf is the perfect place for grimdark antimythology, breaking down what you thought you knew about figures the humans at the time considered positive and flipping the roles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T12:44:39-07:00","id":1514333,"title":"","content":"I definitely agree that the Norse situation is almost as much as a Gordian knot for White Wolf as the Egypt situation, particularly with the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> My usual take at reframing it is something along these lines:<br /> \u2022Odin, Tyr, Thor, and the other Norse Aesir as law-giving gods of human civilization ought to be more aligned with humanity and the Weaver, although perhaps having aspects Garou can call upon <br /> \u2022The Vanir, Fey-like Earthen Spirits, &amp; Giants who represent the forces of primordial nature and the law-destroying forces of chaos are the ones most traditionally associated with the Garou <br /> \u2022Loki as a shape-shifting giant serves as a strong candidate amongst northern Garou for a male-counterpart to Gaia who sired the Changing Breeds<br /> \u2022In this case then Fenrir is born as the patriarch sire of the tribe of Fenris, the Death-Wolf and War-Wolf with Jormungundr &amp; Hel being as aligned as the giants themselves <br /> \u2022In this framing the moment of rupture in the Fenrir\u2019s eyes would probably be when the Aesir bound Fenris Wolf &amp; Loki; representing a local manifestation of the larger narrative impulse in the WoD for the forces of the Weaver to overstep their authority over nature <br /> \u2022In this case the Wyrm is probably the Nidhogg creature <br /> <br /> However there\u2019s another element of this which I think is interesting to consider, namely that I think there are reasons for Odin (unlike any other Aesir figures) to potentially have a closer relationship to the Fenrir <br /> <br /> I\u2019ve mentioned in a few recent posts how I think that the Fenrir work well with flourishes taken from the concept of the Koryos to benefit them. To be brief: the \u2018Koryos\u2019 is an anthropological concept for a wide-spread social tool amongst various Proto-Indo-European peoples to take excess young men of the polity and to induct them into a persistent nomadic warrior-band as simultaneously a means of relieving excess male pressure from the core polity but also as a military instrument. I mention this because of some interesting speculation I\u2019ve heard which posits one origin for the prominence of Odin in northern cultures as being a recollection of this Koryos society - wherein it\u2019s presumed that a few elder men would remain in the Koryos life-long to induct young men and that these men, the death/war-priests who inducted young men into the wolf-pelt clad warrior cults, may have been remembered in the figure of Odin (particularly in his roles as death-god, war-god, leader of the wild-hunt, and patron of berserkers).<br /> <br /> The reason I mention this is that I think it could be interesting to have Odin/The All High as having once been quite close to the Fenrir.<br /> <br /> A sketch I have:<br /> \u2022In the pre-history of Northern Europe we have these PIE cultures and the Fenrir among them and from one group of Fenrir kinfolk came a Koryos with a life long member, the All High as a mortal, not the first but a great example of such a role<br /> \u2022The All High would draw the attention of the Gangrel and become an embrace, uniting his mortal traditions with a sudden infusion of the cthonic mysteries of the vampires <br /> \u2022The Fenrir likely maintain a spirit who the All High was once a particularly gifted adherent of or representative of and one who has become inseparable associated with the All High since due to the vampire\u2019s achievements <br /> \u2022The Fenrir have a love-hate relationship with the All High and their followers; on one level vampires are practitioners of dark and forbidden arts &amp; the All High in particular is a powerful witch and sorcerer with no end to his deviousness and low cunning - on the other hand the All High and his followers inarguably do have a deep interest in averting the Apocalypse (somehow) and do practice a (perverse) form of many traditional Fenrir rites and the All High, despite everything else, is an undeniably gifted warrior-king and vessel of power<br /> \u2022I also agree with a point Black Fox made - the Fenrir would never admit to mortals, especially those ignorant to the old ways, having defeated the All High; the assumption being that he\u2019s in secret retreat somewhere below the earth and carrying out his schemes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:16:26-07:00","id":1514384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514280#post1514280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive historically ran pagan gods as deliberately ambiguous so the idea of wodan/odin/allfather as some evil wizard never really sat right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always liked the euhemeristic approach of Vampire and the early WoD that provided the sources behind the myths and legends, but admit this is very much personal taste. Everyone will have a wide variety of responses from &quot;cool&quot; to &quot;blah&quot; to bad taste or thinks it ruins something else they preferred to happen. That's why my approach isn't so much to &quot;explain&quot; the mythology, but to use it as inspiration. STs can then determine whatever truth they want to use for the actual mythology.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:24:44-07:00","id":1514386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514333#post1514333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be brief: the \u2018Koryos\u2019 is an anthropological concept for a wide-spread social tool amongst various Proto-Indo-European peoples to take excess young men of the polity and to induct them into a persistent nomadic warrior-band as simultaneously a means of relieving excess male pressure from the core polity but also as a military instrument. <br /> <br /> \u2022The All High would draw the attention of the Gangrel and become an embrace, uniting his mortal traditions with a sudden infusion of the cthonic mysteries of the vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's entirely possible the All High was originally a mortal of the proto Indo-European peoples. It also fits in well with Snorri Sturluson's writings in the Prose Edda that described Odin as a human king (not a god) who came to Scandinavia from the south. <br /> <br /> That would put Odin's embrace sometime between 4000 BC and 3000 BC. More powerful than methusalehs like Menele or Helena, but less so than vampires like Baba Yaga or Louhi. I think that's a good spot for him. Enough that the ST can justify him doing whatever the ST wants, but not so much in plot device territory that he cannot be destroyed at the end of a chronicle if the ST wants that as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:30:37-07:00","id":1514387,"title":"","content":"The most obvious group of followers is, of course, other vampires, particularly members of the Gangrel clan and the All High\u2019s own lineage. Much of this is canon pulled from Vampire. The early game must have had plans for this idea because it was mentioned in the first edition World of Darkness and Clanbook: Gangrel. But it seems to have been one of those threads that were lost after Andrew Greenberg left as developer. I don't remember Revised edition doing anything with it.<br /> <br /> We have the Walkure plus an offshoot called the Odinndohter who formed a \u201cradical feminist sect\u201d in West Germany in the 1980s who later infiltrated Russia to investigate Baba Yaga and the Shadow Curtain. <br /> <br /> There are probably various vampire elders native to Scandinavia that might also be members. The Wolves of the Sea sourcebook describe many Norse vampires of Brujah and Gangrel stock in the region, although their numbers are likely fairly low now. But it does tell us that besides the Gangrel, there may be some Brujah elders with some kind of ties or loyalties.<br /> <br /> We also know the Walkure were active in Anarch circles. I think this is not due to any actual sympathies with the Anarch philosophies (the All High and his get would represent the kind of vampire rule that predated the Anarch Revolt), but simply because the Camarilla would be a threat to the All High\u2019s plans. Like many methusalehs, the All High would transcend sect politics. So they are probably a significant influence on Anarchs in northern Europe. I also remember reading that at least one Walkure patrolling the American west coast among the Anarchs, but cannot remember what sourcebook that is from. If anyone remembers, please let me know. <br /> <br /> I also think there are some intriguing possibilities around the Scandinavian Sabbat. The sourcebooks state the Sabbat there are very different from Sabbat elsewhere, and interested in lore. I think it is possible that Walkure could be attempting to cause some of the Sabbat here to defect to their side. Like the Sabbat, the All High is keenly interested in Gehenna and could provide a more attractive \u201csect\u201d for these Cainites since the Sabbat books always described them as being at odds with the sect as a whole. The vaulderie should not present many problems because the Scandinavia Sabbat is very isolated from their other sect mates, and if they defect en masse it should not cause issues with vinculum among the larger sect. The Sabbat in Finland will likely be opposed though because of their connection to Louhi and her work to blot out the sun - the All High would want to prevent that since it is one of the signs of Ragnarok/Gehenna. Just options for the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T19:36:16-07:00","id":1514388,"title":"","content":"But what to do with these vampires in terms of Werewolf?<br /> <br /> Insofar that Odin is a major enemy in Get of Fenris lore, we can probably build on individual Walkure as their own figures. They will all be elders and some could be Methusalehs on their own. These might have their own specific stories about them. They could even be tied to Ancestors or something else to personalize them. Elder vampires can be interesting foes, though in my experience many PC packs will make mincemeat of them. If you are trying to portray the Walkure as worthy opponents, they\u2019ll likely need be foes who are always one step ahead and never physically met.<br /> <br /> I think their semi-Anarch followers are more disposable, and thus less likely to derail the ST\u2019s plot by their destruction. Probably introduce them as nomadic Anarchs not distinguishable from other vampires, but slowly introduce things that reveal their connection. As \u201csurvivalist\u201d style Anarchs, you could even run them as looking to build some kind of rural compound/haven that would be intended to be a future base for Gehenna. Maybe run them low key so it is not obvious this biker gang or survivalists are vampires, maybe even they don\u2019t need to feed on the rural townsfolk, but bring in their own herd. Introduce them like they are legitimate mortal NPCs, and only make the reveal when necessary. Or perhaps have the Garou PCs initially only meet the vampires' mortal retainers or allies so you can sneak them in later with less suspicion.<br /> <br /> And even though these vampires tend to be mentioned only with the Get of Fenris, I think other tribes would also have some sort of dealings with them. Certainly the Fianna would have some experience due to the Anglo-Saxon and Norse invasions of Britain and Ireland. The Shadow Lords and Silver Fangs have also occupied territories that were visited or invaded by the Norse. And since Odin is an old figure that predates the Vikings there is a lot more that can be tied to Garou history. The Germanic invasions of Rome. Stories of a much younger vampire sorcerer on the Eurasian steppe that the Black Furies know. Glass Walkers familiar with the history of a vampire conspiracy in the Varangian Guard at Constantinople. A lot could be done. Personally I would push the idea that Odin and his vampires is a figure that has bedeviled the Garou in general, but that the Get of Fenris just have more experience fighting him and his spawn.<br /> <br /> Not much new to report in terms of Werewolf. But it does serve as a foundation other layers can be built upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T21:14:59-07:00","id":1514393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514280#post1514280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its probably worth noting that fenris is closer to the beast of war than anything in norse myth. You could easily re intepret the children of loki as the triatic wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Fenrir as the Beast of War, J\u00f6rmungandr as the Defiler Wyrm and Hel as the Eater of Souls. Huh. That actually lines up incredibly well. Almost too well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-09T23:59:22-07:00","id":1514407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514393#post1514393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So Fenrir as the Beast of War, J\u00f6rmungandr as the Defiler Wyrm and Hel as the Eater of Souls. Huh. That actually lines up incredibly well. Almost too well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yeah it's something I clocked when I firstI read about the get, you can even it further by making loki the wyrm itself. This then sets up the stage for the norse pantheon as pro gaia.<br /> it also could be used to ad a mystic fate weaver aspect to the get if they're aligned with Odin or a more boisterous pro humanity side if they're linked with Thor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T01:40:57-07:00","id":1514424,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Fenrir is, or is perceived as, a spirit split from the pre-corruption Wyrm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T13:40:11-07:00","id":1514503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514388#post1514388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elder vampires can be interesting foes, though in my experience many PC packs will make mincemeat of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we\u2019re talking ancients then I have it the other way around, higher levels of celerity, advanced fortitude, huge blood pools and millennia of melee skills and you\u2019ve got something that Garou attacks bounce off whilst their delivering attacks that an Ahroun using high rage and spirit of the fray would struggle to keep up with.<br /> <br /> Some ancients would orchestrate from the shadows, but I think feral warrior spirits such as the Gangrel would relish the tooth and claw, especially with high levels of protean it\u2019s the Viking way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514388#post1514388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or perhaps have the Garou PCs initially only meet the vampires' mortal retainers or allies so you can sneak them in later with less suspicion.</div> </div> </div> </div>For the All-Father a being that was mortal in more mythic times I\u2019d have his mortal followers as Jotunn Blooded or derived from Bear or Wolf Blooded kin stock.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s had immeasurable time to preserve or cultivate an elder cryptid human line which feels better than your standard ghouls or even a revenant family.<br /> <br /> As a creature inspiring or masquerading as a mythological being it fits that he\u2019d preserve the descendants of mythical beings for his own ends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-10-2023, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:24:50-07:00","id":1514510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514503#post1514503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If we\u2019re talking ancients then I have it the other way around, higher levels of celerity, advanced fortitude, huge blood pools and millennia of melee skills and you\u2019ve got something that Garou attacks bounce off whilst their delivering attacks that an Ahroun using high rage and spirit of the fray would struggle to keep up with.<br /> <br /> Some ancients would orchestrate from the shadows, but I think feral warrior spirits such as the Gangrel would relish the tooth and claw, especially with high levels of protean it\u2019s the Viking way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even BS Fortitude doesn't go up on a trajectory that suggests that they wouldn't be torn apart by all the agg that an entire pack can inflict. Soaking agg with Stamina +Fortitude is apparently a taxing feat of Fortitude that can't be used very often. This doesn't scream &quot;monster type made to fight that bounces attacks casually&quot;. If your Fortitude is less than 10/Plot Device, you're rotting meat to be.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Garou are expected to go up against Zmei. And thunderwyrms, up to the extra-giant one that serves as a mobile BSD pit. If a vampire elder had to marathon that, they'd get torn apart just like that clown in the Zmei card for Rage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the All-Father a being that was mortal in more mythic times I\u2019d have his mortal followers as Jotunn Blooded or derived from Bear or Wolf Blooded kin stock.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s had immeasurable time to preserve or cultivate an elder cryptid human line which feels better than your standard ghouls or even a revenant family.<br /> <br /> As a creature inspiring or masquerading as a mythological being it fits that he\u2019d preserve the descendants of mythical beings for his own ends. </div> </div> </div>Assuming that vampire blood didn't de-power them and replace their magical-ness with just being regular ghouls, a la the long term effects of ghouling on mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:52:44-07:00","id":1514515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514510#post1514510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even BS Fortitude doesn't go up on a trajectory that suggests that they wouldn't be torn apart by all the agg that an entire pack can inflict. Soaking agg with Stamina +Fortitude is apparently a taxing feat of Fortitude that can't be used very often. This doesn't scream &quot;monster type made to fight that bounces attacks casually&quot;. If your Fortitude is less than 10/Plot Device, you're rotting meat to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>True however we\u2019re talking about level 9 fortitude which is close, with level 6+ powers so yes we\u2019re definitely in the realms of BS Fortitude, combined disciplines etc<br /> <br /> In terms of combat it depends how the ST plays it, pretty confident the All-Father is not about a honourable fight (I\u2019ve never had the impression that Vikings or their predecessor were honourable warriors in any way) more destroy an opponent at any cost picking off pack members with momentous usage of obfuscate, celerity and protean before finishing the final pack member, but yes this is power playing which IMO fits for something like the All-Father.<br /> <br /> For the Fenris to have such emnity it suggests he personally slew tribe members rather than them just suffering losses at the hands of his followers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514510#post1514510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In contrast, Garou are expected to go up against Zmei. And thunderwyrms, up to the extra-giant one that serves as a mobile BSD pit. If a vampire elder had to marathon that, they'd get torn apart just like that clown in the Zmei card for Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but only Rank 4 or 5s have a remote chance against the Zmei and canonically even they failed more often than not, usually by trying to take the dragons on head to head which was suicide.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no guarantee the All-Father would adopt the same tactics as the Zmei, he\u2019s just as likely to satisfy his desire for tooth and claw by ambushing the Garou and striking before they can use the advantage of their crinos forms or gifts.<br /> <br /> His concept of single combat could easily be ambush the pack, leave a single worthy survivor and kill them in single combat (aka Predator) - far less powerful vampires have subdued Garou packs look at Harold Godwinson\u2019s pack captured by mere Ancillae Ventrue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514510#post1514510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that vampire blood didn't de-power them and replace their magical-ness with just being regular ghouls, a la the long term effects of ghouling on mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but my thoughts were these aren\u2019t ghouls purely preserved remnants of Scandinavian crytoid humans, more the All Father preserving semi-mythic humans from his time, very mortal creatures, subservient due to his patronage or protection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-10-2023, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T15:44:30-07:00","id":1514519,"title":"","content":"I doubt I would ever use the All High himself as a physical opponent except as perhaps the &quot;final boss&quot; at the end of a chronicle where he and his followers are the major opponent. I'd probably use the stats for Baba Yaga as a comparison, but a little scaled down as he's not as ancient. But we do have canon stats for Brunnhilde. Those in Children of the Night are barely modified from her first appearance in 1e World of Darkness. She is probably an average, or even superior, version of the Walkure in general. But she doesn't seem that impressive compared to what veteran Garou packs can do. Although Brunnhilde was first written up in early Vampire to possibly be used in a Vampire game, not as an antagonist for werewolf. We can always bump up her stats. And we can always create older Walkure than even her.<br /> <br /> But I still believe elder vampires are best used off screen, setting things in motion. In so far that Brunnhilde herself is the leader of the faction until Odin returns from torpor, it's best she not be brought on stage. If an ST wants one of the Walkure to be on stage and physically interact with Garou PCs, I'd just create a brand new character and use one of the attested names of the mythological valkyries - Skuld, Gunnr, Hildr, Goll, etc.<br /> <br /> How powerful elder vampires are and how well they should do against Garou (as individuals, packs, sept) is very much a personal taste thing. Every gaming group will have their own standard. I think they should be a threat, but how that threat plays out can be very different at each game table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T16:00:09-07:00","id":1514522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514515#post1514515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Fenris to have such emnity it suggests he personally slew tribe members rather than them just suffering losses at the hands of his followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with this, and I think an important flavor text to establish would be specific stories of the kinds of defeats he inflicted on the Get of Fenris (and perhaps the Garou in general). We don't have anything epic in canon like what Set did, but he should be capable of doing something spectacular.<br /> <br /> I imagine that even though the All High was been around since 4000-3000 BC or so, that he didn't become &quot;Odin&quot; until some time between 500 BC and AD 500. That age puts him in &quot;methusaleh as storytelling device&quot; territory. At this point, he can begin doing things like killing individual Garou heroes, duping entire septs into doing something foolish, embracing beloved kinfolk, subverting human worshippers of a Gaia centered religious practice into human sacrificing vampire religion, cursing individual lineages of Garou, and all sorts of things that would humiliate the Garou (and make interesting backstories for PCs or chronicles).<br /> <br /> One thing I do is tie Odin into the events of AD 536 when the sun &quot;disappeared.&quot; Some historians speculate this is around the time that Odin became increasingly important in the Germanic pantheon, eventually usurping Tyr as the leader of the gods.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VbwyR5jLSUQ\" data-code=\"VbwyR5jLSUQ\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/VbwyR5jLSUQ/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T19:13:37-07:00","id":1514537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514515#post1514515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True however we\u2019re talking about level 9 fortitude which is close, with level 6+ powers so yes we\u2019re definitely in the realms of BS Fortitude, combined disciplines etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 9 isn't a plot device by a long stretch, so it's really not even remotely close to 10 dots, where the powers become like Whose Line Is It Anyway, where the rules are made up and the dice don't matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In terms of combat it depends how the ST plays it, pretty confident the All-Father is not about a honourable fight (I\u2019ve never had the impression that Vikings or their predecessor were honourable warriors in any way) more destroy an opponent at any cost picking off pack members with momentous usage of obfuscate, celerity and protean before finishing the final pack member, but yes this is power playing which IMO fits for something like the All-Father. </div> </div> </div>What a coincidence, I doubt that the Fenrir would extend any such concession toward him and probably arrive with every countermeasure they could lay their hands on, be it Fetish, Gift, or having Hyperion/Katanka-Sonnak as a pack patron. The vampires can't catch you if you're on fire!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For the Fenris to have such emnity it suggests he personally slew tribe members rather than them just suffering losses at the hands of his followers. </div> </div> </div>An entire caern and sept with it, according to the legendry in the revised tribebook. Including subverting Freke and Gere to his service.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True but only Rank 4 or 5s have a remote chance against the Zmei and canonically even they failed more often than not, usually by trying to take the dragons on head to head which was suicide. </div> </div> </div>It really depends on how you want to play things. Optimized characters can probably take on the challenge and even win with a bit less support than that (Might of Thor is only Rank 3, so you can be throwing out 20+ dice of damage hits, several at a time for several turns)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There\u2019s no guarantee the All-Father would adopt the same tactics as the Zmei, he\u2019s just as likely to satisfy his desire for tooth and claw by ambushing the Garou and striking before they can use the advantage of their crinos forms or gifts. </div> </div> </div>You seem to have gotten that mixed up. I'm talking about if a Zmei knocked down Valhalla's walls and started exhaling fire down the All-High's ass. Or a massive thunderwyrm ate the haven hosting him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> His concept of single combat could easily be ambush the pack, leave a single worthy survivor and kill them in single combat (aka Predator) - far less powerful vampires have subdued Garou packs look at Harold Godwinson\u2019s pack captured by mere Ancillae Ventrue. </div> </div> </div>Then the last one is Rank 6 and summons Fenris's war avatar. The All-High dies due to Rage 20 spirit. Or is &quot;merely&quot; an elder and uses The Good Death, taking the All-High with them into the Fame-Wolf's gullet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> True but my thoughts were these aren\u2019t ghouls purely preserved remnants of Scandinavian crytoid humans, more the All Father preserving semi-mythic humans from his time, very mortal creatures, subservient due to his patronage or protection. </div> </div> </div>Those don't sound impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T20:28:06-07:00","id":1514543,"title":"","content":"I once ran a campaign with Odin as the big villain. I designed the campaign for a player who pretty much only plays Get of Fenris. Ironically he didn't end up being able to play. I changed up Odin a bit from canon. He had been a mortal mage, a necromancer of vast skill with his goal of being able to learn how to surpass death. He would often journey deep into the underworld. At one point he discovered a vast tree that seemed to reach up forever, though as he got closer he saw that there were countless wraiths impaled on it, writhing in agony. Suddenly one of the branches grabbed him and impaled him to the tree as well. The tree was, in fact, a Neverborn that had grown so large it had burst free of the Labyrinth. For 9 days and 9 nights, Odin mentally wrestled with the Neverborn. Finally he managed to win, tearing free of the tree and having wrested countless secrets from the Malfean but was fundamentally changed in the process, far more dead than alive.<br /> <br /> He isn't exactly a vampire, but he's able to create vampires. His brood are able to pass themselves off as Gangrel (they possess Fortitude, Protean and Auspex). His undead Valkyries search for great warriors, turning them into vampires, or capturing the souls of warriors who had already died and returning to Odin who lives within the Underworld. While impaled to the Malfean, Odin had visions of the future, visions of Ragnarok or Gehenna. He gathers the souls of great warriors and pits them against each other where they fight, die and are reborn. He is preparing a vast army for the Apocalypse. Mechanically I statted him up as something more similar to a Onceborn. In addition to his magical prowess (which has only continued to grow since he was a mortal), he has a number of unique powers and abilities. He calls his underworld kingdom Valhalla but others call it the Dark Kingdom of Blood (due to the blood that is constantly spilled by his undying spirit warriors). <br /> <br /> Ultimately Odin is somewhat similar to Osiris from Mummy. Odin is largely trapped within the Underworld and sends servants out into the real world to do his bidding. His own power is incredible but it's difficult for him to directly emerge into the world, and he has only done so a handful of times over the centuries. In one of his visions he saw himself being killed by a fast wolf, Fenrir, and so he has made it his goal to destroy the creature and its children. Ironically his vision of dying in Fenrir's jaws is what started his feud and will likely lead to his death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-11-2023, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T03:45:59-07:00","id":1514563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514537#post1514537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Level 9 isn't a plot device by a long stretch, so it's really not even remotely close to 10 dots, where the powers become like Whose Line Is It Anyway, where the rules are made up and the dice don't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed but depending on how you want to build this foe, there are some formidable disciplines up to 9.<br /> <br /> Also depending on your appetite as an ST to utilise elder disciplines from DA or SV supplements there are powers that expand blood pool, grant lupine type qualities to vitae, nullify or soak aggravated attacks and so on, crinos type war forms, so entirely dependant on what source your happy to draw from.<br /> <br /> My overall point is this is a creature over 5000 years old, who\u2019s base physical stats could legitimately exceed a crinos and then their disciplines, so with the right strategy could prove an unpleasant opponent as a plot device.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514537#post1514537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What a coincidence, I doubt that the Fenrir would extend any such concession toward him and probably arrive with every countermeasure they could lay their hands on, be it Fetish, Gift, or having Hyperion/Katanka-Sonnak as a pack patron. The vampires can't catch you if you're on fire!</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely and I\u2019m not for a minute suggesting that the Garou are pushovers or if they knew who they were up against wouldn\u2019t throw the full weight of their powers, the Get have always been one of my favourite tribes and the most fearsome in martial ability.<br /> <br /> That said this is an age old opponent who has defeated one of the most combat ready tribes over the course of centuries so he is a bit different from other ancients, as you\u2019ve illustrated most Methuselah stay well away from the Garou with good reason = mincemeat.<br /> <br /> Probably like most longer in the tooth STs I\u2019m more interested in creating memorable plot devices and interesting NPCs, combat is part of our WTA games so it\u2019s nice to keep the Garou on their toes but still give them the opportunity to defeat the end of level villain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514537#post1514537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An entire caern and sept with it, according to the legendry in the revised tribebook. Including subverting Freke and Gere to his service.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which given his age and presumed desire not to commit suicide at the claws of an elder Get he undoubtably did through trickery, deploying his full range of supernatural powers and overwhelming force.<br /> <br /> Following your good points if his ego and desire for combat drove him to further enrage the Get I actually see him ambushing a junior pack as he has a far greater chance of winning and more importantly further enraging his enemies.<br /> <br /> But I take on board your points, this is just firing in some ideas about how to make him a different ancient than the usual unseen hidden manipulator.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514537#post1514537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those don't sound impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, I was just spitballing an idea on a different type of mortal servant.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T03:54:56-07:00","id":1514564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514543#post1514543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once ran a campaign with Odin as the big villain. I changed up Odin a bit from canon. He had been a mortal mage, a necromancer of vast skill with his goal of being able to learn how to surpass death. He would often journey deep into the underworld. At one point he discovered a vast tree that seemed to reach up forever, though as he got closer he saw that there were countless wraiths impaled on it, writhing in agony. Suddenly one of the branches grabbed him and impaled him to the tree as well. The tree was, in fact, a Neverborn that had grown so large it had burst free of the Labyrinth. For 9 days and 9 nights, Odin mentally wrestled with the Neverborn. Finally he managed to win, tearing free of the tree and having wrested countless secrets from the Malfean but was fundamentally changed in the process, far more dead than alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this idea, personally I really like the idea that prior to the Weaver calcifying reality there were mythic creatures that were embraced.<br /> <br /> Even if you keep him as Gangrel it\u2019s a cool concept that he was something more than human before his embrace and the idea of <b>Yggdrasil being a malfean or a malfean being a twisted version is brilliant.</b><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514543#post1514543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of his visions he saw himself being killed by a fast wolf, Fenrir, and so he has made it his goal to destroy the creature and its children. Ironically his vision of dying in Fenrir's jaws is what started his feud and will likely lead to his death.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a really good hook for his emnity towards the Get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T13:42:22-07:00","id":1514611,"title":"","content":"I agree with earlier posters that I think that giving the Most-High a sort of wilderness-survivalist vibe with his Autark, Anarch, &amp; Sabbat followers fits well and feels thematic for a Gangrel Methuselah of this stripe in the deep Scandinavian wilderness. I also agree that many of these early Gangrel &amp; Brujah probably fit well into the night-warrior mold of having a vampire-skewed notion of warrior-honor (I think the idea of picking of 4/5 of a pack from the shadows Predator style before a final 1-on-1 is a really cool and fitting idea).<br /> <br /> That said, I think another element that would be valuable to mine is the All-High as a powerful witch-sorcerer figure and what connections that might bring in.<br /> <br /> To begin with I can imagine that this could be used ti bring about a certain number of northern-undead and dark-magic themed followers. I\u2019m basically imagining wights (not 0 humanity vampires but more like Risen; undead followers of the Most-High) and monstrous fomori which resemble Grendel and his mother and the other laundry list of macabre northern-European folklore beasties that walk around with exaggerated size and open cavities in their bodies exposing decay and awful. <br /> <br /> (this could even be interesting for a vampire campaign - a group playing the assistants to archons or seasoned investigators who find a camp of monstrously oversized humanoids in a wilderness retreat, assume that it must be Tzimisce creations or some such, only to discover that they\u2019re actually the fomori/monster allies of a brood of followers of the All-High carrying out some esoteric scheme which is ostensibly to avert Gehenna but naturally is horrific in its own right, whether or not it has any efficacy)<br /> <br /> I also think that the All-High should probably have some witches, sorcerers, and perhaps even true Awakened Mages amongst his followers. I imagine that you could see a few radical-pessimist splinters of the northern crafts who would ostensibly be Verbena or Euthanatos but who have become persuaded somehow that the weakening of Magick is related to the coming of Ragnarok and so have joined forces with the All-High.<br /> <br /> For a Mage chronicle it might be interesting to have a similar case as the one above, a group of Council mages assuming these weird wilderness-vampire death-cultists are Nephandi only to find out that, no, they\u2019re a particularly dark circle of mages associated with the All-High (who are probably more fantastic hunters of the Nephandi than the PC circle itself).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T14:47:28-07:00","id":1514617,"title":"","content":"The next group are changelings. This shouldn't stop discussion of how to use vampires among the Host. But as others have stated, there are a lot of themes present in &quot;Odin&quot; that can be exploited. Fairies are one of them. In mythology, Odin lead the Aesir and later allied with a separate group of gods called the Vanir. Most mythologists place the Vanir among the elves. In my own chronicles, the Vanir is another name for the Tuatha de Danann. The Unseelie sidhe (elves) of House Aesin are their descendants in northern Europe. So a very long time ago, the All High - a powerful vampire even back then - made pacts and oaths with the fae of that noble House.<br /> <br /> Changeling introduced the idea that the Get of Fenris had a blood oath against the sidhe. I never liked that as it was a huge restriction introduced fairly late. What if players had a Get of Fenris PC in a pack of Stag? This would completely change the existing dynamics of a game. It would invalidate a lot of existing games. So in my chronicles, I changed it so the Get of Fenris only had a blood oath against the sidhe House Aesin instead. That would allow most interactions between the Get of Fenris and changelings to be unchanged, but simply gave STs an additional tool if they wanted to introduce complications. House Aesin therefore made their oath with the All High because 1) the Get were mutual enemies, and 2) the All High knew prophecies of Endless Winter (Ragnarok/Gehenna/Apocalypse) and seemed to be a useful ally.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, this oath is kept by members of the Shadow Court inside House Aesin (and their allies) after the Shattering. A tenet of the Shadow Court is to understand the supernatural world, and make and break alliances as necessary. These fae consider their alliance with the All High as very necessary. I also place within this group a secret tradition of Black Magicians (Dauntain). They trace their forbidden arts to the All High. The ignorant consider them Dauntain, but they reject the idea that they are in thrall to Banality. They merely seek to master its mysteries to use against their enemies - especially the Jotunns (Fomorians) and their allies. They acknowledge it is dangerous lore, but are confidant they can use it carefully enough. Because of their control over Banality, the Black Magicians among the Aesin are critical in maintaining the fae\u2019s relationship with the vampire followers of the All High. They let the other members of House Aesin/Shadow Court (and their other changeling allies) to not worry about any negative impact involving Banality.<br /> <br /> There were probably once fae who had blood bonds with the All High in return for mutual oaths of loyalty, but those are long since gone given that the All High has been in torpor for a thousand years and the massive changes to the fae as well. If the All High ever awakes from torpor, some of the might consider renewing the oath (I also see fae oaths being effective on the All High). But that would be only with the All High. The fae would not consider doing it with any other vampire, including the Walkure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T14:50:04-07:00","id":1514618,"title":"","content":"I think having changelings allied to Odin gives certain tools to a Werewolf ST. First, feuds with these fae against other fae could justify involvement by packs of Stag that tie back to stronger Werewolf elements. Second, changelings can make intriguing enemies on their own whether the ST uses actual Changeling rules, treats them as spirits mechanically, ties it into the Arcadia Gateway, Trod domains, or the many other ways faerie stuff is included in the basic setting. Third, this expands the menace of Odin because many Garou with ties to the Changelings are not Get of Fenris. So the ST has additional hooks and perspectives to introduce the plot. Fourth, it can be quite some time before the PCs realize that these fae are even connected in any way to Odin and vampires. This can be useful in setting up long term plots. PCs might see these fae antagonists to be more of a distraction than actual enemies, or attempt to deal with them in a more positive way than they would if identifiably Wyrm minions were doing the same thing. It just gives the ST a lot more tools.<br /> <br /> I see the fae as providing an unexpected edge to the Host against their foes. Fae and vampires don\u2019t work closely together. Each group mainly pursues their goals independently. But they are aware of the other and their leaders can communicate with one another as needed. Occasionally one side calls in the other when necessary, and often exchanging favors. See them more like as allies than one single team.<br /> <br /> Traditionally, Changeling and Vampire are seen as opposite ends of the World of the Darkness with very little crossover. That makes sense, but there from time to time both game lines make reference to one another. I think an independent group like the Host provides more effective justification and appropriate flavor text than trying to force sects like the Camarilla or Sabbat to changeling society as a whole. I think the limitations added here (House Aesin and the Shadow Court) makes sense, though an ST could always decide to expand things a bit. Even if crossover isn't your thing in playing either of those games separately, I think in the context of antagonists in Werewolf, it can work very well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:12:47-07:00","id":1514620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514611#post1514611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think that the All-High should probably have some witches, sorcerers, and perhaps even true Awakened Mages amongst his followers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odin as some kind of sorcerer is definitely a theme I am going with. The All High should have some form of thaumaturgy, and some of that should be passed on to his disciples. The Paths should all be very old paths (classic folklore magic, not RPG combat magic) - Weather Control, Neptune's Might, Green Path, Elemental Mastery, and Spirit Manipulation seem appropriate to me.<br /> <br /> Instead of Walkure, these vampires might be called Volva or Ergi or Runemasters (depending on the type of magic) within the Host. But they all work within a tradition established by the All High, and they should be seen as a separate tradition than the Hermetic ways of the Tremere, or the Koldunism of the Tzimisce, or the other groups. This isn't so much a Clan Gangrel school of magic, as one associated strictly with the All High and while Gangrel make up a lot of its users, other clans would be participants as well.<br /> <br /> And this will also show up when I discuss mortal cults, paths of sorcery, and the like. I don't talk much about actual Mages, but I agree it'd be easy to throw in a few individual Mages if you want.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly, in the Ars Magica game, the Bjornaer - although a Hermetic house - were descended from Odinic forms of magic. I think it'd be easy to figure out some things if you want to go back to the Ars Magica setting for inspiration, perhaps for some rivalry with the Tremere.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T18:47:53-07:00","id":1514644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514543#post1514543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I changed up Odin a bit from canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of your character back story for Odin could be easily ported as the biography of the All High before he was embraced (or even afterwards). This is good stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514543#post1514543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of his visions he saw himself being killed by a fast wolf, Fenrir, and so he has made it his goal to destroy the creature and its children. Ironically his vision of dying in Fenrir's jaws is what started his feud and will likely lead to his death.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent way to explain some of the All High's behavior. In myth, there are a lot of prophecies that only come true because the prophecy itself causes people to do things they otherwise would not have done. And this can easily be tied into Odin's various attempts to divine the future in his attempts to prevent Ragnarok.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T23:34:22-07:00","id":1514656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514618#post1514618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think having changelings allied to Odin gives certain tools to a Werewolf ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be the first time tho'<br /> <b>War of Silver and Iron </b>from Dark Ages: Fae Rulebook comes to mind,<br /> The Garou discovered that the Fae had used them in the War of Seasons. The Garou slaughtered every fae they found and taught humanity about the restricting power of cold iron. The Fae answered by teaching humanity the power of silver and such spread the usage of these metals among the humans, giving them the tools to ward off the supernatural. The War of Silver and Iron ended when the whole conflict proved to be too expensive for the Fae and they withdrew into Arcadia. After the last werewolf who remembered the conflict had died, they eventually returned<br /> <br /> A similar could have happened/could happens with the conflict between the Get of Fenris and the All-High's Einherjar (you even could use the possibility, the Einherjar are a seperate vampire breed and not descended from Caine. it could work - they are technically the draugar of myths just with soul and sanity attached... but when Frenzy, they are act like the draugar. One can explain, the Frenzy of an Einherjar is when Garmr, the &quot;beast&quot; try to drag back the escaped soul to its mistress, Hel in to her realm, and while the soul try to fight of the blood-stained guardian of Hel's gate, the body regresses back to its draugar-state)<br /> Dark Ages Mage mentions Niflheim, the &quot;Dark Kingdom of Ice&quot; where from the Queen of the Dead rules from her seat in her capitol city of Hel. The city of Hel lies amidst an icy mountain chain, and overlooks a deep abyss that supposedly drops straight into the Abyss. Within the naturally occurring ice it is said that many wonders may be found, but also many terrors. So, too, do they claim that a bridge exists in the mountains that leads to the land of the fey.<br /> <br /> So the connection is there not to mention Norse mythology is ripe with Dark Elf, Light Elves, Dwarves, Giants and Monsters...<br /> A ST could easly use the Fae (especially the nasty ones, or outright the House Balor, they act in concert with Houses Ailil and Leanhaun anyhow, content to bask in the prestige of bringing the Black Spiral Dancers and the modern Fomori into an alliance with the Unseelie...) who saw the possibility to support the All-High and his Einherjar while not really keen to have the Get of Fenris around...<br /> <br /> On the other hand it wouldn't be the first time a vampire were actually the &quot;good guys&quot; in a sense<br /> Sutekh was the champion of Ra, and Serpentis still have the power Pact with Ra, witch invoke the alliance that once existed between Ra and Sutekh and when this is done, the Setite is freed from the greatest curse of his kind; the pain of the sun....<br /> Zapathasura was created/appointed to combat the asuratizayya (Kuei-jin) by the Gods<br /> <br /> The Fenrir Wars from Wolves of the Sea could be seen as the Gods not really supporting the Fenris<br /> In the Einherjar's myth Odin and the All-High is actually two different entity, the All-High is more like an Avatar of Odin, or more like a High Pirest than the actual god, and the Einherjar trace themselves to the warrior Canarl, who was raised from the dead by Odin. The creation myths of the einherjar, as different as they are from the Christian vampires of Europe, foster different duties. There is no sense of filial responsibility. To be chosen as an Einherjar is to be blessed as one of the warriors who will fight and die at Ragnar\u00f6k.<br /> <br /> Fenris is <i>not really</i> a cool guy - not an insane bloodthirsty monstorsity like Griffin for example, but not a nice Totem<br /> I actually had a theory, Winter Wolf, the totem of Wisdom and Fenris are either the &quot;sons&quot; or apsects of the Garou original patron, the one who was patron of the whole species, the Old Wolf of the Woods who is the dying Totem of Respect. (The Old Wolf of the Woods is a totem of spirituality rather than war. He misses the days when all Garou looked to him as their spiritual father, and resents the growing number of homid and metis werewolves as compared to the dwindling lupus. Old Wolf of the Woods is a sad spirit; he knows that he will exist only so long as wolves roam the face of Gaia. When the last wolf falls, he will cease to be.)<br /> <br /> It is totally possible the Gods/Incarna/whatever actually support the Einherjar and the All-High becasue Fenris really dancing on the edge of insanity or falling to the Wyrm... and don't forget hi is in some materials eyeing Helios to devour the Sun to rise in power... (so All-High with his Rune magic maybe/possibly binding Fenris, a mighty totem to prevent the Ragnarok or delay as long as possible actually doing a favor to the world... but naturally the Get of Fenris are not happy a vampire bound and chained their Patron...)<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 06-12-2023, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:15:50-07:00","id":1514730,"title":"","content":"I'm thrilled to see a new topic in this vein, as the whole old topic about Setites was a lot of joy for me. I wanted to drop two NPC's I made for older games there that might be of use to some, but I'm really keen to see where this one will go.<br /> <br /> I'd like to preamble this that I'm not keen on the Gangrel Elder having the same shtick as Set, and would prefer for there to be Aesir and Vanir as spirits created from human belief (or redifnining themselves to mooch of existing belief) who provide and help their followers and are in conflict with the Garou. I also played with the idea of that Odin being a wizard who sacrificed himself on the world tree and that maybe his followers are a kind of Draugr blessed by his power and the power of the World Tree (I do like the idea it ties into the Malfeans, and I was really thrilled to see that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> had similar ideas where to take this group to mine). Playing into this further, I'd possibly have the Valkyire as some kind of special Wraiths that enable the souls of the dead to merge with the bodies of the living, creating a new type of Risen?<br /> <br /> In essence, YES, I want to fight the Aesir with my Get and Fianna, I'd just prefer them not to be Vampires (even if we can map them with Vampiric powers or have the &quot;filthy undead&quot; label applied to them). In portraying them and their power I'd probably pillage sources like the Vaelderman, Once and Future King Thor:Vikings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:22:26-07:00","id":1514758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514617#post1514617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next group are changelings.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, this oath is kept by members of the Shadow Court inside House Aesin (and their allies) after the Shattering. A tenet of the Shadow Court is to understand the supernatural world, and make and break alliances as necessary. These fae consider their alliance with the All High as very necessary. They let the other members of House Aesin/Shadow Court (and their other changeling allies) to not worry about any negative impact involving Banality.<br /> <br /> There were probably once fae who had blood bonds with the All High in return for mutual oaths of loyalty, but those are long since gone given that the All High has been in torpor for a thousand years and the massive changes to the fae as well. If the All High ever awakes from torpor, some of the might consider renewing the oath (I also see fae oaths being effective on the All High). But that would be only with the All High. The fae would not consider doing it with any other vampire, including the Walkure.</div> </div> </div> </div>An idea I like from Dark Ages Fey is Great Oaths (if memory serves I think their Gold and Silver Oaths) in modern nights if the Aesin/Shadow Court have an ancient Great Oath with the All Father it might provide them with plentiful dark glamour or even shield them from Banality.<br /> <br /> Which would support their view that this alliance necessary, it holds back The Endless Winter. <br /> <br /> This probably requires the All Father to wake to renew the Great Oath, but perhaps the Black Magicians (Dauntain) maintain the rites of the oath to eke out its dwindling power .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514617#post1514617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally, Changeling and Vampire are seen as opposite ends of the World of the Darkness with very little crossover. That makes sense, but there from time to time both game lines make reference to one another. I think an independent group like the Host provides more effective justification and appropriate flavor text than trying to force sects like the Camarilla or Sabbat to changeling society as a whole. I think the limitations added here (House Aesin and the Shadow Court) makes sense, though an ST could always decide to expand things a bit. Even if crossover isn't your thing in playing either of those games separately, I think in the context of antagonists in Werewolf, it can work very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this depends on if your campaigns rule is a vampires low humanity is automatically tied to high banality, or defined by the vampires connection to Triatic forces.<br /> <br /> If the All Father is more orientated to the Wyld (plus the Wyrm) rather than the Weaver despite low humanity he may have low Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 06-12-2023, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T20:01:32-07:00","id":1514789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514730#post1514730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to preamble this that I'm not keen on the Gangrel Elder having the same shtick as Set, and would prefer for there to be Aesir and Vanir as spirits created from human belief (or redifnining themselves to mooch of existing belief) who provide and help their followers and are in conflict with the Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least the backstory of Odin is still unknown so an ST has lots of room for interpretation even if they keep to canon. With Set, you not only have that he is a vampire, but you have Osiris, Isis, Horus and many others identified as explicit supernatural forces. If you want to keep to canon, it locks a lot in. The game just has a lot of vampire characters that were either the source of a mythological entity or using it as a mask: Mithras, Tiamat, Louhi, Baba Yaga, and so on. I personally like that, even if it can create a lot of havoc if you try to incorporate real mythology into the games.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping even if you replace Odin as vampire with Odin as Mage or something else, you can get something useful from the thread.<br /> <br /> As for me, whatever the relationship between the vampire All High and the Norse religion, there is the idea in Mage that all the pagan gods exist in some form in the Astral Plane. If you want, it's entirely possible the Odin that exists as a physical figure on the world interacts with these Astral spirit beings somehow. Maybe he even visits them on the Astral Plane using Auspex. There may even be some strange kind of connection between vampire Odin and Astral Odin. That may be a bit too gonzo for me, but some STs might pull some kind of Astral presence with the vampire (or mage or whatever) well.<br /> <br /> Despite both the All High and Set being vampires, I am trying to distinguish both the head vampires and their followers to be distinctive from each other so it is a very different feel for the Garou PCs who may be opposing them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514730#post1514730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In essence, YES, I want to fight the Aesir with my Get and Fianna, I'd just prefer them not to be Vampires (even if we can map them with Vampiric powers or have the &quot;filthy undead&quot; label applied to them). In portraying them and their power I'd probably pillage sources like the Vaelderman, Once and Future King Thor:Vikings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't quite written up the various Aesir and Vanir as members of the Host, but I will have an upcoming post that deals with spirits associated with the faction as a result of chiminage made between the All High and some spirits. It's a mini spirit brood available to the various sorcerers of the Host. And there's no reason why it couldn't have some Jagglings that act in ways similar to certain mythological beings. Maybe &quot;Loge&quot; as a fire elemental (or a Surtur spirit) closely allied to the All High, as an example. Some kind of rainbow spirit with some variant of Heimdall as a name. A sea spirit or ocean storm spirit with a similar name o Ran, and so on. It might not be <i>the</i> Aesir or Vanir, but it could fill that role if someone has the itch.<br /> <br /> People are making a lot of interesting contributions in how they portray the Norse pantheon in their games. There's a lot of incompatibility with them, but it is surprising how many of their ideas can be changed over to a completely different approach and still be evocative. It's the major reason I talked about using the mythology as an inspiration for the faction, rather than trying to determine what the gods themselves should be - too many different ideas on what the truth should be in everyone's own chronicles.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T00:34:25-07:00","id":1514807,"title":"","content":"So, assuming Odin is an elder 4th generation vampire, how would you use him? I think the best place to start looking is at Baba Yaga. She was also an ancient 4th generation vampire. She was a vastly powerful magic user, and in mythology Odin possessed unparalleled skill with magic and runes. After awakening, Baba Yaga constructed a vast Shadow Curtain preventing any supernatural beings from entering or leaving Russia. She easily crushed all of the l9cal vampires beneath her iron feet. She controlled the Zmei, immensely powerful dragons capable of wiping out multiple packs of werewolves. Even though she was &quot;only&quot; 4th generation, she was so powerful the werewolves of Russia had to take the unprecedented step of forming an alliance with vampires, Mages and other beings to defeat her.<br /> <br /> I think that's around where I would want the All Father to be - an unimaginably powerful and ancient vampire capable of causing havoc for werewolves.<br /> <br /> Like Baba Yaga he's ancient (though likely not quite as ancient) and his mystical capacity is probably comparable. He wouldn't have anything like the Zmei serving him, but the big difference is that he's have his own childer, the Valkyries. Baba Yaga had a few older vampires serving her, but she was generally suspicious and untrusting of them. Meanwhile Odin would likely have multiple ancient, thousands year old 5th and 6th generation vampires serving him. Importantly, his Valkyrie would have spent thousands of years seeking out powerful warriors and turning them into fellow vampires, preparing them for Ragnarok. So Odin would likely have a powerful army at his disposal and some of his followers would be so old and powerful they could take on a pack of werewolves. It makes for a nice set of boss fights as the PCs kill his Einherjar and then Valkyries before fighting Odin himself.<br /> <br /> If I were to go the full vampire Odin route, I'd likely go full Gonzo-tier. I'd have him awaken and move to take control of a large part of Scandinavia. He has no use for, or respect for, the Masquerade. His soldiers begin openly moving to take control of cities and towns. Vampires, governments, the Technocracy start scrambling to try and cover up what's happening. Something like this could force another shakey alliance between werewolves and vampires and maybe other groups as both as everyone moves to destroy Odin. If it were specifically for Werewolf, then I'd make it a bit &quot;video gamey&quot; and co.bat heavy where the players slowly take down his minions before facing him directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-13-2023, 03:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T01:20:51-07:00","id":1514809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514807#post1514807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I were to go the full vampire Odin route, I'd likely go full Gonzo-tier. .</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agree, whatever the All-High\u200b is in your chornicle, he should be something big<br /> Vampire or not, the return of Odin (and actually the likes of Baba Yaga and other historical/Mythical names) should be equaly huge<br /> Especially from the Fae perspective<br /> The coming of the Endless Winter and the triumph of Banality was imminent. Science and Reason continued to destroy the mysteries of the world and organize and systematize reality.<br /> Until a miracle occurred. On July 21, 1969, millions of people across the globe saw, on their televisions, astronauts land on the moon. Glamour rocked the world as it was released from confinement with the return of Wonder to so many people simultaneously. From science came forth magic, if only for a moment. That moment was enough.<br /> Now just immagine Odin - again, whetever he is in your chonicle - openly return? (Technically this should have happened in the case of Baba Yaga too, but the little grandmother actually kept a very low profile) And with him the Old Ways? In the very jaded World of Darkness - heck even in our world - I wouldn't be surpsied people would flock to bend a knee to a literal God, especially if he proves, yeah, he is the real deal<br /> Similar happened when in Fallen Lucifer manifested in live TV over Los Angeles and Hell broke loose (excuse the pun) but kickstarted Faith<br /> Odin&quot;s open return should be on par with Lucifer&quot;s manifestaton that millions of people saw<br /> And more improtantly should have an effect like the Moon Landing<br /> With Odin probably would came all the Nine World and its inhabitants (and maybe would start <i>War of the Nine Realms</i>\u200b not unlike the one Malekith started in Marvel comics<i>)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T02:34:48-07:00","id":1514813,"title":"","content":"Tying Odin to the fey is interesting. As a vampiric blood god, he'D probably have closer relations with the Unseelie Court. In such a case I'd probably give him a unique ability where he can Ghoul changelings without interfering with their fey nature. In fact maybe he could even have Dark Ages type fey in his retinue - his blood gives them a semi-static permanency that has allowed them to retain their power for centuries.<br /> <br /> Heck, depending on the chronicle, Odin might not necessarily be the immediate villain. &quot;Ragnarok approaches and I have returned to slay the Sepent that gnaws at the roots of the World Tree.&quot; If the Serpent he plans to slay is Set (or the Wyrm itself) that might set the grounds for Odin and his followers to operate as allis, at least for a time.<br /> <br /> *edit*<br /> <br /> Building on that, it might be an interesting twist to have Odin and his brood operate in a more heroic light. If the serpent that seeks to kill Yggdrasil, and the universe, is the Wyrm, then Odin is an enemy of the Wyrm. Sure he reeks of the Wyrm, but he and his vampires have spent centuries slaughtering is minions - fomori, Black Spirals, etc. His return is the start of the Apocalypse, and some tribes are split on working with him. Maybe, pulling into 5e a bit, if Fenrir ends up falling to the Wyrm after what happens to his tribe, that could explain why he kills Odin and it could make for an interesting twist on the usual, &quot;vampire bad&quot; that we normally see in Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-13-2023, 06:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T04:58:39-07:00","id":1514824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514813#post1514813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Building on that, it might be an interesting twist to have Odin and his brood operate in a more heroic light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Friend or foe, both could work<br /> IF the All-High\u200b is used as a 4th Generation Gangrel (with a knack of Rune magic) but fights against N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr, the dragon who gnaws at a root of the world tree, Yggdrasil (you even could throw a curve ball with the ancient legends, that tells that the roots are trapping the beast from the world, and N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr tries to gnaw itself free... Yggdrasil is Gaia? Or the Roots of Yggdrasil keeping N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr/Wyrm trapped actually the Weaver's webs? Yggdrasil the World Tree is actually the Pattern Web, the frame of the Universe? God so many possibilites!) then he is a potential <i>ally</i><br /> (And then we not even dragged in the whole Fae connection)<br /> Or a horrible foe<br /> Or both - depending the Tribe<br /> Especially if not reeks of Wyrm <i>that much </i>(The All-High\u200b even had <b>Blood-Horn </b>- one drop of blood was added to the ale within, the whole liquid would change into blood. The same would occur with vampiric vitae and mead, which made it possible for the All-High and his einherjar to substain themselves without leaving his temple in Uppsala. - the Artifact that actually minimalized the effect they potentially could have since no really needed to Hunt) I easly could see lots of Garou even find the idea appealing of the Old Ways what He would brought back... and actually would help the All-High\u200b to drag back the world, while its kicking and screaming in to the ancient days, when honor and glory were the norm, might made things right and the banes of the modern world, polution, factories, overpopulation and so on was nowhere...<br /> Unlike Baba Yaga, who had nasty... very nasty friends, the All-High\u200b actually not that bad from a Garou point of view. From a Fenris'? Sure. But at that point I think many opportunistic tribes, like Shadow Lords or even the Black Furies would see the not-that-loved-tribe-anyway as a potential collateral damage and an acceptable loss<br /> The Nation offed a Tribe or whole species for way less after all...<br /> Would make some interesting stories thats for sure!<br /> (Even could lead to the W5 setting where the Fenris lost their mind... even as a cause or even as an effect. Fenris wanted to consume Helios and start Ragnarok... the Tribe became in the eyes of others BSD 2.0... Or... facing/realizing Tribes allied themselves even nominally with the All-High? The Tribe and the Patron looses it after such a betrayal in their eyes)<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T11:25:34-07:00","id":1514864,"title":"","content":"When it comes to concern over the distinction between vampire gods and formal gods who are spiritual-metaphysical, I think that there are ways to square the circle on this.<br /> <br /> I agree that having Odin simply be a vampire runs serious risks of becoming gonzo but I also think there are ways to have figures walking around who can be the Most High in a meaningful sense. This is getting into some nuances of magical/mystical thinking a little, so I hope what follows makes sense.<br /> <br /> I think that you can have a metaphysical It which we can call Odin (what this \u2018It\u2019 is, is a larger discussion than I can manage atm). This It contains the god Odin of the Aesir of Asgard (which you can have represented in the Umbra &amp; Astral Realm as well as being an ineffable spiritual substance which cannot fully be materialized). However I don\u2019t think that precludes the possibility of imagining mortal cults whose practices feed into the spiritual mass which constitutes various parts/forms/manifestations of this spiritual substance. Again, how you interpret this can vary. Furthermore there is a precedent in mystical thought for a layering of presence and manifestation. I do not thinks it is infeasible to allow for their to be a metaphysical It substance for Odin, a variety of umbral manifestations which are recognizably Odinic, and even that a mortal-turned-vampire could apply this mask to themselves. I would even say that this idea of a mask does not need to be limiting - I don\u2019t think that one necessarily needs to suggest that the vampiric Odin is false because you can consider it a Mask; the mask is real and effectual.<br /> <br /> This is somewhat similar to how I feel about having gods appear in werewolf in general. My usual attitude is that there are a variety of primordial spirits in the middle-umbra and that some manifestations of these spirits will \u2018put on the mask\u2019 of a god (for example: there are plenty of storm-spirits, some of whom may put on the Mask of Thor). That by no means makes them a fake-god but it is a more nuanced situation than their being one discrete and true god-form. You can think about it in terms of various rl masking/embodying practices: ritual practioners of say, voudoun or a variety of animist traditions, who through special preparation become the vessels of spirits (gods, ancestors, etc.); they become, in real terms, the spirit but that doesn\u2019t necessarily mean that the spirit is not also active or present elsewhere, it simply means that it has been embodied and realized here.<br /> <br /> I think one can allow for a case like that with the All High, a mortal man who became a vessel for a part of the metaphysical substance we call Odin, and has remained such even after becoming a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T14:27:01-07:00","id":1514881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514864#post1514864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is somewhat similar to how I feel about having gods appear in werewolf in general. My usual attitude is that there are a variety of primordial spirits in the middle-umbra and that some manifestations of these spirits will \u2018put on the mask\u2019 of a god (for example: there are plenty of storm-spirits, some of whom may put on the Mask of Thor). That by no means makes them a fake-god but it is a more nuanced situation than their being one discrete and true god-form. You can think about it in terms of various rl masking/embodying practices: ritual practioners of say, voudoun or a variety of animist traditions, who through special preparation become the vessels of spirits (gods, ancestors, etc.); they become, in real terms, the spirit but that doesn\u2019t necessarily mean that the spirit is not also active or present elsewhere, it simply means that it has been embodied and realized here.<br /> <br /> I think one can allow for a case like that with the All High, a mortal man who became a vessel for a part of the metaphysical substance we call Odin, and has remained such even after becoming a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a lot of STs here I \u201cborrow\u201d ideas from other games, one thing I\u2019m a fan of is the Mythics from In Nomine, the old gods who\u2019s power and worship is diminished but who work to regrow their essence, physical avatars would be one way to restore power.<br /> <br /> One thing we have in our games is in older times an Incarna war where the older Triatic or nature incarna warred with the newer human incarna.<br /> <br /> The idea that the All Father is a physical representation or mask of an Incarna Odin is a really good one which also explains why other supernaturals are willing to follow him.<br /> <br /> Creates another area where everything\u2019s thrown on its head for the Garou, a creature fighting for the old ways, patronised by a totemic spirit, great paradox for the Garou.<br /> <br /> Also reminds me of the different Odin\u2019s in American Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T17:55:46-07:00","id":1514901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514824#post1514824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at that point I think many opportunistic tribes, like Shadow Lords or even the Black Furies would see the not-that-loved-tribe-anyway as a potential collateral damage and an acceptable loss\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the All High should be just enough of a nebulous figure that there can be Garou who could decide to assist him (in at least some ways) and at least justify it among themselves.<br /> <br /> So the Shadow Lords as a whole might not, but the Bringers of Light camp might. If the Bone Gnawers of 1e were willing to make deals with the Sabbat, then there might be Bone Gnawers somewhere in northern Europe who would be willing to make some kind of agreement. Maybe Uktena of the Society of the Bitter Frost might be interested in the magical aid of the All High and cooperate against their common enemies - the Get of Fenris. I'm sure there are others people will mention.<br /> <br /> That's the kind of thing STs will always heavily disagree about, but I do think an ST would be able to pull off a good enough IC justification for such Garou in game. Not a mainstream one, and one that would likely be hidden. But play up the angle that Odin wants to avoid/delay/defeat the Apocalypse enough, it makes sense that some Garou would ask &quot;why not?&quot;<br /> <br /> It would also provide the Host with a very small and imperfect intelligence network inside the Garou Nation. One that would not be willing to betray the Nation, but might provide enough information that allows the Walkure and others to avoid certain areas or fights.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T23:07:44-07:00","id":1514922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514864#post1514864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one can allow for a case like that with the All High, a mortal man who became a vessel for a part of the metaphysical substance we call Odin, and has remained such even after becoming a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is an interesting point, and an ST does not even actually need to believe it in order to introduce it into a chronicle. While it would be self-serving for a vampire to explain it this way, it may be more interesting to introduce the idea to Garou PCs through an elder Theurge, a Mage, human occultist, or whatever.<br /> <br /> One nice thing about using an IC perspective, is it does not force the PCs to agree with the ST OOC. It's simply one thing to argue about IC, and the OOC truth does not ever need to be revealed (assuming the ST has decided on one).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T02:57:56-07:00","id":1515080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514789#post1514789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At least the backstory of Odin is still unknown so an ST has lots of room for interpretation even if they keep to canon. With Set, you not only have that he is a vampire, but you have Osiris, Isis, Horus and many others identified as explicit supernatural forces. If you want to keep to canon, it locks a lot in. The game just has a lot of vampire characters that were either the source of a mythological entity or using it as a mask: Mithras, Tiamat, Louhi, Baba Yaga, and so on. I personally like that, even if it can create a lot of havoc if you try to incorporate real mythology into the games.<br /> <br /> I'm hoping even if you replace Odin as vampire with Odin as Mage or something else, you can get something useful from the thread.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutley. Due to my dislike, I've never used Odin the vampire and his brood in my games. I am however open to brainstorming and am enjoying the discussion. Who knows I might even change my mind by the end of it.<br /> <br /> In general I dislike the whole &quot;oh and this historic diety is a vampire&quot; thing that a lot of the methusalehs have, as I feel it interferes and deevaluates the ethnology and mythology that I enjoy using in my games. After all if I am running Werewolf, my priority is what it needs to do for my game, not what Vampire has to say about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T23:50:36-07:00","id":1515207,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ll also put some Changing Breed types among the All High\u2019s forces, or at least concepts found in the Werewolf gameline. These are also fairly minor forces in terms of power, and I would be very careful before using any of them in a Vampire chronicle. But Werewolf has more scope, and werewolf PCs can handle these kind of potential foes. I\u2019ll provide each one with their own post.<br /> <br /> In my chronicles, Sam Haight is not the originator of the Skin Dancers, merely one of its rediscoverers. And the Garou pelt that allows Skin Dancing is not limited to be used by only one person, but can be passed down to later generations. The All High, in fact, was the person who first figured it out thousands of years ago and taught the first kinfolk how to do it, and there has been a secret lineage of alienated kinfolk Skin Dancers down the ages allied to Odin (which I call the Ulfhednar). Besides them, the All High also figured out how to do the same with the Gurahl and Grondr, but those lines are now lost (although at least one werebear pelt has survived). So there are both a kinfolk line and Skin Dancers among the Host.<br /> <br /> The Ulfhednar are patronized by the Minotaur spirit just like other Skin Dancers, but they know the spirit as the Grinder (Grendel) instead. The Minotaur spirit, for some reason, has a ban for his packs to slay the children of Pegasus. Ulfhednar packs under the Grinder are sometimes mistaken by the Black Furies to be Garou of the Get of Fenris, and their attacks are one (small) reason for the poor relations between those Gaian tribes.<br /> <br /> The vampires have created a story to secure the loyalty of these Skin Dancers. They are the blessed of Odin, specially choosen to battle Odin\u2019s enemy: the Children of Fenris (the Garou). They warn such children that the Get of Fenris are as cunning as they are cruel, and will lie to them in order to turn them against Midgard. (One of their basic lies is to claim their mother is not the evil giantess Angrboda, but the goddess Jord.) However, if they become bloodsworn to the Walkure, the goddess children of Odin, their minds will be protected against such tricks. Such is the power of Odin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T23:52:17-07:00","id":1515208,"title":"","content":"I also provide the origin of the Carrion Crows/Buzzards to the All High (who first learned how to steal the power of the Corax by finding their spirit eggs and use them for his own purposes). This is the origin of the myth of Hugin and Munin. The Host calls this type of Buzzard the Valravn (mechanically the same but slightly different flavor text). The Valravn have proven critical to allow the Host to learn about their enemies among the Changing Breeds.<br /> <br /> Unlike the Buzzards associated with other Wyrm minions, the Valravns are mostly indistinguishable from true Corax except for a slight stench of gravemold or carrion about them, or the acrid tang of blood in the air that seems to hover around them. Often other Fera usually see the Valravn as particularly grim and warlike Corax, and do not guess as to their true nature. One of the goals of the Raven Banner is to ensure that they can always locate at least two Corax spirit eggs to serve as the organization\u2019s spies and messengers. Like the Skin Dancers, the Valravn are also blood bonded to the Walkure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T23:54:15-07:00","id":1515209,"title":"","content":"I am also considering the possibility of adding some Ceilican to the Host. Mainly because I like the association of cats with Freya (who in turn would be tied to the elves of House Aesin). It is limited to only a handful of feline Ceilican in Scandinavia. They are the descendants of Ceilican originally allied to the Unseelie House of Aesin, and thus knew of their alliance with the All High. This arrangement lasted thousands of years. That all changed when the Unseelie lord Samhach (not from House Aesin) discovered a way to bind and enslave the Ceilican, and shortly afterwards other elven lords did the same. But a few members of House Aesin who were part of the Raven Banner offered to protect a small handful of feline Ceilican as a result of their previous assistance to the Host. (O perhaps non-fae members of the Host who knew about them hid them. I am open to changing my mind on who the benefactors should be, but right now I am making it some of the Aesin (or at least Shadow Court fae aligned with them). They, in effect, became servants, but they were at least free from the magical compulsions of their race. Thus when the Ceilican Tybalt de Leon managed to break these magical chains and lead the majority of Ceilican to the New World, a small number of Ceilican decided to stay behind and assist their old allies out of gratitude, now as equals and not servants.<br /> <br /> The Ceilican who are part of the Host are very few in number, all of feline breed, and all remain in Scandinavia close to their allies. These Ceilican concentrate on Shadow Craft, particularly paths of spirit sorcery. They are probably the Host\u2019s foremost experts of the Penumbra. They are perhaps the All High\u2019s only true allies among the Changing Breeds, but it is important to note their involvement in the alliance is through the Fae, not the vampire lord himself (who had disappeared before Samhach enslaved his first Ceilican). And since then they have neglected their previous fae saviors in favor of mortals of the Raven Banner. Just to be more safe and limit the chance of news of their survival from reaching the other fae.<br /> <br /> These Ceilican view their participation in the Raven Banner (and they almost exclusively use this name) as part of their duties to Gaia. And while they honestly help their allies (they feel a debt to those fae who could have enslaved them but did not and valued the various supernatural help the alliance provided them during those centuries), they are also gathering much knowledge about their allies in turn. Who knows what information will be important when the Apocalypse comes? Though few in number and feeling gratitude for their earlier help, they intend to use the Raven Banner for their own purposes, and not be content to be the minions of others. For now they prove useful to their allies both changeling and mortal, and almost unknown to the vampire members of the alliance.<br /> <br /> I am going back and forth on this. These few Ceilican are not obvious members of the Host, and their small numbers mean they may never even show up in game. Little would be missed if they were not included, and there are many easy objections to their inclusion. However, my personal taste leads me to want to include them simply because I think a few Ceilican make a good flavor text. And it possibly allows for the ST to introduce the Host as an unnamed background in a more postivive manner than introducing them through their more obvious villainous elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T23:56:25-07:00","id":1515210,"title":"","content":"There is a rare group of fomori associated with the Host. The All High made pacts with a special kind of Scrag in the ancient days to create a kind of rage filled warrior. This partially lead to the legends of the Norse bersekers. These fomori were, in fact, more common than the Skin Dancers known by such names.<br /> <br /> These fomori appear human, but have the minds and souls of beasts consumed by Rage. They are more aggressive, physically potent, and resistant to injury. They are beserkers, but without any shapechanging. They were found throughout the Norse settlements dedicated to the All High, often blood bonded and even ghouled to the vampire followers of the All High. They were the protectors of the barrow mounds these draugr slept in during the day, and the vanguard against the All High\u2019s human enemies in battle. They were employed as disposable shock troops to protect the more important supernatural members of the Host.<br /> <br /> These fomori, however, required drinking a toxic mixture of alcohol, henbane, hallucinogenic mushrooms, and other poisonous ingredients that tainted the body to make it possible for Scrags to possess them. This wicked knowledge was purged during the Christianization of Scandinavia as dangerous witchcraft. The modern Host works to restore this knowledge, but has only created an imperfect potion. Although it does create fomori, the fomori is actually no more powerful than a normal human unless he imbibes the potion agains, and it only works for several hours. The original version only required the fomori to activate their powers (through a Dexterity + Primal Urge roll). Members of the Host are coming to believe the full secret of the potion will only be relearned once the All High fully returns from his torpor.<br /> <br /> I would assign the following fomori powers to these beserkers.<ul><li>Berserker (5 Rage)</li> <li>Armored Skin</li> <li>Extra Speed</li> <li>Regeneration</li> <li>Sense Gaia</li> <li>Spirit Ties</li> </ul>The fomori berserkers belong to both mortal cults and as vampire allies/retainers. The knowledge of the toxic potion is known to select Walkure and mortal sorcerers of the Host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T00:05:15-07:00","id":1515211,"title":"","content":"If I might add ,don't forget good old <b>Gunnhild</b> from <b>Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised, </b>who is based on Gunnhildr Gormsd\u00f3ttir a quasi-historical figure who appears in the Icelandic Sagas<br /> <br /> Gunnhild, the &quot;Mother of Kings&quot; and Fiend-witch is a Nordic Tzimisce of great potency and age from Scandinavia.<br /> Originally a Finnish witch, she married Eric Bloodaxe and fought the Christian advance of Olaf Tryggvason before her Embrace.<br /> Although her struggle and use of blood magic eventually failed to stop her people's conversion, she survived well past the fall of Uppsala, the sacred royal lands of Freya herself.<br /> During their internment in the frozen lands, the Scandinavian Tzimisce introduced the Sabbat to the notion of the Jomsvikings. These warriors once ranked among the Fiend Witch's entourage, but Gunnhild lost them in the war against Christianity.<br /> Because of Gunnhild's standing among the local Gangrel who still called upon Odin in battle, the Sabbat entered Scandinavia with little difficulty, and they gained valuable allies in the fight against the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Blood magic, rune magic and a nice dose of Koldunism, connectio nto the fae, Odin and all...?<br /> Any Fenris would have a very hard time against the Mother of Kings and her allies<br /> She is a discount Baba Yaga technically<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T13:18:27-07:00","id":1515295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1515211#post1515211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I might add ,don't forget good old <b>Gunnhild</b> from <b>Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised, </b>who is based on Gunnhildr Gormsd\u00f3ttir a quasi-historical figure who appears in the Icelandic Sagas\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I had completely forgotten about this character. But by 2001 when this clanbook had come out, I had determined that the Revised edition didn't scratch my itch, and was increasingly ignoring Revised canon and beginning to work out the first details of what I actually wanted to see in the chronicles I ran. So I hardly remember about anything in the Tzimisce revised clanbook.<br /> <br /> While I do think it's good to look at existing characters and wonder how they could be part of the Host, I am also leery of the idea that simply because a vampire is in northern Europe that it means they must be a follower of Odin. He's not the only powerful methusaleh in the region. He had to have enemies, rivals, and so on while he was active. And of course, Gunnhild would only have been a neonate or ancillae before Odin went into torpor. She's not Gangrel (or Brujah), the clans most associated with the Norse and Odin. And even her mortal origins (in the clanbook though not in history) place her outside of Scandinavia (though her life is integrated with the historical Norse).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1515211#post1515211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood magic, rune magic and a nice dose of Koldunism, connectio nto the fae, Odin and all...?<br /> Any Fenris would have a very hard time against the Mother of Kings and her allies<br /> She is a discount Baba Yaga technically\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your general assessment, but I think my preference would be to make her a vampire <i>enemy</i> of the Host. She's already established to be in the Sabbat. She is best associated with Finland, not the actual Norse lands of Scandinavia. So I am inclined to place her among the enemy Sabbat of Finland aligned with the Malkavian methusaleh Louhi. Not among the mainly Ventrue anti-tribu lorekeepers that are somewhat alienated from the main sect and possibly open to defection (in my reading). So I think the character is best used as another vampire who would oppose Odin's Host.<br /> <br /> Of course, it is possible that in her very young days - centuries before the Anarch Revolt - she might have been a memberin the Host, and could still exchange favors with them in the early days of the Sabbat, but I think any such loyalties would have withered from her centuries spent in the Sabbat. When the Walkure began to take in the mid-20th century, they probably found that Gunnhild's loyalties were now very different. But it is possible some boons might be owed by either side, creating an interesting tension.<br /> <br /> I also admit that a strict reading of the revised clanbook does not explicitly state she is Sabbat. Just that she was &quot;hospitable&quot; allowing the Sabbat/Tzimisce to survive before they fled to the New World. So a case can be made that she had her own reasons for helping them, and does not indicate a member of the sect. Still, she'd be a Tzimisce elder post-Anarch Revolt. If she wasn't affiliated with the Sabbat itself by that point, I would think they would most likely destroy her. Any non-Sabbat Tzimisce should be an enemy. So I'm inclined to more likely make her some kind of Bishop or Archbishop of Finland for the Sabbat, overseeing their activities there and helping Louhi.<br /> <br /> However, I do like the idea that regardless of her loyalties now, that the Get of Fenris could very well believe she is an important member of the Host. As you explained, there are a lot of thematically appropriate elements. They would think its stupid to not believe that the &quot;Witch Gunnhild&quot; or &quot;Mother of Kings&quot; isn't one of the Host, or perhaps even one of its most important leaders. The Get of Fenris simply do not have the knowledge needed to understand vampire politics. So I would think it would be a good idea for the ST to present things as if Gunnhild was a member of the Host. And if for some reason the PCs actually investigated or attacked her and her own forces, it'd be up to them to figure out the truth. It's good for the setting to let the Garou be ignorant on a lot of things.<br /> <br /> I recognize this is more a matter of taste though. Different players will be inspired to do differently, and there are all sorts of justifications that can be made. Whatever an ST does with Gunnhild, I do think this is a great call out which will add to the Host's flavor and use in a chronicle in some way. So thanks for posting this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T16:17:25-07:00","id":1515702,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit surprised that none of the posts on the Changing Breeds produced any comments when the fae posts did! Even if only to hear, &quot;Nah, that's a stupid idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm moving on to the next bit. There are many human cults dedicated to Odin and his other mythological names. They are distinct from historical Norse or contemporary neo-pagan worship of Odin. The cults of the Host are the direct descendants of the original secret society of retainers and allies created by the vampire All High to serve him. This society dates back to the Germanic Migration Age and earlier. However, these human cultists find it useful to recruit members from modern neopagan groups, provided they can \u201ccorrect\u201d them of the \u201cerroneous\u201d lore of the mythologists and folklorists, and introduce the \u201ctrue\u201d and \u201chistorical\u201d (albeit secret) rites and beliefs of the cult of the All High that they have preserved for millennia. And since there is a historical continuity going back to the All High in the setting, they'd have the &quot;facts&quot; to prove it.<br /> <br /> This secret society of \u201cOdin\u201d worshippers has survived for a thousand years since the All High went into torpor. The mortal followers are closely connected with supernatural forces like the Ulfhednar and the Black Magicians of the Aesin. In turn, the humans provide numbers for protection, a source of Glamour for the Aesin, and future kinain. Some serve as Allies, Contacts, Retainers, and Herds for the Walkure and other vampire followers. Others as the kinfolk for the false changing breeds. These supernatural creatures provide the verifiable magic power of the Odin cult. It is rare for specific mortal cults to serve more than one supernatural group of creatures, and each faction has different needs and desires. There can be certain groups that may not be under the &quot;control&quot; of supernatural creatures, but to be members of the Host they still need to be in contact with them. Maybe there is some kind of ritual that can be done that is the mystic equivalent of a telephone ringing among those who swore loyalty to the All High. And many are likely ignorant of the true nature of any of them. A Walkure may be accepted as an actual valkyrie, and not considered to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> Some mortals are also able to practice a form of sorcery that has survived the decline of magic. Such knowledge is not widespread and usually limited to only a few with the talent, intelligence, patience, and time to learn it. Both men and women practice this magic. Sorcery Paths often include those of Divination, Enchantment, and Herbalism/Brewing. Maybe Cursing, Healing, Hellfire, and Weathercraft to spice things up. I would try to keep the more blatant powers limited to the standard splats, and keep mortals more to a supporting role.<br /> <br /> In actual history, many kingly lines of the Norse claimed descent from Odin. So it\u2019d be real easy for these mortal cults to claim they are the actual descendants of Odin as justification for their secret society. It\u2019s part of the family secret or ancestry. Some may consider themselves descended from the Ynglings, and thus the true kings of Sweden or whatever. Whether that\u2019s actually true or not is irrelevant. It just needs to be what these people actually believe. It\u2019s not like anyone could actually verify such claims. Although in this age of easy DNA testing, I\u2019d probably state that these families do heavily share a common paternal gene that is not present in most of the general population. But that isn't necessary. There can be all sorts of people in Scandinavia, England, Germany, and other places that might trace their lineage back to &quot;Odin&quot;.<br /> \u200b<br /> Mortal members of the Host likely view their participation as purely a religious matter, and be happy that Odin and his children/allies favors them with any attention. But I think they should consider being prepared for Ragnarok to happen at any time to be an important obligation, and it'd be a good way to distinguish them from similar groups. I think it might also be interesting to see individual members of this secret society to be in the same organizations that some Get of Fenris kinfolk might join - historical societies, ancestry groups, neopagan religious groups, etc. Could lead to some interesting kinfolk encounters especially since on the surface people repeating the standard legends of Norse mythology won't be seen as &quot;odd&quot; to these kinfolk who are used to people always getting them &quot;wrong&quot;. Someone who claims Fenris is a demon wolf and that Odin is great will just be accepted as normal. And then the ST can do the big reveal later on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-25T08:39:28-07:00","id":1516106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1515702#post1515702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a bit surprised that none of the posts on the Changing Breeds produced any comments when the fae posts did! Even if only to hear, &quot;Nah, that's a stupid idea.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Changing Breed ideas are good and well connected to the Fey, the idea that one of the Sidhe houses brokered a different pact with the Ceilican gives the latter a bit more substance than they might be fallen or extinct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1515702#post1515702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could lead to some interesting kinfolk encounters especially since on the surface people repeating the standard legends of Norse mythology won't be seen as &quot;odd&quot; to these kinfolk who are used to people always getting them &quot;wrong&quot;. Someone who claims Fenris is a demon wolf and that Odin is great will just be accepted as normal. And then the ST can do the big reveal later on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the most interesting aspect of the mortal followers, mortals that the Get or even Fianna claim as their own are actually descendants of the All High.<br /> <br /> Coming full circle there\u2019s also the possibility of their being Ceilican or Ronin Viking Garou kinfolk with these bloodlines (after all their only descended from pure Viking bloodlines not revenants or anything esoteric), so the mortal aspect to the All Highs sect could prove quite a area of competition and fiercely protected by the supernaturals.<br /> <br /> The other aspect is of course the mortal cult aspects reinforcing the various supernatural arms of the family (oaths for the Fey, breeding stock for the changers, purer blood for the kindred). <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T19:03:32-07:00","id":1516299,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you like it.<br /> <br /> There is a small Heretic group of Wraiths called the Companions of Hermodr that have connections with the necromancers of the Host. In mythology, Hermod was the son of Odin who traveled to the underworld to obtain Balder\u2019s release from Hel. So I think Hermod would fill the role of either a Ferryman, Shining One, Reaper, or at least a wraith with lots of Argos. I would make Hermod someone who was part of the Host long ago who became a wraith after he died, and he managed to re-contact the All High. Perhaps even someone who volunteered in some kind of ritual sacrifice by the All High in order to create an agent in the Underworld. There can be other Heretic groups associated with Norse mythology, but this group is the one related to the Host.<br /> <br /> These wraith Companions mainly act as a spy network, keeping the Host informed on the happenings of the Underworld, particularly the Far Realm of Hel. One of the All High\u2019s concerns is that the dead will cross over the Shroud during the Apocalypse, and the leaders and best scholars of the Host follow events in the Underworld with keen interest. The Host of the All High would oppose any group seeking to bring down the Shroud. Ragnarok, of course, has much relevance among Wraiths although they know the concept as Doomsday. Doomsday is a core idea in many Heretic cults. Perhaps the \u201cLoki\u201d who will sail Naglfar with the monstrous hordes of Hel is some kind of Malfean. (Now I'm thinking there could be some sort of Spectre Nephwrack cult that presents itself as servants of &quot;Loki&quot; attempting to escape his prison in Hel.) This is something that will occur some time after Gehenna happens, but is still obviously part of Ragnarok. The All High is concerned with more than just the Jyhad, but the everything concerning the End of the World. I think this also distinguishes him from a lot of other vampires whose interest just comprises Gehenna and seem to believe the Antedeluvians will rule forever afterwards.<br /> <br /> Very few Companions of Hermodr remain. After the Christianization of Scandinavia, recruits plummeted. The group lost many members after Stygia issued the Proclamation of Reason and banished all Shining Ones, one of which was Hermodr. The surviving Companions went underground. Their recruits are now mostly limited to wraiths reaped from mortal cult members who are already adherents. Though in recent decades as neopaganism increases, the Companions have been able to find a new small source of recruits. Whether the wraith Hermod himself is still around, or Transcended, or fallen to Oblivion; is immaterial to the current status of this group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T19:05:17-07:00","id":1516301,"title":"","content":"Given their small numbers and the importance of their mission in the Underworld, few Companions are able to help their compatriots in the Skinlands. Indeed, many of the older Companions now lack Fetters and cannot even remain in the Shadowlands. However, a few are able to manifest in or affect the Skinlands, and they might be used in an extreme emergency. A more likely scenario of assistance is when the necromancers of the Host summon a wraith and ask for them to provide knowledge or to spy on others. I wouldn't overdo it, but this can provide a slight edge against the PCs - and perhaps attributed to a vampire's Auspec, fae Art, or something more mundane.<br /> <br /> In exchange, the Host must assist the wraiths in terms of what matters to them - protecting Fetters, creating Memoriam, maintaining Legacies, preserving Haunts, and other work that supports Wraith Backgrounds. It would take a lot of work for an ST to build all this up for use in game, but it could lead to some really interesting set pieces of seemingly abandoned or lonely buildings in Scandinavia maintained by the Host to do just this, or perhaps a minor local folk museum.<br /> <br /> I should also note that Odin and the valykries also serve as psychopomps in Norse mythology, and this might be reflected as some kind of Necromancy that they know which allows them to enter the Underworld and perhaps interact with their allies. I would probably keep this knowledge very limited though, perhaps just to Odin and one of the Walkure. The Host after all is still quite small and only makes up a small fraction of each supernatural splat.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s also potential ties back to the fae with the concept of Adhene like the Keremets, which are dead souls trapped in the Dreaming as opposed to going to the Underworld or Transcending. Perhaps some of Hermod's companions are Keremets, and there are Black Paths of Balor that lead to some of their hideouts in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> It might be interesting to introduce the Host in a Garou game not by typical means, but by interaction between this wraith group and Garou like the Ivory Priesthood, Silent Striders or Uktena who know the Descent into the Underworld rite, or even a pack of Owl. One thing I want is to have many different ways of introducing the Host of Odin into a Werewolf game from sources that are not typically associated with vampires. Done properly, PCs might think these are all different groups until they begin to notice certain connections or common themes among them.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:16:30-07:00","id":1516571,"title":"","content":"The next thing I want to bring up is how the Host might be impacted by the death of Baba Yaga (assuming that happened in your chronicles). Baba Yaga was building her own - much greater - armies in Russia as the same time the Walkure were waking up and exploring. And while Odin and Baba Yaga did not have same goals, this does not mean some of Baba Yaga's followers would not want to join, link, or ally with the Host. Even if you accept canonically in your own setting that Baba Yaga was killed by Nictuku, there is still the question of what happened to all those forces she was building back in Rage Across Russia. The two forces are very different in their motivations and goals, but individual members might have reasons to work with both methusalehs. So we need to step back and review what we might want to pull from that sourcebook.<br /> <br /> We know the Odinndohter were sent to explore what was going on behind the Shadow Curtain. They could have contacted some of the armies of Baba Yaga after she was destroyed and convinced them to join the All High. The Army of Night and its \u201cGeneral\u201d Viktor was made up of 25 vampires. Per the sourcebook, their job was to control the cities and use human bureaucracy to support the Shadow Curtain by keeping out outsiders. There could be individual vampires who will prefer working with the Host rather than the Camarilla, Sabbat, or as independents. I suspect this part of the Baba Yaga\u2019s Army just went back to being regular vampires and either joined the Camarilla or remain unaligned and independent. But there are still some named NPCs associated with her. One was the 6<sup>th</sup> generation Gangrel methusaleh/elder Viktor who was embraced in 6 BC, and who was blood bond to Baba Yaga. Now that the bond is gone, he could join the Host or be its enemy.<br /> <br /> Then there is Sergei Voshkiv, Baba Yaga\u2019s 5<sup>th</sup> generation childe embraced just in 1991. Voshkov did not seem to be a member of the Army of the Night and ran a separate group, the \u201cEyes of Baba Yaga\u201d. The Eyes are (of course) an intelligence group of Nosferatu of Baba Yaga\u2019s line that are lead by Sergei. The text actually states \u201cchilder of Baba Yaga\u201d, but given their leader is also a childe, but just a neonate, I think it makes more sense these are much weaker generation Nosferatu of her line that could be intimidated by Sergei\u2019s powerful generation and closeness to Baba Yaga. I don\u2019t think he\u2019s a good candidate for the Host given his backstory, but he\u2019s likely still out there doing something. His stats in Rage Across Russia are utterly fantastic given his young age, but I would associate that with help from Baba Yaga. Now that she is gone, his augmented powers are likely back to where they should be for such a young vampire. Young vampires of potent generation are a diablerie target risk.<br /> <br /> I think the real question is what motivated these 25 vampires. Was it a fear of Gehenna/Apocalypse, and they hoped Baba Yaga would allow them to survive? Was it a love of the Russian motherland a desire to protect it? Was it fear that Baba Yaga would devour them if they did not help her? Was it love through the Blood Bond? That will determine whether they would be willing to defect to the Host. Unless one of the powerful vampires join, I don't think this will noticeably improve the Host. But any new vampire members would allow them to expand their operations in the former Soviet Union and gain new recruits.<br /> <br /> The Host might also be helping \u201cTyphon\u201d Incarna break free of Grandfather Thunder, though perhaps the spirit uses an alternative name like \u201cDonar\u201d, \u201cThor\u201d, or \u201cThunraz\u201d among the Host. For those who don\u2019t have the sourcebook (and spoiler warning), this was a spirit of Grandfather Thunder\u2019s brood who wanted independence and was helping Baba Yaga to get it by corrupting the Shadow Lords to the Wyrm. He had a sept and several packs following him, and some of the members had outright joined Baba Yaga (in secret). If you go down that route, much depends on whether you base Typhon as he was in Rage Across Russia or as written in Revised Shadowlords Tribebook (which does not mention any of this), or decide to make those descriptions as two different spirits. Personally, I think these two different depictions of Typhon are incompatible with one another, and was part of Revised era attempt to dissociate the sourcebook with the game (which Baba Yaga's destruction in a Vampire sourcebook fulfilled). But if you want to go down the route of &quot;Typhon&quot; as portrayed in Rage Across Russia, I think the spirit - assuming he was not found out and destroyed by Grandfather Thunder - would be looking for a similar ally and the All High could be it. This would give the Host some potent new allies.<br /> <br /> Perhaps one or more of the Verbena helping Baba Yaga (there were four in a chantry), who are more interested in supernatural lore or information concerning the end of the world than they are about concerns over contemporary Russia, might join. The All High and some of his followers possess many occult secrets and magical knowledge which might tempt these mages. <br /> <br /> I don't see the All High as trying to work with the Zmei in Russia or try to free Koschei. I think he'd be opposed to both since he wants to prevent or survive Ragnarok. But here there is an opportunity for the Host to serve as secret or dark quest givers to the Garou. Perhaps they even do so with their new Shadow Lord allies (through Typhon) in order to promote them in ranka nd prestige.<br /> <br /> Lastly, there are also ongoing negotiations between the Host and the Ravnos elder Durga Syn and the forces she compiled to fight against Baba Yaga. Their goals are not identical, but there are some similarities. I would think that the discussions have been honest, and it is possible that Durga Syn could rise to be an important leader among the Host. The big obstacle is that for most of Durga\u2019s existence, the Gangrel methusaleh has been in torpor, and she has no way of knowing if he would be a similar menace like Baba Yaga. For now the negotiations continue as Durga Syn considers her options and whether it is wise to associate herself with such a being like the All High.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Baba Yaga still exists in your chronicle, then the activities of the Odinndohter complicate things for her, and that is its own post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T07:16:26-07:00","id":1516967,"title":"","content":"Whilst I really like some of the early edition kitchen sink plot ideas, always hated the off screen destruction of a villain the writers made too powerful, The Baga Yaga was one of these.<br /> <br /> In our home canon she was destroyed by greater Incarna taking exception to her raising the Zmei and other Wyrm beasts, following the destruction of major caerns spirits, they broke the Spirit Curtain allowing various forces to cripple her army and allowing the Garou to eventually trap and kill her.<br /> <br /> Following some of the ideas from earlier in the thread in terms of the All-High I can actually see the Walkure being opposed to the Baga Yaga seeing her as a direct sign or manifestation of Ragnar\u00f6k/Gehenna and if they are opposed to the Wyrm actively fighting her or at least aiding those who are.<br /> <br /> The Baga Yaga represents one of the most Wyrm corrupted kindreds in canon, after all the Zmei could easily be children of J\u00f6rmungandr and the Walkure could have assisting in bringing about her destruction.<br /> <br /> In terms of aftermath Victor would be an interesting one, a fellow Gangrel but one that served the Gehenna Hag, if Durga Syns actions were more in line with the All-Highs agenda I can see him being an opponent and their interests colliding (that\u2019s if he survives the Silver Fangs hunting him down).<br /> <br /> Sergei Voshkiv is as you\u2019ve said a undead man walking literally a target for diablerie for every disgruntled kindred, I can see him desperately trying to form an alliance with another powerful elder quickly.<br /> <br /> Typhons an interesting idea, if he manages to keep his shenanigans secret from Grandfather Thunder and survives, manifesting as Thor would be cool, however the host wouldn\u2019t be able to protect him if his secret gets out. I can more see him throwing heavy favours at powerful Shadowlord packs and trying to prove his value.<br /> <br /> If the Host were opposed to The Hag I can also see them forging links with the Evenk Dreamspeakers which they may maintain to this day.<br /> <br /> All told Russia would worry the All High as it\u2019s the first major manifestation of Ragnar\u00f6k in the flesh, a manifestation that could have easily spilled into the Nordics so I can see the Host being quite active in cultivating allies in the region.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T07:21:32-07:00","id":1516968,"title":"","content":"Did anyone ever home cannon Baba Yaga being killed off by, say, <i>player characters</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T11:07:05-07:00","id":1516983,"title":"","content":"Turth to be told, no<br /> Not even an Elder chronicle<br /> Michael, Mithras, Meneleus, Boukephos, Samiel... fair play, I would say<br /> But the likes of Baba Yaga, who went toe-to-toe with her own Antediluvian on the next night following her Embrace and managed to chase away Absimiliard?<br /> No<br /> She is on the level of Ur-Shulgi, Odin, the Dracon, Hazimel or the Word-Eater<br /> There are 4th Generation monstrosities who are &quot;above&quot; the other &quot;low tier&quot; 4th Generation monstrosities...<br /> Those &quot;rookie 4th gens&quot;? When the stars are right and with preparations could be defeated by players<br /> But Baba Yaga and the likes of her...?<br /> No, not really<br /> <br /> Of course this is just me, but in my eyes they are so ancient and powerfull, they even would give some Antediluvians a run for their money<br /> <br /> We don't know much about Odin, but the All-High\u200b is the center of the Einherjar society for a reason; safe to assume, everything from the myths are true, he knows/inveted Rune Magic, probably familiar with necromancy (and collecting the best souls in &quot;Valhalla&quot;, and they ready to answer his call, not unlike Demongo, the Soul Collector, from Samurai Jack or Shang Tsung) in the posession of artifacts, like the Blood Horn and his spear, familiar with the &quot;Nine Realms&quot; and probably forged alliances left and right with the Fae and god knows what else... and the top of that, one of the most fearsome and powerfull Garou tribe, the Get of Fenris considered/considers him a <i>threat</i><br /> Hell, he even probably bound Fenris with his magic in one point, tho' like most of it this is just pure speculation from my part, and like Baba Yaga, ate Septs for breakfast<br /> Hating a vampire is one thing, most of the Garou do<br /> But septs and whole Tribes were and are <i>terrified</i> of Baba Yaga, Sutekh and Odin <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T11:49:21-07:00","id":1516987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1516571#post1516571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Host might also be helping \u201cTyphon\u201d Incarna break free of Grandfather Thunder, though perhaps the spirit uses an alternative name like \u201cDonar\u201d, \u201cThor\u201d, or \u201cThunraz\u201d among the Host. For those who don\u2019t have the sourcebook (and spoiler warning), this was a spirit of Grandfather Thunder\u2019s brood who wanted independence and was helping Baba Yaga to get it by corrupting the Shadow Lords to the Wyrm. .</div> </div> </div> </div>If Susanowo, the Lord of Storms; the Hakken totem now possibly corrupted by the Wyrm from Hengeyokai: Shapeshifters of the East joins to form an alliance - or unholy trinity?<br /> May Gaia have merc\u200by on the souls...<br /> Never ending strom, like in the Underworld would probably cover the Earth/Midgard, eternal darkness...<br /> ...and with it?<br /> Cold<br /> Fimbulvetr<br /> Next step: Ragnarok<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T12:02:21-07:00","id":1516988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1516983#post1516983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turth to be told, no<br /> Not even an Elder chronicle<br /> Michael, Mithras, Meneleus, Boukephos, Samiel... fair play, I would say<br /> But the likes of Baba Yaga, who went toe-to-toe with her own Antediluvian on the next night following her Embrace and managed to chase away Absimiliard?<br /> No<br /> She is on the level of Ur-Shulgi, Odin, the Dracon, Hazimel or the Word-Eater<br /> There are 4th Generation monstrosities who are &quot;above&quot; the other &quot;low tier&quot; 4th Generation monstrosities...<br /> Those &quot;rookie 4th gens&quot;? When the stars are right and with preparations could be defeated by players<br /> But Baba Yaga and the likes of her...?<br /> No, not really<br /> <br /> Of course this is just me, but in my eyes they are so ancient and powerfull, they even would give some Antediluvians a run for their money<br /> <br /> We don't know much about Odin, but the All-High\u200b is the center of the Einherjar society for a reason; safe to assume, everything from the myths are true, he knows/inveted Rune Magic, probably familiar with necromancy (and collecting the best souls in &quot;Valhalla&quot;, and they ready to answer his call, not unlike Demongo, the Soul Collector, from Samurai Jack or Shang Tsung) in the posession of artifacts, like the Blood Horn and his spear, familiar with the &quot;Nine Realms&quot; and probably forged alliances left and right with the Fae and god knows what else... and the top of that, one of the most fearsome and powerfull Garou tribe, the Get of Fenris considered/considers him a <i>threat</i><br /> Hell, he even probably bound Fenris with his magic in one point, tho' like most of it this is just pure speculation from my part, and like Baba Yaga, ate Septs for breakfast<br /> Hating a vampire is one thing, most of the Garou do<br /> But septs and whole Tribes were and are <i>terrified</i> of Baba Yaga, Sutekh and Odin</div> </div> </div> </div>Still doesn't help make her getting offed by a one off character much less cheap. They could have at least let players <i>try</i> to take her on. Weren't Werewolf players told they expected to inevitably lose, anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T12:27:22-07:00","id":1516990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1516988#post1516988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still doesn't help make her getting offed by a one off character much less cheap</div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> But Vasilisa at least had a little setup<br /> Baba Yaga said was Embraced around 5000 BCE, so in 2000 when she died, was 7000 years old<br /> Vasilisa was said to be <i>twice</i> the age of Baba Yaga<br /> Baba Yaga may have left her humanity behind centuries ago, but &quot;Vasilisa&quot; did not have much to begin with... and was not very human even in the distant past when he was human.<br /> Anything resembling human thought process is now gone. He \u2013 it \u2013 has become the predator, and is now more a <i>presence</i> than a sentient being and taking on recognizable, almost archetypal forms to hunt its prey.<br /> In this regard, something that once was a human boy transcended and became the <i>idea</i> of the Hunt, the <i>presence</i> or <i>essence </i>of a Predator<br /> Something lovecraftian and unknow<br /> <br /> True, the whole scenario wasn't the best written one, but the only thing I could immagine realistically was capable to deal with Baba Yaga was... well.. something like the thing called itself Vasilisa, and because of its nature, being an idea that takes shapes to hunt, it was fitting, it manifested as Vasilisa, the only person basically in myths that was able to 'win' against Baba Yaga<br /> And it was capable to do this because in a sense narrative causality<br /> Because the power of the Legends and Stories<br /> A bit Changeling and Drweaming or Mage territory (or the two combined), but the <i>thing</i> that took the Vasilisa's form was able to win because of those. Because human beliefe, and the power of stories<br /> Becasue why the third boy will always succeed where his two brothers failed before him in a sense<br /> Surprsingly they set up this quite nicely<br /> In Night of Propecy and Rage Across Russia and other supplements they made Baba Yaga something so powerfull, realistically speaking, no one should been able to defeat her. She was for all tense and purposes the Baba Yaga of the myths<br /> So only a myth, the only one in the stories who won against her had a chance - not only had a chance, but was &quot;destined&quot; to won<br /> And Baba Yaga knew that<br /> She feared no one, truly no one<br /> But when she saw the thing that manifested as Vasilisa?<br /> She was <i>terrified</i><br /> She knew it is ower<br /> And all of its flaws, the story did great in that sense<br /> Sure could have been better, but how they set up the whole thing and what Vasilisa is or became? Was fitting<br /> <br /> Follwoing this, it is fun to think about Fenris is destined to kill Odin... but in turn be killed one of Odin's Children, Vidarr will tore his jaw opened and killed him, avenging his father, Odin.<br /> If someone follows this path, would give a very dark and very grim tone to the chronicle<br /> And would explain the burning Rage of the Fenris - they know their totem is prophesied to... lose.<br /> And in the mean time will give hope<br /> Surtr's flames will consume... but will cleanse Gaia\u200b<br /> ...just they will be not around to see it\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T15:37:13-07:00","id":1517009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1516988#post1516988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still doesn't help make her getting offed by a one off character much less cheap. They could have at least let players <i>try</i> to take her on. Weren't Werewolf players told they expected to inevitably lose, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the board could easily do a &quot;how to run or improve Rage Across Russia&quot; thread like we've had threads on the Vampire forum on running some of the City By Night books. Rage Across Russia could easily have been twice or thrice the size and still left an enormous amount for the ST to figure out on their own. It's concept is so big, but there are so few details available.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-02T17:37:04-07:00","id":1517017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517009#post1517009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the board could easily do a &quot;how to run or improve Rage Across Russia&quot; thread like we've had threads on the Vampire forum on running some of the City By Night books. Rage Across Russia could easily have been twice or thrice the size and still left an enormous amount for the ST to figure out on their own. It's concept is so big, but there are so few details available.</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be a fun collab topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T00:19:39-07:00","id":1517038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1516983#post1516983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, he even probably bound Fenris with his magic in one point, tho' like most of it this is just pure speculation from my part</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, remembered why speculated that<br /> The 1st edition Get of Fenris Tribe Book mentioned, wyrm-minions assaulted Fenris lair and bound the Wolf-Father in chains, preventing it to enter Gaia's realm again<br /> In my head, connected the two <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> ...of course, the first edition also mentions, the Get were tought how to use tools and iron weapons by the Dvergar - Dwarves and they made bitter enemies of the Trolls and the Jottun - great giants<br /> <br /> Teh revised edition went in to details about the mythic (or bronze, depending of the story) age<br /> According that, the Fenrir battled against the minions of the Wyrm that crept from the earth and had survived the Ice Age. The Fenrir worked to repopulate their protectorates, sowing forests to strengthen the Wyld and making alliances with its children, the Fae<br /> Back then the capital Caern of the tribe was Heimhalla in the Ural mountains, the residence of the Vanir and home to Fenris and Sigun (Queen of the Vanir and Fenris would-be mate and girlfriend).<br /> During these days, the Fenrir of Heimhalla were locked in war with the Jotunn kingdom of Utgard and the Aesir kingdom of Valhalla. Valhalla was led by a being named Odin...<br /> Odin marshaled his forces and attacked Heimhalla while the bulk of the Fenrir was in a campaign against the Utgardian forces. Aided by two traitors, Freke and Gere, Odin burst through the Caern's defenses and massacred the Fenrir's Kin. Sigun fought valiantly, but could not stand against Odin. Her sacrifice, however, saved the heart of the Caern, as the entire structure collapsed over the invading forces. The surviving Fenrir, lead by Great Fenris himself, vowed vengeance and turned westward, settling in the lands of modern Scandinavia.<br /> <br /> If we follow this tale, it seems Odin followed the Get of Fenris - chased them even - with the Army of Valhalla (aka, the Host what <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\">Black Fox</a> </b>\u200bmentioned) and eventually managed to bind the Totem itself or at least achieved to pevent the Incarne to enter Gaia's realm<br /> <br /> In any chases, it is interesting to explore this war entangled with myths and legends but either version (and be it vampire, changeling, werewolf, - mage even - sources) would make the All-high and the followers of Odin as a Werewolf setting element or foe without a doubt","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-03-2023, 03:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T10:16:38-07:00","id":1517081,"title":"","content":"It's been so long since I read the original Get of Fenris tribebook, I forgot they ever mentioned the binding of Fenris. <br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I also wanted to reference the legend, but didn't want to make the Fenris spirit seem like some kind of chump. So in my version, after some offense Fenris intended to materialize in the Realm and really go after his enemies. And all the spirits were really alarmed at what this might do. So one spirit - I think I made it an Incarna of the Mars Celestine because Tyr/Tiwaz is a variant of the war god - offered Fenris great chiminage - his own hand - if he would refrain his fury until the Apocalypse so that the Realm would be spared devastation. And Fenrir then went into a kind of quasi-slumber - still awake enough to be contacted and do things, but much less active than other Incarna.<br /> <br /> I thought that was a good enough explanation. Players could understand how such a story would be re-interpreted, but it would not be so offensive to the Garou of the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T05:38:46-07:00","id":1517154,"title":"","content":"In Norse mythology there was another strange goddes who could be either an ally or the member of the Host<br /> Elli, the personification of old age who defeated Thor in a wrestling match. She is the embodiment of the &quot;crone&quot; and the wisdom and strength of the elderly.<br /> <br /> &quot;There is no need to make a long matter of it: that struggle went in such wise that the harder Thor strove in gripping, the faster she stood; then the old woman attempted a hold, and then Thor became totty on his feet, and their tuggings were very hard. Yet it was not long before Thor fell to his knee, on one foot.&quot;<br /> <br /> Elli basically by a touch made him weak, weakened by age...<br /> Now if this isn't Temporis and Elli wasn't a True Brujah, then I don't know what <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Sure not everybody love Temporis and the True Brujah (or similar temporal shenanigans) but Norse mythology centered and revolved around Fate, destiny, time and prophecies <br /> Even the Gods themselves are fated to die (well most of them anyhow, some destined to survive) when Ragnarok comes - an inevitable event (not unlike the Apocalyse)<br /> As I said before, in the Fenris eyes even the Ragnarok and the all-consuming flames of Surtr could be interprted as a &quot;good thing&quot;, Gaia will be clean from darkness, monsters... humans, a new age comes (or, you know the Kuei-jin/Hengeyokai 6th Age where the Demon Emperor ruled ends, and comes the 7th)<br /> So it is not that farfatch to shoehorn such an enigmatic figure like the Goddess Elli either te member of the Host/Odin's army (or followers) ... or either an enemy<br /> Even the mighty Thor, god of thunder, lord of the Stroms (Sutekh, is that you? Grandfather Thunder? Susanowo? Tyhphon) fell on his knees, defeated by old age the wisdom and strength of the elderly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T09:40:07-07:00","id":1517162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517081#post1517081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I made it an Incarna of the Mars Celestine because Tyr/Tiwaz is a variant of the war god - offered Fenris great chiminage - his own hand</div> </div> </div> </div>About Tyr... a little funny quesy-historical tidbit<br /> <br /> Snorri Sturluson, a 13th century Icelandic historian, believes Odin was a famous warrior who led his people out of Troy and into Scandinavia.<br /> His greatness was such that he ascended to the status of a god, and became worshiped as one.<br /> His myth continued to grow, especially among Germanic peoples, and he eventually usurped Tyr as the chief god, both in myth and in religious practice and worship.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T11:04:21-07:00","id":1517163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517162#post1517162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Tyr... a little funny quesy-historical tidbit<br /> <br /> Snorri Sturluson, a 13th century Icelandic historian, believes Odin was a famous warrior who led his people out of Troy and into Scandinavia.<br /> His greatness was such that he ascended to the status of a god, and became worshiped as one.<br /> His myth continued to grow, especially among Germanic peoples, and he eventually usurped Tyr as the chief god, both in myth and in religious practice and worship.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do know this, and in my chronicles this is actually true. Except that Odin did not come from Troy (around 1200 BC), but was part of the original Indo-European peoples as they were leaving the steppe and embark on the Indo-European invasions (Odin was likely part of the Yamnaya Culture peoples around 3000 BC, and he followed what would become the Germanic peoples into northern Europe). And that, of course, he was a vampire instead of just being a sorcerer.<br /> <br /> At that time, all the progenitors of the Indo-European cultures we know today had one mythology that eventually became all the different mythologies of the Greeks, Celts, Germans, Slavs, Indians, Persians, etc. that we know today. Little is known about it, but linguists and comparative mythologists have reconstructed some elements of it.<br /> <br /> Since Odin was just a neonate when the migrations began, it took him a long time before he could plausibly portray himself as an actual &quot;god&quot;. In my chronicles, this process began some time before the Romans made contact with the Germanic peoples, and was accomplished sometime around the 6th century AD. This process slowly transformed the (fictionalized) Germanic pagan religion from a more &quot;Gaian&quot; centered faith heavily influenced by the Garou (and their kinfolk) and turned into the human sacrificing religion to Odin we know from history. This &quot;corruption&quot; is one reason the Get of Fenris really hate Odin.<br /> <br /> This is just part of the background, and the details aren't very relevant to Garou PCs in any kind of modern chronicle. But this is the kind of archaeology and fitting actual myth and history to setting lore that I often do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":".  typos 07-07-2023, 02:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T11:15:55-07:00","id":1517164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517154#post1517154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said before, in the Fenris eyes even the Ragnarok and the all-consuming flames of Surtr could be interprted as a &quot;good thing&quot;, Gaia will be clean from darkness, monsters... humans, a new age comes</div> </div> </div> </div>Since there are fire spirits named the Surtur that are part of Fenris's brood in Axis Mundi, this makes a lot of sense. It's another one of those unexpected inversions of real Norse mythology. We would expect that Surtur - one of the great enemies of the gods (just like Fenris) - should be part of the Wyrm's forces, but the spirits named after him are Gaian. It just makes reconciling the mythology to Garou lore really difficult. Everyone is going to have their own interpretation, which is why I think taking &quot;inspiration&quot; from myth rather than stating clearly what is going on is a better approach. There's been some great ideas on this thread of how people have done that in their own chronicles, but they are all mutually contradictory. Which is fine, everyone will approach it in the way they like best.<br /> <br /> In terms of the outcome of the Apocalypse, I prefer the idea that the outcome is essentially unknown (which is why it is important to fight). In the early days when Garou numbers were more plentiful, the Wyld was flourishing, and the great Garou heroes lived, I like the idea that the Garou easily assumed they were going to win. The next age was going to be great and cleansed Gaia of evil. But in the modern day with their numbers reduced, various ecological damage, vampires flourishing, and Garou culture, ideals, and identity in decline, many Garou assume they are either going to lose or that the odds are stacked against them. Those that remain optimistic are seen as delusion. They fear they are going to lose and the next world to come will be everything they are struggling against. It's a cultural collapse.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T11:31:40-07:00","id":1517166,"title":"","content":"One thing I like in Werewolf are ancient artifacts and relics and the like. Since the Garou have fetishes and sometimes name them and have legendary reputations for them (primarily for klaives, but not exclusively), I think it's appropriate if their enemies do as well. And we have a rich trove of mythology to mine.<br /> <br /> While not from mythology, we already know about the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Blood-Horn\" target=\"_blank\">Blood Horn</a> from the Wolves of the Sea sourcebook. There's already been some discussion of that on this thread.<br /> <br /> In an earlier Vampire thread, I discussed the Eye of Odin as a vampire relic inspired by similar &quot;relics&quot; mentioned in the original Storytellers Guide to the Sabbat, so I won't detail it here. But here is <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1445128-vampire-relic-the-eye-of-the-all-high\">the link to the thread</a> for those interested. Instead, I'll talk about some other artifacts that the Host should have, once had, or are searching for.<br /> <br /> Another vampire relic is the Head of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%ADmir\" target=\"_blank\">Mimir</a>. In my chronicles it is the decapitated, mummified head of an ancient Malkavian vampire who once accompanied the All High before he was destroyed. The fae members of the Host believe Mimir willingly allowed himself to be sacrificed by the fae in a magical ritual in order to seal the alliance between them and the All High. That is how important Mimir viewed the alliance between the All High and House Aesin in preventing Ragnarok. The head is contained in a sack and would be easily confused with the preserved head of any bog mummy.<br /> <br /> Anyone who consults the head can evoke the memories of Mimir. The head may provide five additional dice like the Ancestors Background (difficulty 6) for any skill or language the ST sees fit for an ancient Malkavian vampire destroyed thousands of years ago to know. Because consulting the Head takes time, it is best that these additional dice are best used for Knowledges, as combat skills and the like are not a practical use of consulting the Head. The head of Mimir can also provide advice from the perspective of a Malkavian vampire who was destroyed during the Nordic Bronze Age. Occasionally, the audience will hear advice and memories from the Head so alien and bizarre that he descends into crazed fits. If a Storyteller does not want to decide what information it contains, she can have the character roll Intelligence (difficulty 9). A botch means the wearer has called up knowledge and memories he would rather not have.<br /> <br /> The Head of Mimir is currently in possession of the National Museum of Denmark where the head is simply identified as \u201cUlfeldt Man\u201d, an extremely well preserved head of a bog mummy. At some point, the vampire Brynhild will discover its location and attempt to retrieve it.<br /> <br /> I'll post some more ideas later.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T15:33:08-07:00","id":1517230,"title":"","content":"This may be a bit of a tangent, but in the brilliant book Threats, Shadowrun has an organisation called Winternight, that claims to be run by powerful shamans/wizards embodying the figures of nordic mytholoy. While the core implication is that they seek to cause ragnarok itself, I feel that a lot of the tone for the kind of work Winternight does and the large scale plans they embody could make for highly playable scenarios for Werewolf as well against Odin and his host.<br /> <br /> While they are definitely more on the antagonist than the &quot;neutral&quot; side, the tone and the idea of a controlled Ragnarok that ensures their eschatonicization and manipulating others into furthering it could work quite well for Odin's brood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T22:12:44-07:00","id":1517248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517230#post1517230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the core implication is that they seek to cause ragnarok itself, I feel that a lot of the tone for the kind of work Winternight does and the large scale plans they embody could make for highly playable scenarios for Werewolf as well against Odin and his host.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am completely unfamiliar with Shadowrun and this sourcebook, but think we should steal whatever inspiration we can. Good ideas are good ideas. Is there anything specific about Winternight you think can apply to the Host? You talk about work and specific plans of the organization that could apply to the Host, but you don't list them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T06:25:09-07:00","id":1517272,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I didn't want to go into too much detail just in case Shadowrun was not going to make the cut here. The extra time also allowed me to dig out the book and refresh myself. Essentially Threats is one of the best books for Shadowrun (and one of my favourite RPG books in general). It presents a number of antagonists and well, threats that are presented as in character conspiracy theories and or dubious accounts posted onto a Shadowrunning forum. Then these accounts are spiced up by commentary of other Shadowrunners.<br /> <br /> Winternight themselves are presented through a lens of a WMD investigator who got recruited into serving them through addiction to visions of himself as a grand \u00dcbermensch warrior and threats of blackmail against his family. The man snaps and murders his family and blows up his offices, posting his account into the forums.<br /> <br /> As presented, Winternight:<ul><li>Is a secretive cabal of evil shamans serving the destructive aspect of Raven and Wolf (Banes in WoD parlance)</li> <li>Their goal is to achieve Ragnarok at their own conditions, enabling them to ascend into full Godhood and take over the world that is to come</li> <li>Towards this goal they seek to use nuclear weapons imbued with magic or biowarfare to incite a form of Fimbulwinter and triggering Ragnarok</li> <li>They have no scruples and are willing to do anything to anyone if it furthers their goal (after all, Godhood is on the line). They will lie, cheat, infiltrate, kidnap, murder, addict people, torture people and even force their own members to do horrible things to their own families</li> <li>One of their chief tools is a special type of induced euphoric trip that convinces the user that they are the greatest and most powerful berserkers in the world, seeking glory, blood and the death of their enemies. The trip is the best feeling ever overloading their senses and adrenal system into pure ecstasy, but slowly eroding their sense of self and selfcontrol</li> <li>This makes the users willing to do anything to get more of this power (done through uploaded stimuli in Shadowrun, but I could see Dominate or Thaumaturgy being used to do this) Of course the trips are rationed by the members of Winternight to get more out of these people</li> <li>They work in secrecy, coopting or murdering anyone that finds them, using intermediaries and PC's to help them out</li> </ul>It just sprang to me last night that this spin could be used for the Brood of Wotan - eschatonic ideas to empower him and the leaders into true Godhood, and a Ragnarok on their own terms - they don't seek the Apocalypse as the Werewolves would see it, but could be collecting artifacts and weapons preparing for the ultimate rush. The fact that they manipulate and coopt humans and human organizations already stinks of Vampires and the whole &quot;drug induced berserkers addicted to more blood and glory&quot; is great fodder for mooks or servants, especially if they are fed blood as a part of their trips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T09:01:27-07:00","id":1517284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517272#post1517272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a secretive cabal of evil shamans serving the destructive aspect of Raven and Wolf (Banes in WoD parlance)</div> </div> </div> </div>To go further into this, the Ravens are usually Avengers, while the Wolves are Poisoners. Avengers are typically trying to off humanity for being a blight, while the Poisoners just want to kill shit, and don't care who, where, or how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T09:59:49-07:00","id":1517288,"title":"","content":"In Shadowrun Canon Winternight brought down the worlds permanently global matrix (internet) requiring a complete rebuild, using the J\u00f6rmungandr virus and almost succeeded in nuclear Armageddon.<br /> <br /> In WTA they are their role could be:<br /> 1. In trying to prevent Ragnarok the Host use any and all tactics, including addiction, kidnap, murder, extortion, blackmail, terror tactics, insinuation into all levels of government etc as @<b>Asmodai </b>said very vampire tactics but not friendly to the Masquerade\u200b (this would be how they clash with the Camarilla and Glasswalkers, as well as Fenris).<br /> 2. Winternight are an opposing faction (maybe even a splinter group and/or powerful Defiler Wyrm cult) that want to start Ragnarok, the Wolves or Poisoners are defilers of the land amongst other things, whilst the Ravens could be fallen Garou or Fera. They could be a twisted form of Nephandic Verbena Mage who\u2019ve collected supernatural forces of their own.<br /> Alternatively they readily mix magic and technology (a conflicting notion in Shadowrun) so could easily be renegade Technocracy or Glasswalkers.<br /> <br /> The Threats book does a great job as introducing them as a ominous dark conspiracy that appears to have eyes everywhere, with no conscience or limit to what they\u2019ll do to achieve their aims or anyone that gets in their way.<br /> <br /> As an added twist a Winternight inspired group could be masquerading as the Host if you wanted to add that layer of conspiracy.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T18:24:49-07:00","id":1517320,"title":"","content":"Shadowrun can afford to be more gonzo because the supernatural is obviously known in its setting. The WoD is &quot;supposed&quot; to have the supernatural more low key in order to preserve the idea that it is present, but hidden from most of humanity. So any idea stealing has to take that into consideration. They can act in a more direct and obvious way than the Camarilla, but if you want to keep the setting somewhat similar to the real world, you cannot go too far.<br /> <br /> I think the berserker angle has already been addressed by the idea that there is a certain kind of fomori that mirrors this. You may just need to twist some flavor text to bring more of a Winternight angle it seems to me.<br /> <br /> I do agree that in order to try to prevent Ragnarok (or gain advantage when it happens) that the Host could have no scruples and engage in a lot of things through its various camps (vampires, fae, mortal cults, etc.) Kidnapping, murder, blackmail, torture, etc. And it does somewhat fall into line in the early canon detail that Brynhild was responsible for the assassination of Swedish Prime Minister Olof Palme (although why she would do that was never explained; it was just a cheap way to attribute all sorts of mysterious events to vampires). <br /> <br /> But that is easier to say than do as an ST because we would need concrete details on specific things they'd do. Why would they kidnap or murder this person? Why would they sabotage or attack this power station or other installation? And so on? Whatever they did would need to be directly tied to preventing Ragnarok, and how would they determine that? We'd probably need some kind of &quot;Prophecies of Odin&quot; akin to the Prophecy of Phoenix that provide something actionable. They could very well be wrong in their actions (because they interpreted the prophecy wrong), but it would provide guidance to them. Another possibility is that such extremist actions is not to prevent Ragnarok, but done in retaliation for someone who defied them or prevented them from doing what they wanted (deliberately or inadvertently).<br /> <br /> I do think one way this could be translated was the Host taking a more active role in locating and obtaining occult artifacts. That is more low key than someone obtaining a nuclear weapon, and does dovetail into the idea I was just mentioning about artifacts in general. A missing bog mummy head from a Danish museum does not create the same sense of panic like one of Russia's nuclear warheads going missing. Some of these could just be drawn from a list of artifacts already associated with Odin or the Host. But others could be unrelated, but that the Host has identified. These could be things the Garou are also after - like one of the Talons of the Wyrm. Simply because the Garou has possession of Narlthus or something else does not mean the Host thinks it is in safe hands - they may want it because they think their hands are even safer!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T18:44:25-07:00","id":1517322,"title":"","content":"Looking at some of the mummies that got brewed up in our last thread, I'd be less concerned about a missing Nuke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T19:08:12-07:00","id":1517324,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, the supernatural - especially in the WoD - can be a great threat. But from the perspective of the vast majority of humanity, the supernatural does not exist. If they don't know about Bane Mummies, they have no reason to worry about them. But if they hear some previously unknown &quot;terrorist group&quot; stole a nuke, there'd be panic. But hearing some large stone meteorite from a Canadian mining site has been stolen, or some Medieval book that few people have heard from is now missing from Miskatonic University, or other innocuous sounding artifacts? Only those with knowledge of the supernatural might be concerned depending on how much they know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T19:28:29-07:00","id":1517326,"title":"","content":"I'd like to note here that Arcanus may have represented Winternight in a more open way than it is. At one point it's discovered that they had multiple nukes stored away. People didn't know they were missing who they belonged to, and even after the reports, the people who usually know this stuff (the shadowy mercs of Shadowrun) found the story preposterous and suspicious. Winternight in its riginal incarnation wasn't public, it only became public after their huge attack. Before that, they were the bogeyman and the urban legend controlling even the people that are supposed to know about them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-06T19:31:02-07:00","id":1517327,"title":"","content":"And simply because I am a bit surprised this hasn't been referenced yet, I'll share it because I think it's awesome.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9x8-1MAAB44\" data-code=\"9x8-1MAAB44\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9x8-1MAAB44/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-07T01:20:03-07:00","id":1517334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514881#post1514881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also reminds me of the different Odin\u2019s in American Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>There has been a little mention \ud83d\ude09, but seriously agreed great book and great adaptation.<br /> <br /> Provides a good example of how multiple versions of supernatural beings could exist, without just being something that\u2019s borrowed another beings name.<br /> <br /> With realms such as the Higher Umbra and Dreaming very easy to have an umbrood created as a representation of the All-high etc <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:10:43-07:00","id":1517588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517334#post1517334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There has been a little mention \ud83d\ude09, but seriously agreed great book and great adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just like the quote (I see very little in American Gods that is actually applicable to the All High, but everyone has their own inspirations). I like it because it shows he has lots of &quot;names&quot; (or titles)., and that even &quot;Odin&quot; is just one of them ( that and his other names in Germanic cultures just means something like &quot;lord of the possessed or frenzy&quot;, it is not a personal name) (and because the scene is just awesome cinematically).<br /> <br /> Anyway, here is another artifact, obviously brought from mythology.<br /> <br /> Gungnir is the spear of the All High. In myth, it was created by dwarfs and could always hit its target regardless of its wielder's skill. This spear of the All High is a powerful Fae Treasure that can slay chimerical creatures and deal aggravated damage to others. It works against the Fae just as well as cold iron. It was created by the Fae allies of the All High to cement their alliance. While elves of House Aesin originally recovered Gungnir after the burning of the temple at Uppsala, it was subsequently lost during the Shattering. House Aesin would love to recover the Treasure as it is said that without the spear, the All High will not be able to avert Ragnarok or slay the demon spirit Fenris. Unfortunately for them, they do not know its current location.<br /> <br /> If we want to use the idea that the Host is actively preparing for Ragnarok, and that the search for occult artifacts is a good way to do that (and can be a great hook for PCs), then finding this spear would be very important. It is an ancient spear from the Nordic Bronze Age, and now might only be a well preserved bronze spearhead with no shaft. Perhaps only those who can see chimerical things could recognize the spearhead for what it is. It might be forgotten in some warehouse of a museum, or perhaps part of someone's private collection. If you want to introduce it in game, it could be put up for sale in an antique gallery or shop. Perhaps with various groups becoming aware of its importance through the typical means of Gifts that provide prophetic knowledge, dream omens, and so on. Vampires, mages, Garou, and Changelings might become interested, but only the members of the Host would actually recognize it for what it really is (and know the secret means to unlock its &quot;true&quot; power, without such knowledge it might seem like a much less powerful Fae Treasure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:26:29-07:00","id":1517589,"title":"","content":"An idea that occurs to me which could provide an interesting flavor, which others have alluded to in this thread, is the idea of nuclear warfare and the like.<br /> <br /> While of course the All High has been kicked around since long before the Cold War, Sidhe like those of House Aesin returned to earth in the flat middle of those years where the specter of The Bomb must have been hanging heavy throughout the Umbra &amp; Dreaming.<br /> <br /> Even now when the fear of the Bomb is nowhere near as prevalent, I think it could provide an interesting touchstone. The idea occurs to me of having a reoccurring trend of the Host be to repurpose old bunkers and fallout shelters. This would be a neat way of combining the thematic threads of War, Apocalypse, &amp; Historical weight which lends itself well to the Host. I also think on an esoteric level, the subterranean nature of these bunkers is a nice modern vessel for the older cthonic vibrations which these sort of cultic organizations had as their bread and butter. <br /> <br /> I know for instance in my home town there are a number of older buildings that have decades old signs posted declaring them to be the locations of fallout shelters. I can\u2019t imagine that the local bank or high school checks on the Eisenhower era bunkers built below their buildings but even if they do, they may not in the WoD. The idea of a group of PCs tracking down a mysterious cult group and finding a shrine of the All-High hidden within the abandoned fallout shelter under some innocuous local institution is a striking image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:37:25-07:00","id":1517591,"title":"","content":"I also think we can use artifacts not inspired by Garou myth to be a target of the Host. After all, limiting ourselves to just those make things very predictable.<br /> <br /> I don't have a list of existing artifacts already published in the World of Darkness sourcebooks that would make a good list to pillage from. I am aware of some sources that could provoke the Host and Garou PCs into conflict. The Sept of Bygone Visions held by the Black Furies could make a tempting raiding target because of the many occult treasures housed in the Womb of the sept. We know there are some powerful Wyrm items there (including one of the Talens of the Wyrm), legendary books of white and black magic, and other occult artifacts. Hearing news of some spectacular raid on this Sept would certainly be a strong hook.<br /> <br /> There are also some published Legendary Fetishes that could make a good target. If the Host could obtain the Elder Stone (a fragment of the mythical Table Rock where the Garou first created the Litany mentioned in the 1e Storytellers Handbook), that could become an epic quest to recover it.<br /> <br /> Perhaps one reason the Odindohtter are gathering information in Russia because they want to recover Koschei's Soul Egg. Per Rage Across Russia, this a gemstone fetish prisone currently possessed by a small group of Uktena Banetenders in Siberia. This might be at the sole Uktena sept mentioned in RAR, the Sept of the Spirit Stone located in Yakutia/Sakha, or perhaps at one of the several other Uktena, but nameless, septs that the ST will need to create.<br /> <br /> If people know of other tempting targets (whether from canon or even personal invention), I think it would be beneficial for the thread. It would transform the Host from a background element into something that is more active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:39:36-07:00","id":1517592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517589#post1517589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea occurs to me of having a reoccurring trend of the Host be to repurpose old bunkers and fallout shelters. This would be a neat way of combining the thematic threads of War, Apocalypse, &amp; Historical weight which lends itself well to the Host. I also think on an esoteric level, the subterranean nature of these bunkers is a nice modern vessel for the older cthonic vibrations which these sort of cultic organizations had as their bread and butter.<br /> <br /> I know for instance in my home town there are a number of older buildings that have decades old signs posted declaring them to be the locations of fallout shelters. I can\u2019t imagine that the local bank or high school checks on the Eisenhower era bunkers built below their buildings but even if they do, they may not in the WoD. The idea of a group of PCs tracking down a mysterious cult group and finding a shrine of the All-High hidden within the abandoned fallout shelter under some innocuous local institution is a striking image.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a strong idea. And of course we could easily tie in the belief of some cultists that the legendary Fimbulwinter might be a prediction of a nuclear winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:53:58-07:00","id":1517594,"title":"","content":"I could definitely see a strain of the Host viewing the possibility of Nuclear War being a part of the accomplishment of their schemes and hopes for Ragnarok.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T13:54:07-07:00","id":1517595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517588#post1517588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it because it shows he has lots of &quot;names&quot; (or titles)., and that even &quot;Odin&quot; is just one of them ( that and his other names in Germanic cultures just means something like &quot;lord of the possessed or frenzy&quot;, it is not a personal name) (and because the scene is just awesome cinematically).</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, even his initially introducing himself to Shadow as \u2018Mr Wednesday\u2019, although I do picture the All-High as a monsterous Marvel Thor as much as I like Mr McShane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517588#post1517588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This spear of the All High is a powerful Fae Treasure that can slay chimerical creatures and deal aggravated damage to others. It works against the Fae just as well as cold iron. It was created by the Fae allies of the All High to cement their alliance. While elves of House Aesin originally recovered Gungnir after the burning of the temple at Uppsala, it was subsequently lost during the Shattering. House Aesin would love to recover the Treasure as it is said that without the spear, the All High will not be able to avert Ragnarok or slay the demon spirit Fenris. Unfortunately for them, they do not know its current location.<br /> <br /> If we want to use the idea that the Host is actively preparing for Ragnarok, and that the search for occult artifacts is a good way to do that (and can be a great hook for PCs), then finding this spear would be very important. It is an ancient spear from the Nordic Bronze Age, and now might only be a well preserved bronze spearhead with no shaft. Perhaps only those who can see chimerical things could recognize the spearhead for what it is. It might be forgotten in some warehouse of a museum, or perhaps part of someone's private collection. If you want to introduce it in game, it could be put up for sale in an antique gallery or shop. Perhaps with various groups becoming aware of its importance through the typical means of Gifts that provide prophetic knowledge, dream omens, and so on. Vampires, mages, Garou, and Changelings might become interested, but only the members of the Host would actually recognize it for what it really is (and know the secret means to unlock its &quot;true&quot; power, without such knowledge it might seem like a much less powerful Fae Treasure).</div> </div> </div> </div>This is interesting on a number of levels a treasure hunting game is a good change of pace, but with his alliance with the Aesin and the chimeric properties of the spear that suggests the All-High may have abilities similar to being Enchanted.<br /> <br /> I like that only those able to see the Chimeric or possibly the host can detect the spear, as it opens up a Fianna or Changeling angle, also possible that there are Fey factions who oppose the Host (Trolls, other Vanir) who might be working to keep the spear hidden.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-09T15:21:14-07:00","id":1517601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517589#post1517589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even now when the fear of the Bomb is nowhere near as prevalent, I think it could provide an interesting touchstone. The idea occurs to me of having a reoccurring trend of the Host be to repurpose old bunkers and fallout shelters. This would be a neat way of combining the thematic threads of War, Apocalypse, &amp; Historical weight which lends itself well to the Host. I also think on an esoteric level, the subterranean nature of these bunkers is a nice modern vessel for the older cthonic vibrations which these sort of cultic organizations had as their bread and butter.<br /> <br /> I know for instance in my home town there are a number of older buildings that have decades old signs posted declaring them to be the locations of fallout shelters. I can\u2019t imagine that the local bank or high school checks on the Eisenhower era bunkers built below their buildings but even if they do, they may not in the WoD. The idea of a group of PCs tracking down a mysterious cult group and finding a shrine of the All-High hidden within the abandoned fallout shelter under some innocuous local institution is a striking image.</div> </div> </div> </div>Norway, Sweden and Finland have incredible networks of underground tunnels,bases and weapon storages. Some of these sites are still militarily active, others could just be sealed away until needed - what could the Host stock with there and how great would a fully armed fortress untouched by sunlight be to them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517588#post1517588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we want to use the idea that the Host is actively preparing for Ragnarok, and that the search for occult artifacts is a good way to do that (and can be a great hook for PCs), then finding this spear would be very important. It is an ancient spear from the Nordic Bronze Age, and now might only be a well preserved bronze spearhead with no shaft. Perhaps only those who can see chimerical things could recognize the spearhead for what it is. It might be forgotten in some warehouse of a museum, or perhaps part of someone's private collection. If you want to introduce it in game, it could be put up for sale in an antique gallery or shop. Perhaps with various groups becoming aware of its importance through the typical means of Gifts that provide prophetic knowledge, dream omens, and so on. Vampires, mages, Garou, and Changelings might become interested, but only the members of the Host would actually recognize it for what it really is (and know the secret means to unlock its &quot;true&quot; power, without such knowledge it might seem like a much less powerful Fae Treasure).</div> </div> </div> </div>Tying in with the world changing and the ecological bent of Werewolf, maybe it has just thawed from a glacier or an iceberg, and was rather publically found and lampoond as masterwork of the bronze age. Now the archeologists are beset with the Fae that seek their ownership, the host that seeks to bring their master his weapon and the garou who believe only Gungnir can strike down the All High forever more?<br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-10T18:04:36-07:00","id":1517665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517591#post1517591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have a list of existing artifacts already published in the World of Darkness sourcebooks that would make a good list to pillage from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am quoting myself only because my post was caught in the spam net for a while, and people have likely missed it.<br /> <br /> Anyway besides the items or places mentioned in that original post, I've also found a list of vampire artifacts on the White Wolf Wiki located <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Artifact_(VTM)?so=search\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. Some of the more powerful, and unique, items might be sough by the Host in preparations for Ragnarok. The Lamp of Constantine or Sword of Nul (among others) might be useful to have when Ragnarok happens, or just to keep out of the hands of their enemies. Again, these could be good &quot;quest&quot; items that become a hook for Garou PCs.<br /> <br /> Less powerful, but more ubiquitous, &quot;artifacts&quot; might be a nice way to distinguish the Host and the assets it controls from other factions. Maybe they are the ones who have access to the most extant Giant's Blood relics (from the first Sabbat Players Guide)? That might encourage the Sabbat or Tremere to go after them. Maybe they know the secret of the Powder of Rigidity (from the first Storyteller's Handbook) or the Berserker Fangs (from the 2e Vampire Players Guide)?<br /> <br /> While I normally shoo away from having &quot;magic items&quot; in my Vampire games, they can be used appropriately if judiciously. But I think its appropriate for a group like the Host to have access to magic long since forgotten. They may not be able to make these things themselves anymore, but they could know where some of the last remaining caches are. Plus, if individual vampires of the Host are to battle a pack of Garou PCs, they are going to need all the help they can get. Or provide a good way to justify one of the Valkyries to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T23:59:40-07:00","id":1517741,"title":"","content":"There is a wyldcard of a vampire in the area, if you want to add some &quot;spice&quot; to the mix<br /> Louhi is a queen witch in Finnish mythology and the mythology of Lapland.<br /> In WoD?<br /> Louhi is a Malkavian methuselah who serves the Lasombra Antediluvian. She is one of the most talented thaumaturges of the World of Darkness. She was Embraced by Lerterimas, a childe of Malkav, in Finland during the first century.<br /> She is an old witch, with the smell of several alchemical experiments and she always carries a black staff inscribed with various runes. Her thaumaturgical powers rival even those of the most powerful Tremere elders with her own revenant family that serves her - the Keskinen.<br /> Now how this vampire comes to the picture you may ask?<br /> Simple!<br /> Her goal is non less than... bloat out the Sun and cover the Earth in total darkness (eternal Winter adn cold eg. Fimbulvetr - the rpelude to the Ragnarok) <br /> <br /> oh, and Werewolf Players Guide, p. 76 mentioned as having a 'rumored' alliance with the Society of Nidhogg<br /> <br /> True, the Society of Nidhogg is a Shadow Lord camp, but hey, In scandiavian mythology N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr is a dragon who gnaws at a root of the world tree, we all know that, but interestingly an &quot;evil&quot; that will survive Ragnarok itself and will be there in the new world, he will be among those to survive the fire and flood, and shall continue to nom tasty dead things for eternity...<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T09:06:08-07:00","id":1517788,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of evil Vampire wizards that want to end the world in this way or that :P<br /> Endless source of targets for the Fera!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:10:12-07:00","id":1517811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517741#post1517741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a wyldcard of a vampire in the area, if you want to add some &quot;spice&quot; to the mix<br /> Louhi is a queen witch in Finnish mythology and the mythology of Lapland.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, I mentioned this very briefly in discussion about the Host's relationship with the Sabbat <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1514387#post1514387\">here</a>, since the All High would be likely to oppose her since the blotting out of the sun is one of the signs of Ragnarok. These two methusalehs must hate each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1517741#post1517741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, and Werewolf Players Guide, p. 76 mentioned as having a 'rumored' alliance with the Society of Nidhogg<br /> <br /> True, the Society of Nidhogg is a Shadow Lord camp, but hey, In scandiavian mythology N\u00ed\u00f0h\u00f6ggr is a dragon who gnaws at a root of the world tree, we all know that, but interestingly an &quot;evil&quot; that will survive Ragnarok itself and will be there in the new world, he will be among those to survive the fire and flood, and shall continue to nom tasty dead things for eternity...\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't know there was a connection between Louhi and this Shadow Lords camp.<br /> <br /> It might be an interesting twist for the pack of Garou PCs to somehow ally with Odin's Host in order to fight another ancient vampire and a pack of Shadow Lords in this camp. It complicates a lot of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T22:27:25-07:00","id":1518410,"title":"","content":"I think now is a good time to go over what spirits might be allied to the Host. Spirits and the spirit world are an important part of Werewolf, and they would be an important part of Odin's Host. The All High made various pacts with spirits, and they constitute a small brood available to the sorcerers of the Host. These spirits can be seen as a subset of normal spirits of their type, as they are functionally the same as their kind but have extensive chiminage relationships with the All High and the Host. These includes outright Banes, unassociated spirits, and Gaian spirits that have various levels of corruption.<br /> <br /> The sorcerers of the Host come from all types of members - vampire blood sorcerers, humans, black magicians of the Fae, and even some of the allied Changing Breeds - who know the appropriate paths of spirit sorcery. Below are examples of some spirits known to sorcerers of the Host, but the spirits capable of being summoned by them are not limited to them.<br /> <br /> Technically, this is not a spirit brood because Odin is not an Incarna and cannot serve the same kind of protective role the Icarna can perform. But the Host does have a body of spiritual knowledge that allows them to summon some groups of dependable spirits based on prior and ongoing chiminage.<br /> <br /> I'll start first with some typical spirits known to the Garou.<br /> <br /> <b>Raven</b><br /> <br /> There are many kinds of raven spirits existing in multiple spirit broods. It seems it is just the nature of these kinds of spirits that they, as a whole, have chosen many masters. A number of raven spirits have simply chosen to help the followers of the All High. The sorcerers of the Host use them mostly as spies and messengers. A smaller subset of these spirits are heavily Wyrm tainted, and it is these - and only these - that assist the Valravn and find the location of additional spirit eggs. I would use the same mechanics as normal Raven spirits, and just give them some different flavor text.<br /> <br /> <b>Wild Hunt</b><br /> <br /> The All High also managed to seduce a small number of spirits associated with the Wild Hunt, something which infuriates the Fianna. The sorcerers of the Host typically only summon these Wild Hunt spirits when they need to deal with a martial threat in the Umbra. They can also summon them to manifest in the physical realm to kill someone, but can only do so between the autumn and spring equinoxes, and only at night or if stormclouds blot out the sun. These limitations are a result of the chiminage the All High needed to perform in order to seduce these spirits. Again, the spirit mechanics are the same, but use different flavor text. The Huntsman himself appears much like the All High while his Hounds appear more like wolves.<br /> <br /> <b>European Wildcat</b><br /> <br /> The Ceilican sorcerers and their mortal friends are the ones most likely to deal with the Wildcat spirit, as he is their patron. This spirit is unlikely to assist more obvious Wyrm creatures unless it suits the individual spirits\u2019 own purposes. Unlike the other spirits here, these European Wildcat spirits are not corrupted and are still Gaian. They only deal with the Ceilican and not others in the Host.<br /> <br /> <b>Bat</b><br /> <br /> Bat spirits are heavily divided due to the madness of their Incarna after the destruction of the Cazamotz. Many serve the Wyrm while others remain loyal to Gaia. As a result, the All High has managed to secure the services of many bat spirits. While mortals and fae make much greater use of raven spirits, vampire sorcerers have found bat to be very useful, especially for exploring underground caves that provide shelter from sunlight (and potential enemies). Bat is also a possible totem for the Ulfhednar Skin Dancers.<br /> <br /> <b>Carrion Bird</b><br /> <br /> Originally a spirt associated with the totem of the White Howlers, it has fallen into disfavor since that tribe\u2019s fall but is not explicitly a Wyrm totem. Long neglected by the Garou in the centuries since, the spirit is known to help a variety of Garou who seek his help. This spirit is petitioned most by the Ulfhednar, but assists others in the Host as well. The Carrion Bird spirits are not exactly corrupt or Wyrm tainted, but are of dubious nature and desperate for any form of chiminage and support. If they cannot get it from the Garou, then the Host will work fine.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T22:30:13-07:00","id":1518411,"title":"","content":"Next are more typical Banes and corrupted spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Minotaur (Grendel/Grinder)</b><br /> <br /> The Minotaur, known to the Host as the Grinder (or Grendel), is the patron of the Ulfhednar skin dancers. The Grinder is best seen as an Aspect of Minotaur that has a pact with the All High.<br /> <br /> <b>Scrags</b><br /> <br /> Many Scrags have relations with the Host of the All High. Although Banes are servants of the Wyrm, the All High considers Scrags as mere tools, lacking the wit and will to oppose him. Like fire, Scrags can be a dangerous tool, but the followers of the All High believe they know enough precautions to deal with them successfully.<br /> <br /> <b>Scryers</b><br /> <br /> The Host considers the Banes known as Scryers to be similar to Scrags. Scryers are useful tools they can obtain from their enemy. Useful, but weak, properly trained sorcerers can easily impose their will, and the Host has access to many Scryers.<br /> <br /> <b>Bitter Rages</b><br /> <br /> A powerful Bane, the Host consider Bitter Rages very dangerous and unpreditable, but sometimes it is necessary to use them when a particularly powerful pack or larger group of Garou are attacking them. Only the most wise and powerful sorcerers of the Host would ever seek to make use of these Banes.<br /> <br /> <b>Thunraz</b><br /> <br /> These are storm spirits under the Incarna Typhon written in the Rage Across Russia sourcebook. Odin needs his own storm god ally, and the description of Typhon in Rage Across Russia provides a good reason for it. Werewolf gave us two different descriptions of Typhon - the villainous spirit in Rage Across Russia, and the Typhon written in the revised Shadowlords Tribebook where no mention of his villainy was present. It is not clear if this was an outright retcon, or if Typhon\u2019s betrayal of Thunder was not mentioned because of the player oriented nature of the tribebook. I suspect it was the former. If you want both kinds of Typhon spirit, I\u2019d just make them two different spirits and rename the one in Rage Across Russia and move on. (I think the Typhon described in the Freak Legion sourcebook is an entirely different spirit, much more clearly aligned with the Wyrm. It's a shame that the game misused this spirit's name so many times. It just creates confusion.) While the \u201cThunraz\u201d Incarna himself may be Typhon, I would use a variation of the Sturms in Axis Mundi as the actual spirits of this description that would be summonable by the Host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-20T22:34:31-07:00","id":1518412,"title":"","content":"Lastly I'll discuss some &quot;fairy spirits&quot;. There are some \u201cfairy spirits\u201d in Rage Across Russia. The distinction between fairies and spirits is not very clear in folklore, and in much early WoD the two are not clearly divided either. A common translation of fae creatures in Werewolf is to portray them as spirits anyway, even if they are technically chimera. If I had to completely reconcile the two, I would say they are certain \u201cspirit masters\u201d of an area with a Charm that allows them to manifest in Chimerical reality (the Dreaming) as well. That way I can eat my cake and have it too - both spirit and chimera.<br /> <br /> I would make them generic or adapt them for the Scandinavia locale. The Host would have access to these spirits because of Odin's alliance with members of the Shadow Court of House Aesin.<br /> \u200b<br /> Here are some such spirits mentioned in Rage Across Russia that I\u2019d use for the Host as well. If you don\u2019t like the explicit Russian names, it\u2019d be fairly easy to rename them as something more generic. Here are the ones I think are most appropriate as allies for the Host.<br /> <br /> <b>Bolotnyi </b>- \u201cspirit master\u201d of the swamps and often lives in the taiga<br /> <br /> <b>Leshii</b> - spirit master of the forest<br /> <br /> <b>Morozhki</b> - Frost Demons that are often, but not always, Wyrm tainted<br /> <br /> <b>Rusalka</b> - \u201cghosts\u201d of drowned maidens. The majority of them are creatures of the Wyrm. I would say instead of being ghosts, they are spirits that represent the danger of drowning -perhaps Wyrm corrupted lake and river spirits. Perhaps they are created only after a young girl drowns in the place, and the spirit gains in power for each additional drowning that happens<br /> <br /> <b>Vodianoi </b>- foul tempered water shpirits often tainted by the Wyrm, and capable of shapechangers In actual myth they are water spirits similar to Nixies, but often dangerous and unattractive looking. they are often the husbands of rusalka. perhaps if the vodianoi become wyrm tainted, they are given a wife by the Wyrm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T08:49:50-07:00","id":1518431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518410#post1518410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think now is a good time to go over what spirits might be allied to the Host. Spirits and the spirit world are an important part of Werewolf, and they would be an important part of Odin's Host. The All High made various pacts with spirits, and they constitute a small brood available to the sorcerers of the Host. These spirits can be seen as a subset of normal spirits of their type, as they are functionally the same as their kind but have extensive chiminage relationships with the All High and the Host. These includes outright Banes, unassociated spirits, and Gaian spirits that have various levels of corruption.<br /> <br /> The sorcerers of the Host come from all types of members - vampire blood sorcerers, humans, black magicians of the Fae, and even some of the allied Changing Breeds - who know the appropriate paths of spirit sorcery. Below are examples of some spirits known to sorcerers of the Host, but the spirits capable of being summoned by them are not limited to them.<br /> <br /> Technically, this is not a spirit brood because Odin is not an Incarna and cannot serve the same kind of protective role the Icarna can perform. But the Host does have a body of spiritual knowledge that allows them to summon some groups of dependable spirits based on prior and ongoing chiminage.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518410#post1518410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thunraz</b><br /> These are storm spirits under the Incarna Typhon written in the Rage Across Russia sourcebook. Odin needs his own storm god ally, and the description of Typhon in Rage Across Russia provides a good reason for it. Werewolf gave us two different descriptions of Typhon - the villainous spirit in Rage Across Russia, and the Typhon written in the revised Shadowlords Tribebook where no mention of his villainy was present. It is not clear if this was an outright retcon, or if Typhon\u2019s betrayal of Thunder was not mentioned because of the player oriented nature of the tribebook. I suspect it was the former. If you want both kinds of Typhon spirit, I\u2019d just make them two different spirits and rename the one in Rage Across Russia and move on. (I think the Typhon described in the Freak Legion sourcebook is an entirely different spirit, much more clearly aligned with the Wyrm. It's a shame that the game misused this spirit's name so many times. It just creates confusion.) While the \u201cThunraz\u201d Incarna himself may be Typhon, I would use a variation of the Sturms in Axis Mundi as the actual spirits of this description that would be summonable by the Host.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Think this draws heavily on previous ideas on this Thread, in the Odin was a powerful magician or even inhuman before his embrace, alive when cannonically the gauntlet was a lot thinner, so his command of spirits, knowledge of the Umbra and alliances are signficantly greater than most Kindred of even similar age. (one idea has been he's even in torpor in one of the Umbras).<br /> <br /> So on a grand storytelling perspective why has he amassed such a force and continued through his Host (whilst in Torpor), is it simply to seize Scandanavia ala Baga Yaga, that could be his first objective but that will hardly prevent Fimbulwinter and is certain to provoke a response that could lead to his destruction.<br /> One of his main aims is to prevent his own destruction so has he got grander aspirations on the umbral side to assure this, is it to elevate an allied spirit to Greater Incarna status thus providing himself with a level of protection from the Garou, Camarilla and Mage factions.<br /> <br /> Is Lourhi his major concern as an almost direct manifestation of Fimbulwinter (now that The Hag is gone), if she being one if not the most powerful thaumaturgists on Earth is seeking to achieve the very thing he seeks to prevent is he amassing the magical and spirit contingent to counter her, conceivably given her age and power the Society of Nidhogg aren't her only allies.<br /> <br /> One thing that does seem to be clear is that there are definitely Methuselah generation kindred that are not just Wyrm creatures by mere virtue of undeath or humanity loss, the likes of Baga Yaga, Zettler, Lourhi appear to be deliberate and willing disciples going by their actions, if the All High is looking to stop one of them he needs some serious spirit backup as Lourhi's potentially comes straight from the Abyss or even Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Of course if the All High is looking to elevate his own Totem or Umbral God such as Typhon, Totems and greater of Gaian Garou will direct their packs attentions to prevent this whilst Wyrm totems may want to see this come to pass or they themselves prevent it, so depending on the the Hosts biggest opponent would see them using a lot of spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518410#post1518410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly I'll discuss some &quot;fairy spirits&quot;. There are some \u201cfairy spirits\u201d in Rage Across Russia. The distinction between fairies and spirits is not very clear in folklore, and in much early WoD the two are not clearly divided either. A common translation of fae creatures in Werewolf is to portray them as spirits anyway, even if they are technically chimera. If I had to completely reconcile the two, I would say they are certain \u201cspirit masters\u201d of an area with a Charm that allows them to manifest in Chimerical reality (the Dreaming) as well. That way I can eat my cake and have it too - both spirit and chimera.<br /> <br /> I would make them generic or adapt them for the Scandinavia locale. The Host would have access to these spirits because of Odin's alliance with members of the Shadow Court of House Aesin.<br /> \u200b<br /> Here are some such spirits mentioned in Rage Across Russia that I\u2019d use for the Host as well. If you don\u2019t like the explicit Russian names, it\u2019d be fairly easy to rename them as something more generic. Here are the ones I think are most appropriate as allies for the Host.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> This is one of the fun bits of there being areas of contradiction in the WOD versions having cake and eating it - we have Spirits with the Chimeric Cloak Charm which does as you've described means they have dual forms, I see this as ancient nature spirits making alliances with the elder fae and some dream and nightmare spirits being an obvious dual natured creature.<br /> <br /> Plus it fits really well with the Fianna, it makes sense for some of Stags children to be spirits of both given the Totems fondness for the Fey.<br /> <br /> I think this is fitting in that you would have Wyrm tainted nightmares birthing Chimeric Banes and the fact that the Dreaming does interact with areas of the Umbra via the Paths so spirits frequenting these paths would conceivably have the ability to enter both realms, I can also see the Ghille Dhu (or their Vaesen Kin) and Nunnehi interacting with nature spirits as well as Chimera.<br /> <br /> In our cmapign we also have Hobgoblins from CTL (as the Hedge is a boundary between the MIddle Dreaming and Fae Kingdoms) which are full hybrids both Umbral and Chimeric spirits due to the Hedge being connected to all of the Umbras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T12:57:14-07:00","id":1518445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518431#post1518431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on a grand storytelling perspective why has he amassed such a force and continued through his Host (whilst in Torpor), is it simply to seize Scandanavia ala Baga Yaga, that could be his first objective but that will hardly prevent Fimbulwinter and is certain to provoke a response that could lead to his destruction.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my imagination, the purpose of the Host is not to &quot;seize&quot; Scandinavia. Yeah, they want a safe haven and the Valkyries are encouraging the Anarchs and killing some Camarilla vampires, but I don't think they need or want anything like a physical territory. They just need enough influence to make sure their members are left alone so they can do what they want. I know some earlier depictions of the Valkyrie implied they somehow wanted to return Scandinavia to its form back in the Viking Age, but that always seemed ridiculously stupid to me. How exactly was this going to be accomplished? So while I want the Host to have similarities to Baba Yaga building her armies, I do want it done in a less gonzo way. That's my preference at least.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, if we go the Snorri Sturlson route, Odin likely originally was from the Eurasian steppes somewhat close by the Don River. And the Norse colonized a lot of other lands outside Scandinavia - the British Isles, Normandy, and Russia. And we know the Valkyries began to recruit in places like Germany. So I dislike the idea of limiting the Host to just Scandinavia. They are active in a lot of Europe and probably elsewhere as well. In fact, I think it might be interesting to do things like make some rural part of Normandy or Minnesota a stronghold and hotbed of activity for the Host, or some other place not obviously connected to Odin.<br /> <br /> I do think that once Ragnarok begins that maybe one of the steps at that point is to turn some kind of territory into some fortress, but that would not be a first step. It is a contingency plan in case their attempts at preventing Ragnarok fails.<br /> <br /> So what would be their goals from a Storytelling perspective? What should the ST be having them do? STs need something actionable. You gave some good ideas. Below are some initial ideas of my own, but hoping to hear the ideas of others too.<br /> <br /> 1) Deprive their enemy Fenris of his weapons on Earth - attack caerns and packs of the Get of Fenris intelligently and in a way to minimize their own casualties. That's obviously something obvious to do for a Werewolf chronicle. The problem is figuring out how to do it in a way that makes sense. Maybe targeted assassination of lone Get of Fenris whenever they get away from their packs or caerns. We could build a situation like Grendel picking off Hrothgar's men at Heorot. This is not a conquest. But a long term raiding and killing taken place over long decades, and changing the target locations in order to minimize the Garou ability to respond meaningfully. The PCs could thus be introduced into a general situation where this is happening, but the local Garou don't know who their enemy is or how it is being done.<br /> <br /> 2) Recover useful magical artifacts for their use in either preventing Ragnarok or to use during it.<br /> <br /> 3) Eliminate obvious enemies who are forwarding Ragnarok according to the internal prophecies and information the Host has. I would make the vampire Louhi one of these targets. I would also include plenty of non-vampire targets. This could include Talons of the Wyrm, certain monsters, key members of the Black Spiral Dancers, certain heads of PENTEX, leaders of certain Wyrm cutls. Maybe heads of Heretic cults in the underworld allied to the Far Shore where Naglfar is being built (whatever that may mean in the context of Wraith). Groups like the Orphic Circle. There are wide variety of targets an ST could pick for local members of the Host. And an ST may not even do this to concentrate on the Host, but simply use the Host as a means to introduce other elements to the PCs in their a local chronicle.<br /> <br /> 4) Destabilize the existing vampire domains of Scandinavia (both Camarilla and Sabbat) and recruit more members. This is not exactly conquest, but to create the conditions of dominance and to achieve a safe zone. This could also be done in other areas favorable to the Host. If Baba Yaga was able to devastate enough of Russia's vampires before her own destruction, maybe that gives the Host some opportunities there that they would not have in Scandinavia. A natural advantage of the Gangrel is their mobility - they should use that to their advantage to hit and run, gradually weakening their (real or potential) enemies until they can subborn them and convert them to (perhaps unwilling) allies.<br /> <br /> 5) Establish safe zones throughout the world that the Host can flee to to &quot;ride out&quot; certain stages of the Apocalypse as needed. Why not have some valley in the Rocky Mountains that could be hardened by some survivalist group? Or some remote location in the Canadian wilderness? That may mean attacking any nearby Garou, or scouting the wilderness to find places where the Garou do not dwell or dwell in low numbers.<br /> <br /> 6) Gather as much information as possible that may be relavant to Ragnarok. Develop spirit allies through chiminage, have agents join Gehenna cults in the Camarilla, ask their fae allies to explore parts of the Dreaming. Maybe even build an information network through the very few Garou allies they may have cultivated as a result of their anti-Ragnarok stance. That could be started by PCs overhearing a conversation with some other Garou NPC and eventually investigate and figure out what is going on.<br /> <br /> 7) Try to divine the resting place of the All High in torpor and awaken him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518431#post1518431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one of the fun bits of there being areas of contradiction in the WOD versions having cake and eating it - we have Spirits with the Chimeric Cloak Charm which does as you've described means they have dual forms, I see this as ancient nature spirits making alliances with the elder fae and some dream and nightmare spirits being an obvious dual natured creature.<br /> <br /> Plus it fits really well with the Fianna, it makes sense for some of Stags children to be spirits of both given the Totems fondness for the Fey.<br /> <br /> I think this is fitting in that you would have Wyrm tainted nightmares birthing Chimeric Banes and the fact that the Dreaming does interact with areas of the Umbra via the Paths so spirits frequenting these paths would conceivably have the ability to enter both realms, I can also see the Ghille Dhu (or their Vaesen Kin) and Nunnehi interacting with nature spirits as well as Chimera.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was not aware of the Chimeric Cloak charm. Thanks for citing it. Where is that mentioned?<br /> <br /> In Axis Mundi, we learn that Stag also has an ancient alliance with Oak. And oak trees are heavily associated with fairies as well. I would put a lot of these &quot;spirit masters&quot; of the land spirits as part of Oak's brood just to make them a little but different from Stag's brood.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Wyrm minions birthing Chimerical terrors or similar Banes that can manifest in the Dreaming. Maybe certain kinds of fomori or monsters. That would help motivate some crossover if that if what you want. Good for packs of Stags.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T13:55:15-07:00","id":1518451,"title":"","content":"This may be a thought connected to the Safe Zone idea but something I also imagine the Host may be doing which could serve as ST fuel is a type of \u201crecruitment\u201d.<br /> <br /> Now I don\u2019t think the Host is exactly handing out pamphlets but I do imagine that the sorcerers and spirit cults (not to mention the Awakened) would be trying to induct new members.<br /> <br /> What I imagine is something like a Germanic/Nordic True Detective scenario. The Host is set up somewhere and one of its goals is to draw potential members. Perhaps allied spirits make contact with would-be occultists and draw them near. Perhaps the Host kidnaps youth (particularly of certain bloodlines) and puts them through preparatory rites to enter the Cult of Wotan - the goal being to create powerful sorcerers and/or spirit-ridden berserkers but even with the failures providing a fodder of acolytes and lesser spirit-ridden to be used as pawns.<br /> <br /> I could see one of the vectors of the Hosts activity in an area, aside from targeting the Fenrir or archaeological work, being they\u2019re trying to produce the right sort of conditions to add to their own ranks.<br /> <br /> (Related to this was a realization while reading this that in many ways this interpretation of the All High is not too dissimilar to some interpretations of Set on this forum - namely the notion that Set, potential Typhonic corruption aside, is/was trying to overcome the Wyrm and become a Gnostic Overlord rather then either becoming a powerful Wyrm tool or becoming one with the Wyrm itself if that was Typhon\u2019s goal).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T15:37:07-07:00","id":1518456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518445#post1518445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was not aware of the Chimeric Cloak charm. Thanks for citing it. Where is that mentioned?</div> </div> </div> </div>I should have said Homebrew (sadly W20/C20 didn\u2019t make those leaps) we use a version of the Materialise Charm (or equivalent Rede), for either High Umbra (Dream zones), Middle or Dark.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518445#post1518445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Axis Mundi, we learn that Stag also has an ancient alliance with Oak. And oak trees are heavily associated with fairies as well. I would put a lot of these &quot;spirit masters&quot; of the land spirits as part of Oak's brood just to make them a little but different from Stag's brood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also has good links in the Americas with Oak being one of the Nunnehi Totems, personally I like plant totems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518445#post1518445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of Wyrm minions birthing Chimerical terrors or similar Banes that can manifest in the Dreaming. Maybe certain kinds of fomori or monsters. That would help motivate some crossover if that if what you want. Good for packs of Stags.</div> </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s lots of potential, in a crossover game the Wyrm or Elder Darks corruption would definitely be felt in the Dreaming as well as Umbra, but also places of death etc<br /> <br /> Its created some interesting situations, but works the other way the advantage of it being only certain beings with a charm or rede can interact with both, most stick to their lanes and can\u2019t see the other.<br /> <br /> Our Fey Mage (Dreaming minor sphere and Spirit One) was watching a monkey spirit to see if it interacted with some chimeric spidersweb it had no awareness but did unconsciously step around them.<br /> <br /> On another occasion he encountered some graveyard spirits that seemed to interact with both Umbra and Dreaming, so it adds to the mystery.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T23:06:51-07:00","id":1518680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518451#post1518451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I imagine is something like a Germanic/Nordic True Detective scenario. The Host is set up somewhere and one of its goals is to draw potential members. Perhaps allied spirits make contact with would-be occultists and draw them near. Perhaps the Host kidnaps youth (particularly of certain bloodlines) and puts them through preparatory rites to enter the Cult of Wotan - the goal being to create powerful sorcerers and/or spirit-ridden berserkers but even with the failures providing a fodder of acolytes and lesser spirit-ridden to be used as pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that idea. Building up from a mortal perspective helps ground a lot of ideas. Because anytime you approach things from a purely supernatural angle, it can tend more towards fantasy than a more grounded reality which I think the WoD needs/<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518451#post1518451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Related to this was a realization while reading this that in many ways this interpretation of the All High is not too dissimilar to some interpretations of Set on this forum - namely the notion that Set, potential Typhonic corruption aside, is/was trying to overcome the Wyrm and become a Gnostic Overlord rather then either becoming a powerful Wyrm tool or becoming one with the Wyrm itself if that was Typhon\u2019s goal).</div> </div> </div> </div>I heavily dislike the Revised era depiction of the Setites because it is in complete opposition to their role in 1e/2e. It is just a different clan entirely. If you prefer that, OK. But it is a huge retcon.<br /> <br /> However, I think that angle is perfectly fine for the All High. One, we know very little about the All High so there's no contradiction to established lore. And two, if you want to go that route, you have a very strong differentiation from all other enemies of the Garou. If you go with the idea that the All High is figuring out how the become a &quot;god&quot;, then it presents a challenge to the PCs - how do we prevent our enemy from becoming a god? There's a lot of spiritual speculation that goes with that, but for an ST interested in that subject, it can be drive a lot of interesting scenes for Theurges and Galliards.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-23T23:11:28-07:00","id":1518681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518456#post1518456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s lots of potential, in a crossover game the Wyrm or Elder Darks corruption would definitely be felt in the Dreaming as well as Umbra, but also places of death etc\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it would be great if we had some explicit Elder Darks that could also be marked as Wyrm antagonists with common enemies and opponents.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1756\" data-vbnamecard=\"1756\">MythAdvocate</a> had <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1309473-fomorian-dreams-and-stranger-things\">a thread in Changeling that discussed some of this</a>. I think we could use more of that. It would certainly provide Werewolf with some much needed diversity of Wyrm opponents, especially if one is running a Dark Ages or other historical chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T05:05:38-07:00","id":1518693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518681#post1518681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would be great if we had some explicit Elder Darks that could also be marked as Wyrm antagonists with common enemies and opponents.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1756_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1756\" data-vbnamecard=\"1756\">MythAdvocate</a> had <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1309473-fomorian-dreams-and-stranger-things\">a thread in Changeling that discussed some of this</a>. I think we could use more of that. It would certainly provide Werewolf with some much needed diversity of Wyrm opponents, especially if one is running a Dark Ages or other historical chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is an excellent thread (book marked) in terms of antagonists purely from the thread Crom Cruach and The White Court look suspiciously like a manifestation of the Fimbulwinter, particularly the <b>Ke'let</b>\u200b which sound suspiciously like something from Wendigos brood.<br /> <br /> That leads to some interesting possibilities in the US where the Walkyri and their fey allies are working against creatures resembling the hunger spirits brood, the Fuath look to be a good opponent for both the Host and Wendigo.<br /> <br /> I think from the list Alcyoneus and Crom sound like Wyrm Maeljin manifest in the Dreaming, whilst I'd have the the likes of Dagon and the Dark Mother as being Outer beings from the Deep Umbra, like you I like there to be a range of opponents for the Garou/Changelings and not just from the wyrm.<br /> <br /> For less monsterous Elder Dark, Hecate (Black Court) and the Crimson King (Red Court) springs to mind (the Hell Boy and Baltimore versions).<br /> <br /> I like the Formori crossovers (the Hollowmen), also brings to mind there could be forms of Enticer that are like Elder Dark versions of Sidhe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T05:24:11-07:00","id":1518694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518451#post1518451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I imagine is something like a Germanic/Nordic True Detective scenario. The Host is set up somewhere and one of its goals is to draw potential members. Perhaps allied spirits make contact with would-be occultists and draw them near. Perhaps the Host kidnaps youth (particularly of certain bloodlines) and puts them through preparatory rites to enter the Cult of Wotan - the goal being to create powerful sorcerers and/or spirit-ridden berserkers but even with the failures providing a fodder of acolytes and lesser spirit-ridden to be used as pawns.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518680#post1518680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like that idea. Building up from a mortal perspective helps ground a lot of ideas. Because anytime you approach things from a purely supernatural angle, it can tend more towards fantasy than a more grounded reality which I think the WoD needs/</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this adds a welcome tone to WTA, my group like investigatory games (from their COC days) so often keep their changer natures hidden until needed or forced, investigating cults is a great conspiracy theme, plus there are some creative powers that mortal assailants can have to keep changers at bay, plus theres the threat of the breaking the Veil.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518680#post1518680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I think that angle is perfectly fine for the All High. One, we know very little about the All High so there's no contradiction to established lore. And two, if you want to go that route, you have a very strong differentiation from all other enemies of the Garou. If you go with the idea that the All High is figuring out how the become a &quot;god&quot;, then it presents a challenge to the PCs - how do we prevent our enemy from becoming a god? There's a lot of spiritual speculation that goes with that, but for an ST interested in that subject, it can be drive a lot of interesting scenes for Theurges and Galliards.</div> </div> </div> </div>One idea from earlier in the thread is that the All High is actually in Torpor in the umbra, perhaps thats not by choice but by banishment, one of his enemies cast him into the Shadowlands etc, the Walkyri struggle to find him as he's not on material Earth, maybe once again hung on the malfean tree.<br /> <br /> Now the Host may be unaware so contiue to search everywhere or perhaps their sorcerors and fey allies have worked it out, hence the search for ancient artefacts, rituals and crucially the right place to bring him back, on a conspiracy basis this could lead to all sorts of cult activity (and investigations) as they are trying to complete all of this without their enemies (including the Get) realising.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T10:23:49-07:00","id":1518707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518694#post1518694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One idea from earlier in the thread is that the All High is actually in Torpor in the umbra, perhaps thats not by choice but by banishment, one of his enemies cast him into the Shadowlands etc, the Walkyri struggle to find him as he's not on material Earth, maybe once again hung on the malfean tree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an intriguing idea that I must have missed earlier. If Enoch in the underworld has slumbering ancient vampires in torpor, then Odin (or other vampires) might be in a similar position.<br /> <br /> It does make for an interesting scenario as the Valkyrie cannot find him. And perhaps one element of the Host's early activities in a chronicle is getting the means to figure that out. Then if they do, then they have to get the means to send some team into the underworld and then begin to find him. That Heretic group would be useful, but they likely need to be able to send a vampire into the underworld in order to provide vitae to wake him. So there's lots of things that could happen while that search is conducted. It could be interesting to have Garou PCs go through that same process of figuring out what is going on, and then try to stop them. They'll have to learn rare rites to do so, and that may mean politicking with the rare Garou who know them. It is not even necessary for the All High to be actually be found. There can be other things that are going on. Perhaps the Garou PCs discover that idea first, and they now need to figure out how to prevent the Host from reaching the same conclusion. Lots of different ways for an ST to proceed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T10:34:51-07:00","id":1518708,"title":"","content":"I wonder how would the D\u00edsir would fit in the Host...?<br /> The Disir are often depicted as <i>the spirits of dead female ancestors</i>\u200b<br /> What exactly did the Disir do? Again, that is a tough question. We already know the Dis are female ancestors who have died. These spirits are capable of aiding their kin in battle or looking after warriors who have already died, much like the Valkyries. With that said, they can be spiteful beings at times.<br /> It\u2019s the color of their clothing that tells the type of message they\u2019re bringing. When seen on the battlefield or in dreams, they will usually be riding horses and wearing either white or black. If dressed in white, they will offer wards and defenses. If seen in black, though, then it might mean death and destruction are near.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T10:49:26-07:00","id":1518711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518707#post1518707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an intriguing idea that I must have missed earlier. If Enoch in the underworld has slumbering ancient vampires in torpor, then Odin (or other vampires) might be in a similar position.<br /> <br /> It does make for an interesting scenario as the Valkyrie cannot find him. And perhaps one element of the Host's early activities in a chronicle is getting the means to figure that out. Then if they do, then they have to get the means to send some team into the underworld and then begin to find him. That Heretic group would be useful, but they likely need to be able to send a vampire into the underworld in order to provide vitae to wake him. So there's lots of things that could happen while that search is conducted. It could be interesting to have Garou PCs go through that same process of figuring out what is going on, and then try to stop them. They'll have to learn rare rites to do so, and that may mean politicking with the rare Garou who know them. It is not even necessary for the All High to be actually be found. There can be other things that are going on. Perhaps the Garou PCs discover that idea first, and they now need to figure out how to prevent the Host from reaching the same conclusion. Lots of different ways for an ST to proceed.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well if we wanted to draw upon more legends, what if the legend around Lokis imprisonment by Ska\u00f0i and the serpent is actually about the All-High.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s a myth based on events perhaps Ska\u00f0i was an Dark Ages Theurge or maybe an Incarna who helped with the banishment, perhaps the serpent is an ancient spirit bound to the quest of preventing the All-Highs location being discovered (or an Underworld cult dedicated to keeping him imprisoned).<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T10:53:41-07:00","id":1518712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518708#post1518708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how would the D\u00edsir would fit in the Host...?<br /> The Disir are often depicted as <i>the spirits of dead female ancestors</i>\u200b<br /> What exactly did the Disir do? Again, that is a tough question. We already know the Dis are female ancestors who have died. These spirits are capable of aiding their kin in battle or looking after warriors who have already died, much like the Valkyries. With that said, they can be spiteful beings at times.<br /> It\u2019s the color of their clothing that tells the type of message they\u2019re bringing. When seen on the battlefield or in dreams, they will usually be riding horses and wearing either white or black. If dressed in white, they will offer wards and defenses. If seen in black, though, then it might mean death and destruction are near.</div> </div> </div> </div>So possibly another Heretic Cult or possibly an alternative to the Wild Hunt, the white versus black is interesting I wonder what determines their choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-24T17:17:45-07:00","id":1518726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518708#post1518708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how would the D\u00edsir would fit in the Host...?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily think that we need to connect every bit of Norse mythology to the Host. Only if it would add something cool. Furthermore, my (limited) understanding of the term dis indicates it might just be a general term for female deities, not necessarily a distinct type of beings separate from others. I know the term is associated with the valkyries and norns in general.<br /> <br /> So I probably would not create anything new for the Host just for this. Although that term might be used by the Host to refer to any number of beings - the female Gangrel already known as the valkyries, female wraiths of the Companions of Hermodr, maybe even spirits the Host knows which take female form. That might make things more confusing to Garou PCs if they hear the term and they think it is a distinct group. Sometimes that can be good (other times it might make the game too confusing for the PCs).<br /> <br /> But if someone can figure out something interesting to add, I wouldn't hesitate to steal the idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-27T19:27:58-07:00","id":1518980,"title":"","content":"Just because I haven't seen it mentioned, Odin has a major place in Dark Ages: Mage as the patron (sort of) of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valdaermen\" target=\"_blank\">Valdaermen</a>. These were Mages whose power was rooted in Sacrifice and shaped by the Runes, and not insignificant necromancers. They didn't exactly worship Odin so much as see him as an archetypal example of their own kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T04:45:18-07:00","id":1519003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518980#post1518980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because I haven't seen it mentioned, Odin has a major place in Dark Ages: Mage as the patron (sort of) of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valdaermen\" target=\"_blank\">Valdaermen</a>. These were Mages whose power was rooted in Sacrifice and shaped by the Runes, and not insignificant necromancers. They didn't exactly worship Odin so much as see him as an archetypal example of their own kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting that although they viewed Odin as having given them the Runes, they were indifferent viewing him as self serving - perhaps in this context they understood what he was or that there may have been two versions.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m guessing as well as struggling with the Christian Mage, they may have been targets for the Fenris as well or allies (see below).<br /> <br /> From a story/campaign usage it could be that the Valdaermen were opposed to the false Odin, especially if they originated from the same roots (which given the geography could well be the case), they might have viewed the All Highs corruption of the Rune Giver as an affront (this may be where they reached common group with the Fenris).<br /> <br /> Might be an interesting spin for the village of Kaldheim in to have some relevance, by the Modern Days the Valdaermen are allegedly gone absorbed into the Dreamspeakers or Verbeva but what if the <i>svalahodr</i>\u200b necromancers opposed the All High and some important lore or artefacts are hidden in the ancient ruins of the village as well as their former servants.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T05:35:34-07:00","id":1519007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1518980#post1518980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because I haven't seen it mentioned, Odin has a major place in Dark Ages: Mage as the patron (sort of) of the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Valdaermen\" target=\"_blank\">Valdaermen</a>. These were Mages whose power was rooted in Sacrifice and shaped by the Runes, and not insignificant necromancers. They didn't exactly worship Odin so much as see him as an archetypal example of their own kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do feel the Valderman are one of the best proofs that there are multiple entities that would take the mantle of Odin. They don't really feel like a group that would take kindly to vampires. However, considering that a lot of their goals align with what Black Fox suggested for Odin, they could be an interesting kink - maybe even Odin the Mage was the progenitor of the Craft before he became a vampire? What is their relationship to him now? Do they see him as an example of how the might have fallen, a dire enemy or an ally?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:05:45-07:00","id":1519010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519007#post1519007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do feel the Valderman are one of the best proofs that there are multiple entities that would take the mantle of Odin. They don't really feel like a group that would take kindly to vampires. However, considering that a lot of their goals align with what Black Fox suggested for Odin, they could be an interesting kink - maybe even Odin the Mage was the progenitor of the Craft before he became a vampire? What is their relationship to him now? Do they see him as an example of how the might have fallen, a dire enemy or an ally?</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine there was (is?) a lot of &quot;It's... it's different, okay? Look, it's complicated!&quot; sorts of excuses thrown around for the mages who still consider him an ancient ally or a revered predecessor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Potential source of inspiration <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris#post1031595\">found here</a>. Written by Chris Allen, one of the writers for Forsaken 2e, as a homebrew expansion material on one of the Dark Eras that star Uratha. The descriptions for Ymir and his jotnar could be reskinned for the All-Father and his Valkyries. Meanwhile, the abilities of the three monsters (especially the last one) could be reskinned as a variety of vampiric or corrupt-Garou powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:27:35-07:00","id":1519015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519010#post1519010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine there was (is?) a lot of &quot;It's... it's different, okay? Look, it's complicated!&quot; sorts of excuses thrown around for the mages who still consider him an ancient ally or a revered predecessor.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Would't be the first <br /> The mages of the Celestial Chorus honor Mithras as an early Singer. Some, particularly the Sons of Mithras faction, go so far as to recognize him as a deity...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:32:24-07:00","id":1519016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519015#post1519015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would't be the first<br /> The mages of the Celestial Chorus honor Mithras as an early Singer. Some, particularly the Sons of Mithras faction, go so far as to recognize him as a deity...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Goddang vampires are fricking everywhere, I swear <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:40:57-07:00","id":1519019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519015#post1519015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would't be the first<br /> The mages of the Celestial Chorus honor Mithras as an early Singer. Some, particularly the Sons of Mithras faction, go so far as to recognize him as a deity...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the same Mithras, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T06:43:50-07:00","id":1519020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519010#post1519010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I imagine there was (is?) a lot of &quot;It's... it's different, okay? Look, it's complicated!&quot; sorts of excuses thrown around for the mages who still consider him an ancient ally or a revered predecessor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Potential source of inspiration <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1031595-dark-eras-the-fall-of-fenris#post1031595\">found here</a>. Written by Chris Allen, one of the writers for Forsaken 2e, as a homebrew expansion material on one of the Dark Eras that star Uratha. The descriptions for Ymir and his jotnar could be reskinned for the All-Father and his Valkyries. Meanwhile, the abilities of the three monsters (especially the last one) could be reskinned as a variety of vampiric or corrupt-Garou powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This stuff is pretty cool!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T08:56:43-07:00","id":1519033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519019#post1519019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that the same Mithras, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of?<br /> <br /> Historically, there were two Mithrases (Mithrae?) that were kinda-sorta connected. The original Mithra was a Persian deity, Zoroastrian god of light, the sun, justice, etc. The later Cult of Mithras was a mystery religion (typified by secret knowledge and tiers of initiation; think freemasonry if you need a modern cognate) popular with the Roman military, but it's connection to the older Mithra was basicallly... fanfiction?<br /> <br /> IIRC, the Voices are more in line with the original Mithra even if some of their connection comes via the Roman Cult, and Mithras-the-Vampire is meant to literally have been the being at the heart of the Roman cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T09:32:16-07:00","id":1519038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519020#post1519020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This stuff is pretty cool!</div> </div> </div> </div>For the purpose of this thread the Jotun and Ymir are excellent super-Formori or other Wyrm creature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519007#post1519007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I do feel the Valderman are one of the best proofs that there are multiple entities that would take the mantle of Odin. They don't really feel like a group that would take kindly to vampires. However, considering that a lot of their goals align with what Black Fox suggested for Odin, they could be an interesting kink - maybe even Odin the Mage was the progenitor of the Craft before he became a vampire? What is their relationship to him now? Do they see him as an example of how the might have fallen, a dire enemy or an ally?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> Given that their survivors merged with different Traditions it could easliy be all three, I can see both elements of the Dreamspeakers or Verbena seeing him as some revered force of nature or a spiritual blight, as you say could introduce some interesting kinks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27824,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","user":"Arcanus","date":". 07-28-2023, 12:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T18:45:30-07:00","id":1519064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519007#post1519007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do feel the Valderman are one of the best proofs that there are multiple entities that would take the mantle of Odin. They don't really feel like a group that would take kindly to vampires. However, considering that a lot of their goals align with what Black Fox suggested for Odin, they could be an interesting kink - maybe even Odin the Mage was the progenitor of the Craft before he became a vampire? What is their relationship to him now? Do they see him as an example of how the might have fallen, a dire enemy or an ally?</div> </div> </div> </div>The All High clearly predates the Norse by thousands of years. And while a lot of information/legends about him (both true and untrue) did influence the development of old Germanic religion in my chronicles, he certainly did not control every aspect of Norse culture. He was just one influence as the Norse developed their culture and religion. So I have no problem with there being some group of rune masters using magic that has come connection to the All High's own magical studies, but being completely independent of him when they began sometime in the first millennium AD. Their vision of Odin is probably based on the actual Norse religion, so I imagine they'd view the All High as some kind of vampire usurper and they'd just reject the notion he is the true/original &quot;Odin&quot;.<br /> <br /> Given the strong connection between Odin and magic, I imagine the All High must have been a Mage while living, and figured out his own paths of Blood Magic after he was embraced. Not that the Traditions existed back then, but he'd probably be some kind of proto-Verbena. That earthy kind of magic could have been what attracted Ennoia to him (assuming the Gangrel antedeluvian was in fact his sire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T18:52:52-07:00","id":1519066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519038#post1519038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the purpose of this thread the Jotun and Ymir are excellent super-Formori or other Wyrm creature.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my chronicles, the mythological Jotunns are like the Zmei, originally forces of the Wyld that were corrupted to the Wyrm. I start with the stats for the Vo'lag in the Apocalypse book, but individualize them and make them as powerful as I need. But I also have the &quot;Giant Blooded&quot; which are human fomori that carry this taint in their bloodlines like a Fomori Family, and other humans can be introduced to those rituals and become fomori as well.<br /> <br /> I like the idea in the Christopher Golden Hellboy novel, the Bones of Giants, that some chains of rock boulders and the like are actually the bones of these old giants/titans/jotuns. One of the things the Giant Blooded do is try to find these &quot;bones&quot; and perform rituals to resurrect and bind them.<br /> <br /> Most cultures have stories of powerful giants and such, so this is not limited to Scandinavia. The general concept applies almost everywhere. But any human cultists or Giant Blooded fomori typically organize according to the myths of their human heritage, and do not work together.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T00:59:22-07:00","id":1519080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519066#post1519066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my chronicles, the mythological Jotunns are like the Zmei, originally forces of the Wyld that were corrupted to the Wyrm. I start with the stats for the Vo'lag in the Apocalypse book, but individualize them and make them as powerful as I need.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do like the idea that some mythological creatures turned to the Wyrm to avoid the Fading and stay in the Realm.<br /> <br /> These Forsaken creatures reminded me of a super hollow man for spirits, which sounded quite horrific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519066#post1519066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I also have the &quot;Giant Blooded&quot; which are human fomori that carry this taint in their bloodlines like a Fomori Family, and other humans can be introduced to those rituals and become fomori as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Supernatural human lineages are good (although I\u2019m careful not to overdo it), I mentioned earlier in the thread the possibility of the Host tracking down Jotun Blooded to use as foot soldiers.<br /> <br /> The backstory\u2019s quite useful though is the Jotun or Jotunnblooded can be persuaded that it\u2019s in their interest to oppose Fenris.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519066#post1519066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most cultures have stories of powerful giants and such, so this is not limited to Scandinavia. The general concept applies almost everywhere. But any human cultists or Giant Blooded fomori typically organize according to the myths of their human heritage, and do not work together.</div> </div> </div> </div>We have a number of types of giants, crytids (Sasquatch which Younger and Older Brother and the Red Talons try to keep hidden), Fey creatures, some surviving Wyld creatures (clinging to places of mythic energy) and Wyrm creatures.<br /> <br /> The only thing I\u2019m not so keen on is just making them spirits (as per Rage across Appalachia) , but that\u2019s just personal taste.<br /> <br /> I quite like the idea of there being Gorgon Blooded Jotun, where the human or animal merge has been passed down, mechanically it can be represented through merits and throws the odd curveball perhaps being the basis for say John Henry etc","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-30T18:12:20-07:00","id":1519214,"title":"","content":"I half-remembered some statement that the Valkyries were active near the Anarch Free states, but was not able to find it so I didn't mention it. However, I've now located it in the Revised Clanbook: Gangrel. Because it's heavily mixed up in the Revised era metaplot, some of this is probably retconned away. And I often don't like new things in the Revised era. But that is a matter of taste. In any case, I'll repeat what that sourcebooks contains here for convenience.<br /> <br /> First, we're told there are four Valkyrie in California to investigate and agitate within the Anarch Free State. At the time, I think this was to set up some elder Gangrel versus Kuei-Jin conflict. But the original decision of Brunnhild to send some of their sisters there did not involve the Kuei-Jin. I like the idea that there are some Valkyrie who have left Europe, and regardless of their original reasons to investigate California, I don't see any reason why they could not remain in North America. After all, they are not limited to trying to use the Anarchs as a recruitment device. There are plenty of other things they might want to here especially given the large Scandinavian migration to the US and Canada. Personally I like the idea of a bunch of Gangrel &quot;anarchs&quot; wandering the woods of Canada, exploiting the wilderness there to build up some &quot;survival&quot; bastions.<br /> <br /> Second, the clanbook description of Brunnhild gives us some details on the location of the All High. In winter 1977, Brunnhild learned of six exsanguinated Lupines on an icy plain, and Brunnhild investigated the land to discover the location of the All High. That appears to have been a stone table previously buried in an &quot;ice cairn&quot; that had melted away. He woke again in 1982 and subsequently devoured a group of &quot;Wild Ones&quot;. Then in summer of 1999 (the sourcebook was published in 2000 and the wording says &quot;last summer), Brunnhild had a particular vivid dream of Ragnarok. (This is also what prompted her to send four of her sisters to California, meaning they arrived in 1999 and not before). This is likely all retconned by now. But if someone wanted, they could choose to place the All High slumbering under some mountain glacier in Norway or Sweden (although perhaps Svalbard is also possible). Presumably he used Protean to accomplish this.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily think that this contradicts the idea - mentioned earlier on this thread - that the All High might be lost to the underworld as well. Buried things with the dead do show up in the Shadowlands. So someone could connect the two ideas. There is also a possible connection to frozen Niflheim or Niflhel which Odin once visited, and was at least once said to be a real location located in the north. So perhaps the All High used some kind of sympathetic magic to enter the underworld from there to learn something.<br /> <br /> I would also like to point out a legend found in Saxo Grammaticus' Gesta Danorum Book 8. The story, which I originally encountered in the Enchanted World volume Fabled Lands, describes how a ship of vikings (lead by Gorm the Old, King of Denmark) sailed far north (beyond Finnmark) to find giant treasure and encountered the giant Gudmund in his hall Glaesisvellir which was a borderland between the living and the dead. It was a testing ground and if they passed, they could find a land of treasures. At least one scholar associated Gundmund and Glaesisvellir with Odin and Valhalla. From Gudmund they learned how to proceed further into the realm of the dead so they could see the treasures of the giant Geirrod who had been slain by Thor. This legend fits in very well with the description above. One could easily put the All High on the Arctic Shore or even Svalbard, hanging out in half spirit/dreaming and half real place in the 10th century. The Gesta Danorum is about the semi-legendary kings of Denmark, so the lineage of kings surrounding Gorm won't correspond to the lists created by historians.<br /> <br /> I also like that perhaps Brunnhild is receiving dreams from the All High (regardless of whether she actually found his location) that is influencing her to make certain decisions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T11:23:05-07:00","id":1519271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519214#post1519214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, we're told there are four Valkyrie in California to investigate and agitate within the Anarch Free State. At the time, I think this was to set up some elder Gangrel versus Kuei-Jin conflict. But the original decision of Brunnhild to send some of their sisters there did not involve the Kuei-Jin. I like the idea that there are some Valkyrie who have left Europe, and regardless of their original reasons to investigate California, I don't see any reason why they could not remain in North America. After all, they are not limited to trying to use the Anarchs as a recruitment device. There are plenty of other things they might want to hear especially given the large Scandinavian migration to the US and Canada. Personally I like the idea of a bunch of Gangrel &quot;anarchs&quot; wandering the woods of Canada, exploiting the wilderness there to build up some &quot;survival&quot; bastions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think there\u2019s lots of hooks for activity in California simple recruitment disenfranchised anarchs, travelling north to Vancouver, tracking down other lost Gangrel Elders etc <br /> <br /> Interesting the Host and Kuei-Jin have a lot in common with some Dharmas and Wu working to stop the Sixth Age or Ragnarok (although I think their working out this common ground unlikely).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519214#post1519214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily think that this contradicts the idea - mentioned earlier on this thread - that the All High might be lost to the underworld as well. Buried things with the dead do show up in the Shadowlands. So someone could connect the two ideas. There is also a possible connection to frozen Niflheim or Niflhel which Odin once visited, and was at least once said to be a real location located in the north. So perhaps the All High used some kind of sympathetic magic to enter the underworld from there to learn something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, I quite like the idea that he\u2019s used a weak spot in the Shroud (a glacier sounds perfect for virtually non-existent Shroud) to secret himself away but has then been trapped by forces unknown, occasionally breaking free for limited amounts of time.<br /> <br /> In my mind it provides an immediate mission for the Walkyrie/Brunhilde in having to find a way of enabling his long term/permanent escape (the artefacts etc from earlier in the thread)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-31T22:50:14-07:00","id":1519316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519271#post1519271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think there\u2019s lots of hooks for activity in California simple recruitment disenfranchised anarchs, travelling north to Vancouver, tracking down other lost Gangrel Elders etc</div> </div> </div> </div>Vancouver might make an interesting locale for the Host. The Dark Alliance: Vancouver sourcebook provides an interesting locale. It is supposed to be a place where Lupines and vampires coexist with some amount of peace. As a vampire domain, it is independent - not of the Camarilla. The Great Sept has Raven as a totem (and some kind of Raven spirits should be associated with the Host). So it opens a lot of possibilities for an ST who wants to be inspired by canon.<br /> <br /> I personally think that Dark Alliance is a very flawed sourcebook, but it does have some ideas I like. And possibly making it an area where the Valkyries of North America utilize makes a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T10:29:52-07:00","id":1519349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519316#post1519316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that Dark Alliance is a very flawed sourcebook, but it does have some ideas I like. And possibly making it an area where the Valkyries of North America utilize makes a lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it\u2019s fairly typical of a number of the earlier setting books where there\u2019s a good idea but it falls into some of the default setting assumptions which don\u2019t make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Firstly the Ancient (under the University) is manipulating an experienced elder with inhuman intelligence and very high levels of Dominate and Presence, as well as pretty high survival instincts, so Siegfried not sensing influence is a bit clumsy and just follows the VTM default.<br /> <br /> Secondly for the Garou to have agreed to the pact there would have to be a compelling reason other than they were being reasonable, it was in their interest or being similarly manipulated. (There\u2019s plenty of other settings where an alliance with Kindred who control forestry companies or to get peaceful access to a city Caern).<br /> <br /> Also the Covenant itself feels slightly wasted, a neutral independent city where the peace is enforced by an encircling force of Garou (ancestral enemies who\u2019ve agreed not to attack Kindred), sounds like the perfect place for a neutral meeting ground between factions.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d have it that the Ancient approached Seigfried with a proposal, based on the fact that the Ancient (with its vast knowledge of the land and Garou ways) had sensed something even more ancient and evil imprisoned under the territory (or a similar threat for both the city, the kindred or the Garou).<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Ancient had discovered the true nature of Pentax and decided they were a much bigger threat to Vancouver.<br /> <br /> Whatever the threat this was backed by Necross, Roger Daly being aware of this threat, with the support of the Uktena was able to sell the idea to the Silver Fangs and so on.<br /> <br /> The adventure also makes little sense as Seigfried is a formidable agent for the ancient who orchestrated the whole thing so why allow a coup (where the book says he could have stopped it at any time), plus a millennia old elder had no contingencies, agents in place etc to stop betrayal (he must have faced a few insurrections in his time).<br /> <br /> In terms of the Host Vancouver has a large Germanic population so plenty of reasons to explore the city, plus the Ancient could either be an ancient ally or enemy of the All High, especially if the cities special nature is worked out a bit better - as an independent city it would make a great base of operations for The Host.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T13:12:35-07:00","id":1519356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519349#post1519349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, it\u2019s fairly typical of a number of the earlier setting books where there\u2019s a good idea but it falls into some of the default setting assumptions which don\u2019t make a lot of sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is certainly a lot of weirdness that can only be explained by it being such an early product that people were still figuring things out about the setting. If I ever ran a chronicle there, I'd ditch a lot of the canon and rebuild it using its ideas only as an inspiration. I'd certainly make a lot of the vampire NPCs a lot younger and lesser generation. If Siegfried is so dominant because of his individual power, you cannot have other vampires there who should be able to rival him. Stalest is only one generation less than him, but is almost 1000 years older than him. Lyle is of equal generation and even older. Necross is of more potent generation and older. There's four more NPCs that are between 500-800 years. If these characters were in Chicago, they'd dominate politics there.<br /> <br /> If I had to better explain the Covenant, I'd use the ancient methusaleh under Stanley Park, the Slumbering Giant (as much as I hate that early trope that there is always some methusaleh in torpor under the city). We know as the sire of the Wanderer, this 4th generation Gangrel has been in North America for at least 2000 years and seems to really like the Pacific Northwest. He probably doesn't stink of the Wyrm. He seems to know a lot about North America and makes strong relations with whatever peoples he lives among. That implies he's made contact with the Three Brothers a lot, and that they didn't do anything about him.<br /> <br /> So I would say that the Slumbering Giant is a well known legendary figure among the Uktena and Wendigo (and perhaps in Native American folklore and myth). They don't think he's a vampire. They might think he is some kind of materialized spirit, kami, or force of the Wyld. He's an immortal ally who helps them. He would be one of the people who helped the Garou understand that they could have built the Great Caern there. And when this torpored vampire visits them in dreams, they think it's natural. They listen to what the Slumbering Giant tells them like they would any other spirit.<br /> <br /> He has his own plans for the area. That he travelled to North America so early implies he was trying to escape the Jyhad. That Siegfried wants the domain to be independent implies that is what the Slumbering Giant wants as well. That Necross established the Great Library - presumably of a lot of lost knowledge - implies that too is important to the Slumbering Giant. Use the traditional conceits of a torpored Methusaleh influencing the people in charge. Perhaps he thinks that this is a good place to withstand the Jyhad, and that with the contents of the Great Library people could rebuild civilization after Gehenna. This may not have been the Slumbering Giant's original plan when he went into torpor, but why not take advantage of a good thing? By making the Garou and Siegfried keep the peace, he protects the Great Library and the knowledge of the vampire librarians there so the Garou don't inadvertently destroy them. By having the Garou outside the city, he protects these vampires from other vampires.<br /> <br /> Siegfried then believes a pact with the Garou make sense. While the Garou obey because this legendary figure they know from thousands of years is communicating to them that a pact pleases him, even though they are not exactly sure why. The Wendigo and Uktena are most trustworthy, while the Eurasian tribes are willing to defer to them because they know the local area. Someone like Guttooth then can be used to show Garou who are more distrustful of this unknown spirit, kami, whatever because he thinks this is too fishy.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, what might attract the four valkyries and Host to Vancouver - though they don't know it, they just get omens - is the Great Library. It should be filled with all sorts of information and artifacts they would want to pillage if they ever learn about it. And since the circumstances of the domain make it an obvious place to wait out Ragnarok, that would attract them anyway. They visit and leave, keeping the peace. But over time they may learn something (whenever the ST wants them to).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T13:34:38-07:00","id":1519359,"title":"","content":"There's another thing that's been percolating in my head. Black Foxes version of Odin is incredibly reasonable, one would wonder why he never managed to find some kind of a truce or a common enemy with the Garou over the thousands of years he has existed.<br /> <br /> Maybe he has a problem. Freya is one of the few Gods that can hold her own in a flyt with Loki and Odin and has had an <i>interesting</i> relationship with Odin in different tales. Coupled with the fact that she chooses half of the slain and that a lot of Christian sources would portray her as a wicked temptress. To this mix we can add the fact that there are theories about connections between Cybele and Freya.<br /> <br /> So, what if Freya/Cybele was one of the first children of the All Father? She started out loyal, but them being bitter immortals soured the waters and created a rift. She has spent thousands of years sabotaging and taking from the All Father, keeping him in check and seeing him as an old fool that she can conquer in the endless Jyhad. She has access to the quirks of their blood, and the magics he has developed. She may have followers among the Spa-Kona and her own Chosen among the slain. She is also portrayed as accompanied by twin cats - could these be some kind of fey beasts, powerful ghouls, fomori or even Bastet abominations! Considering her cloak of Eagle-feathers, just as Odin is symbolised by Ravens, she would be symbolised by Eagles.<br /> <br /> There are few ways to really rain on someone's parade as well as making sure their relations with the Garou are as poisonous as possible. And this is what she has done among a million other plans to sabotage Odin's fixation with something she feels is irrelevant or patently wrong. Or maybe she feels he has the wrong approach, and has joined with the Sabbat and seeks to marshall the great army of the All Father against the Antedelluvians, rather than the child's tales of Ragnarok.<br /> <br /> <br /> You've all definitely increased my like of the concept of a vampiric Odin and his influence on the world of Werewolf. I did start out rather skeptic, but the thread has been a lot of fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'll leave you with a quote from Norse Mythology from Gaiman that must be a thing among the Get Gailards:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><i>\u201cHere is the last thing, and a shameful admission it is. When the all-father in eagle form had almost reached the vats, with Suttung immediately behind him, Odin blew some of the mead out of his behind, a splatter wet fart of foul-smelling mead right in Suttung's face, blinding the giant and throwing him off Odin's trail.<br /> <br /> No one, then or now, wanted to drink the mead that came out of Odin's ass. But whenever you hear bad poets declaiming their bad poetry, filled with foolish similes and ugly rhymes, you will know which of the meads the have tasted.\u201d</i></b><br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T18:08:47-07:00","id":1519385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519359#post1519359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Foxes version of Odin is incredibly reasonable, one would wonder why he never managed to find some kind of a truce or a common enemy with the Garou over the thousands of years he has existed.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably an indication I need to give him some explicit deeds that are clearly crimes to the Garou. I'm not trying to make him be a good guy. He just wants to survive by preventing the end of the world (if possible), or by destroying his enemies (if not). I just want him to be ambiguous enough that conceivably players may want to have their PCs interact with the Host at times rather than outright kill them. But that doesn't mean the All High is not ruthless, cruel, and treacherous when he needs to be.<br /> <br /> (like this version found in the video game God of War Ragnarok)<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RxRn6tpSqkc\" data-code=\"RxRn6tpSqkc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/RxRn6tpSqkc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> My version does support making corrupted Corax and having Skin Dancers so that is something the Garou would have against him. And he's willing to use utilize Banes, he's just knowledgeable enough so they don't corrupt or use him. Possibly I could have the very few Ceilican allied to the Host be outright blood bonded to one or more of the vampires.<br /> <br /> He did usurp and corrupt the original Gaian religion of the extremely ancient Germanic peoples with a new religion that assigned him as the head god. So the Get of Fenris remember that.<br /> <br /> And there must be a ton of stories of how this Garou hero's kinfolk family member was turned into a vampire, or sacrificed to the All High, or some other action that would cause personal blood feuds.<br /> <br /> Plus there is the idea that at different times in the past, the Get of Fenris (and other Garou) DID work with the All High because they do have common interests. And every time it bit them in the ass. But like all things, it'd be better for the ST to have concrete details and stories as examples not just a statement. By the time of the Germanic Iron Age, you have lots of Ancestor spirits of the Get of Fenris warning the tribe - DO NOT TRUST THIS MAN.<br /> <br /> One thing I have not mentioned is that in my chronicles, he's partly responsible for the Lhiannan bloodline. Just as Odin had his valkyries so did Freya have hers. And since Freya was one of the Vanir (Tuatha de Danaan), that meant some kind of weird vampire faerie he embraced that somehow created the Lhiannan bloodline. I figured if you are going to name a vampire bloodline after a kind of faerie, that'd be appropriate to connect the two. Now when the All High did this, it was thousands of years before we could say there was a Germanic people with their own mythology. So how the Norse remembered those events and how the Lhiannan vampires remembered them seem to be two different stories. Their &quot;Crone&quot; was just the female faerie who was embraced by the All High. The signature Oghma Discipline of the Lhiannan would clearly anger the Garou for multiple reasons.<br /> <br /> Now that presents all sorts of problems with canon if you want to go with what's been published. And while their original bloodline description just makes them generically European pagan found in multiple cultures, I think later depictions tried to make them more explicitly tied to the Celts. So I didn't mention it to avoid discussions of &quot;here's what's wrong with your use of this very limited lore&quot;. But in my chronicles, this was part of the Host of Odin, and the Garou destroying the last of them in the 14th century was a major victory against the All High.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T18:13:44-07:00","id":1519386,"title":"","content":"Oh don't worry,you didn't sell me on him being a Good Guy. I'd have surely amped his villainy and backstabbing if I was to use him in a game. However, the focus has been so much on making him reasonable with a sensible core goal that we are lacking some more context for why is so universally hated and key to Garou mythology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T18:15:20-07:00","id":1519387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519359#post1519359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, what if Freya/Cybele was one of the first children of the All Father?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to be clear, are you talking about the ancient Baali vampire? I assume that means changing her clan from Malkavian to Gangrel and having someone else sire the Malkavian Petaniqua. But that's easily doable. And it'd be interesting.<br /> <br /> Or are you talking about someone else?<br /> <br /> There is so much lore now - especially in the latter eras of the game - that I just don't know.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-01T18:20:14-07:00","id":1519388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514259-the-followers-of-odin-as-a-werewolf-setting-element-foe?p=1519387#post1519387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to be clear, are you talking about the ancient Baali vampire? I assume that means changing her clan from Malkavian to Gangrel and having someone else sire the Malkavian Petaniqua. But that's easily doable. And it'd be interesting.<br /> <br /> Or are you talking about someone else?<br /> <br /> There is so much lore now - especially in the latter eras of the game - that I just don't know.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm assuming a new character and childe of the All High. Using his origin to capitalise on the historic Cybele and play up the antagonistic elements of Freya.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T00:05:50-07:00","id":1519940,"title":"","content":"Something I consider important about the All High, is that while we heavily associate Odin with the Norse, he probably pre-dates the Norse by many thousands of years. In my imagination, I place the All High as part of the Yamnaya Culture during his embrace. It fits both the needs of an ancient methusaleh vampire as well as the &quot;history&quot; of Snorri Sturlson. As such, I use various things associated with that culture to inspire me.<br /> <br /> I find the author Dan Davis to be particularly useful in that regard. He has studied a lot of that early Bronze Age culture, and I use it to imagine the values of the All High. Now we know very little about those actual cultures. The &quot;knowledge&quot; of that era and place is heavily dependent on reconstructed mythology and linguistics as well as anthropology. Mr Davis assumes a lot of that reconstructed knowledge is real, but is really just supposition. But regardless of its value as actual history, I think it is good inspiration for the fictional reality of the World of Darkness. Here are some of his most pertinent videos on YouTube.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GalZLoTeU74\" data-code=\"GalZLoTeU74\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/GalZLoTeU74/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zEXXA0naXkk\" data-code=\"zEXXA0naXkk\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zEXXA0naXkk/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oqOp81KQO4A\" data-code=\"oqOp81KQO4A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/oqOp81KQO4A/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> One of the things that is very obvious is the association with elements we associate with the Garou. That could indicate the All High was an actual kinfolk of one of the Garou tribes. That would justify a lot of the knowledge the All High has about the Garou, and how he would be able to manipulate them and use intimate knowledge of the Changing Breeds. The actual tribe the All High would have been kinfolk of is probably irrelevant. The Garou of 3000 BC would be very different than the Garou today. Even the Children of Gaia would be noticeably hardcore compared to today.<br /> <br /> What can we pull from this that might make distinctive elements of the Host in modern nights? Human cults part of the Host might be limited to Norse culture because of the limitations of human history and understanding. But vampires thousands of years old would not be. Many elements of Bronze Age culture would still fit the Norse culture many years later. But certain things would not, and it might mean an opportunity for STs to do something interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T08:11:27-07:00","id":1534641,"title":"","content":"I have to say that \u2018Vampire Odin\u2019 is definately one of my favourite High Concepts for a WEREWOLF: THE APOCALYPSE villain - it\u2019s delightfully gonzo, whilst making a certain amount of sense (I recall one tradition that even in his high seat of Valhalla Odin never actually ate, only drank, which has a lot of potential for \u201cI never drink \u2026 wine\u201d reinterpretation).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}